/* Transit readings for the Today tab, written about you (see CLAUDE.md): aspects from each transiting planet to your chart (conj, soft, hard), planets moving through your houses, and what each planet's transits bring. */
window.AstroDeep = window.AstroDeep || {};
window.AstroDeep.transitAspectsRich = {
  "jupiter|sun": {
    "conj": "For the next few weeks Jupiter sits on your Sun, and you feel larger than usual, as if someone turned the lights up in every room you walk into. Invitations arrive, people remember your name, and a project you had half abandoned finds a backer. You catch yourself saying yes before the question is finished, to trips, roles and second helpings alike. This is a once in twelve years moment to be seen for who you are, and you are warmer and more hopeful than you have been in a long while. Confidence also runs ahead of your time and money, so you promise three things where one would have been plenty. What you start now keeps growing for years.",
    "soft": "Over these few weeks life keeps saying yes to you in small, pleasant ways. A manager mentions your work in a meeting you were not even in, a friend passes on a lead, and the form you dreaded goes through first time. You feel easy in your own skin, quicker to laugh and less driven to prove anything. Because the help comes without fanfare, it is easy to enjoy the mood and let the chances drift past unused. When you act on a hunch now, the world meets you halfway. It is a fine stretch for applying, pitching or turning up where you want to belong.",
    "hard": "Jupiter pressing on your Sun for several weeks inflates everything, including your sense of what you can carry. You take on the extra project, book the pricier option and tell people you will be there, then discover the week still has only seven days. Someone bigger or louder than you seems to crowd your space, or you are the one who oversteps and has to apologise. Pride gets touchy, and a small slight feels like a verdict on your worth. Underneath the excess is a hunger to grow, telling you that your current life has become too small. These weeks reward you when that hunger chooses one direction instead of five."
  },
  "jupiter|venus": {
    "conj": "For a few weeks Jupiter rests on your Venus, and pleasure becomes easy to find. You are more attractive than you realise: people linger in conversation, a flirtation starts in the queue for coffee, and friends want you at their table. Money moves more freely in both directions, and a gift or bonus lands just as you spot the thing you have wanted for months. You feel softer, more affectionate and quicker to forgive. Indulgence is the obvious snare, whether the extra bottle, the impulse purchase or the romance you rush into because it feels lovely today. This is a lucky season for love, art and anything that makes your life more beautiful, and it deepens whatever you already value.",
    "soft": "Through these weeks Jupiter smooths the path around love and money. A dinner turns into a long, happy evening, an old friend gets back in touch, and a negotiation over price goes your way without a fight. You feel appreciated, and you show appreciation more readily too, sending the message you usually only think about. Creative work flows, and you find yourself buying flowers, rearranging a room or planning a trip purely for joy. Because nothing forces the issue, the good mood can slide by without leaving much behind. A relationship or creative plan you nourish now pays back well after Jupiter moves on.",
    "hard": "Jupiter squaring or opposing your Venus for several weeks turns up the appetite for more: more affection, more treats, more reassurance that you are loved. You overspend on something beautiful, overcommit socially, or hope a partner will fill a gap that comes from your own boredom. A relationship feels either wonderfully expansive or cramped and not enough, and you catch yourself comparing it with other people's. Someone promises more than they deliver, or you do. The generosity is real, though, and so is the wish for a fuller, warmer life. What these weeks show you, plainly, is where pleasure has become a stand in for what you want."
  },
  "jupiter|saturn": {
    "conj": "Jupiter meets your Saturn for a few weeks, and the part of your life that has been slow, heavy and dutiful finally starts to move. A long application is approved, a senior person opens a door, or the structure you built patiently turns out to have room to grow. You feel grown up in a good way: ambitious but realistic, hopeful without fantasy. Old fears about not being good enough loosen their grip, even if only a little. Luck here comes wrapped in responsibility, a bigger role with bigger demands, so the work does not vanish. It is one of the best moments in twelve years to expand something solid rather than start something flimsy.",
    "soft": "For these weeks your sense of duty and your sense of possibility line up. Plans that felt stuck gain traction, a budget balances, and a boss or mentor backs you with practical support rather than kind words. You find it easier to commit, to sign the lease or agree the schedule, because the risk feels measured. Work is still work, yet it feels meaningful instead of grinding. The easy mood is simple to spend on routine, and the chance to formalise something larger slips by if you let it. Steady progress made now is the kind that holds for years.",
    "hard": "Jupiter pulling against your Saturn for several weeks sets growth and caution at odds inside you. One day you want to leap, the next you remember every reason not to, and plans stall halfway. At work an opportunity arrives that clashes with an existing obligation, or someone in charge says yes in principle and no in practice. You feel held back, and part of you is the one doing the holding. Excess caution loses the moment, while overreaching costs more than it earns. The tension earns its keep by forcing you to decide which commitments deserve to grow and which have outlived their purpose."
  },
  "jupiter|northNode": {
    "conj": "For a few weeks Jupiter crosses your North Node, and the direction you have been circling for years comes within reach. Chance meetings matter: a stranger at a party mentions the course, the city or the kind of work you had quietly been drawn towards. You feel encouraged, and people who belong in your future appear with surprising ease. Old habits still pull, and you notice yourself reaching for the familiar role even as a new one is offered. The new path feels less comfortable than what you know, and doubt lingers for that reason. Growth now is less about luck than about recognising that the open door in front of you is the right one.",
    "soft": "Through these weeks life nudges you gently towards where you are heading. A friend's suggestion, a book left on a table, a conversation after a meeting: each points the same way, and you start to notice the pattern. You feel supported in growing beyond your usual role, and stepping into something new costs less courage than normal. Teachers and allies are easy to find, and they seem pleased to help. Because the push is mild, you can mistake it for coincidence and carry on as before. Following even one of these small signals now sets up a longer change in the shape of your life.",
    "hard": "Jupiter squaring or opposing your North Node for several weeks shows you, loudly, the gap between comfort and growth. Opportunities arrive that flatter your old strengths, and you are tempted to accept them because they are easy. People urge you in directions that suit them more than you, and the advice is generous but slightly off. You feel restless, sure that more is possible yet unconvinced by the obvious offers. Saying yes to the familiar leaves you oddly flat afterwards, like a meal that fills without feeding. This is a season of learning what growth means for you, often by noticing what no longer satisfies."
  },
  "saturn|mercury": {
    "conj": "For a few months Saturn sits on your Mercury, and your mind turns serious. Words weigh more: you reread emails three times, choose phrases carefully and feel judged when you speak up in meetings. Studying, writing or learning a hard skill goes slowly, but what you learn now stays with you for decades. Worry loops in the small hours, as the same problem turns over without resolution. Contracts, forms and official letters demand close attention, and there is little room for sloppiness. By the end of this stretch you think more precisely, speak with more authority and know where your knowledge is solid.",
    "soft": "Over these months Saturn lends your thinking discipline and patience. Detailed tasks that normally bore you become oddly satisfying, and you finish the report, the thesis or the tax return without drama. People take your words seriously in meetings and on paper, and an older colleague or teacher offers solid, usable guidance just when you need it. Your speech becomes more measured, so you say less and mean more. The mood is steady rather than exciting, which makes the progress easy to underrate while it happens. Plans you write down now tend to become lasting structures in your life.",
    "hard": "Saturn squaring or opposing your Mercury for some months brings mental pressure. Deadlines stack up, forms come back unaccepted, and someone in authority questions your reasoning or picks apart your words. You second-guess yourself, draft messages you never send and lie awake replaying conversations. Talking with a parent, boss or older person feels stiff, as though every sentence is being marked. Pessimism creeps in and colours small setbacks as proof that nothing works. Yet this is also when you learn to think rigorously, check facts and say exactly what you mean, a skill that outlasts the discomfort by years."
  },
  "saturn|jupiter": {
    "conj": "For a few months Saturn sits on your Jupiter, and your hopes get a reality check. Big plans that lived comfortably in your imagination now have to face budgets, timelines and other people's diaries. Some dreams shrink, and you feel the loss; others turn firmer, sturdier and within reach. Beliefs you took for granted come under examination, often through study, travel or a mentor who challenges you hard. Your generosity grows more careful as you notice where you have been giving beyond your means. What this period builds is faith that has been tested, an optimism that has earned its place.",
    "soft": "Through these months Saturn steadies your sense of growth. Long-term plans for study, travel, publishing or business get the structure they needed: a timetable, a sponsor, a signed agreement. You feel optimistic in a grounded way, trusting effort more than luck. Advisers and older people are helpful, the bank manager included, and your own judgement becomes reliable in a way others start to notice and lean on. There is no great drama, so coasting is tempting when the support is there to be used. What you put in place now keeps growing long after Saturn has moved on.",
    "hard": "Saturn pressing on your Jupiter for a few months makes expansion feel expensive. Opportunities are real but come with conditions, delays or small print that dampens the excitement. You feel caught between wanting more and fearing you have already taken on too much. A course, a trip or an investment runs into obstacles, and you question whether it was ever the right idea. Faith in yourself, or in something bigger, wobbles, and cynicism is tempting on the bad days. The pressure strips away inflated hopes and leaves the ones strong enough to build on, which is valuable even when it hardly feels so."
  },
  "saturn|mc": {
    "conj": "Saturn reaching your MC marks a peak in your career cycle, and it shapes many months. You are more visible at work than usual, and the results of long effort, good or poor, become public. Promotions, formal recognition or a demanding new role often arrive now, and so does the weight of accountability. Some days you feel tired, aware that people are watching and expecting a lot. Anything built on weak ground wobbles, and a job that no longer suits you becomes hard to pretend about. This is the moment to take full ownership of your standing in the world, because what you claim now defines your reputation for years.",
    "soft": "For these months Saturn supports your working life in a steady, businesslike way. Managers notice your reliability, the way you quietly fix what others leave half done, and you are trusted with more responsibility without the usual strain that comes with it. A long-term career plan becomes concrete: a qualification, a promotion track, a business registered in your own name. You feel mature and capable, more comfortable being the one people consult before they decide. The pace is slow, and impatience for payoffs is the main irritation when others seem to rise faster. Everything done carefully now adds lasting weight to your name.",
    "hard": "Saturn squaring or opposing your MC for several months puts pressure on the balance between work and the rest of your life. Career demands collide with home or family duties, and you feel pulled in two directions at once. A boss grows exacting, a project stalls, or an institution tests whether you are truly committed. Sometimes the push comes from home instead: a parent needs care, a move is unavoidable, or the house demands attention just as work peaks. You feel tired and under examination. The stretch makes plain what your working life must look like to be sustainable, and it pushes you to rebuild it on firmer ground."
  },
  "uranus|moon": {
    "conj": "Uranus sits on your Moon for a year or more, and your emotional life refuses to stay predictable. Moods shift quickly, and you feel restless in rooms and routines that used to comfort you. Home changes are common: moving house, someone moving in or out, a sudden urge to strip the walls and start again. Old feelings about family surface in surprising ways, and you react with an intensity that startles you. The unsettledness is exhausting on days when sleep is broken or plans keep changing. Underneath it you are freeing yourself from emotional habits that kept you small, and by the end you know far better what makes you feel at home.",
    "soft": "For a long stretch Uranus brings fresh air into your emotional life. You feel freer to change your routines, your home or the way you look after yourself, and those changes come without much fuss. New friends or unusual people bring a sense of belonging you did not expect. You are more open about your feelings, and sudden insights about your family history arrive over coffee or in vivid dreams. Because the energy is easy, it can pass as mild restlessness. Small impulses followed now, a new way of living, a different town, a fresh morning ritual, lead somewhere liberating.",
    "hard": "Uranus squaring or opposing your Moon for a year or more shakes up your emotional foundations. Home life feels unstable: a move you did not plan, a household change, or tension with family that erupts without warning. You feel jumpy and quick to react, and sleep suffers when your mind will not settle. Someone close to you changes overnight, and you have to adjust faster than you would like. You catch yourself either clinging to routines or blowing them up entirely. What emerges once the dust settles is a more honest life that fits the person you have become rather than the one you used to be."
  },
  "uranus|mars": {
    "conj": "Your drive turns electric while Uranus sits on your Mars, a charge that lasts a year or more. You want to act now, change course fast and break free from anything that feels like a cage. New sports, risky adventures or bold career moves start to appeal, and you throw yourself at them with surprising energy. Your temper flares quickly, and minor frustrations such as traffic or a slow colleague set you off. Accidents come more easily when you rush, so haste costs you more than usual. Beneath the restlessness is a surge of courage, and it frees you to fight for things you once only dreamed about.",
    "soft": "Uranus supports your Mars for a year or more, bringing bursts of inventive energy. You find new ways to work, train and chase what you want, from a dawn swim to a side business started on a whim, often with a daring that surprises your friends. Chances to break from routine appear, and you act on them without the usual hesitation. Desire feels fresh, whether in love, ambition or a personal project you have been sitting on. Because change comes so easily, your energy scatters across too many experiments at once. Channelled into one bold move, this surge buys you a lasting kind of freedom.",
    "hard": "Impatience runs hot while Uranus squares or opposes your Mars, a stretch of a year or more that makes you reactive. You snap at people, push against limits and feel an urge to walk out of things abruptly. Conflicts erupt suddenly with bosses or partners who seem to block your way, and you surprise yourself with how hard you push back. Accidents and strains come more easily when you rush, and frustration sits close to the surface all day. The tension is exhausting when it builds without release. Beneath it is a need to free your drive from rules that no longer fit, and this period shows you, sometimes forcefully, what you are ready to fight for."
  },
  "uranus|asc": {
    "conj": "Uranus crosses your Ascendant over a year or more, and you start to look, sound and act differently. A drastic haircut, a new wardrobe or a fresh way of introducing yourself signals that something inside has shifted. Friends notice you are harder to predict, and some are delighted while others feel unsettled. You feel restless in your own skin, eager to reinvent how you come across. Sudden changes in circumstance, a move, a new relationship or an abrupt ending, reshape your daily life. The upheaval brings a strong new sense of independence, and people meet a version of you that is closer to who you really are.",
    "soft": "Uranus opens fresh doors, over a year or more, in how you present yourself. You feel freer to experiment with style, habits and the way you introduce yourself, and people respond with curiosity rather than judgement. Unusual friends and unexpected invitations bring new energy into your week, and you say yes to the gig, the class or the trip you would normally skip. Your body feels livelier, and you are drawn to new kinds of movement or self-care you would once have laughed at. Because the change comes lightly, you can write it off as a phase. Embraced fully, it gives you a more authentic way of being seen.",
    "hard": "Uranus squaring or opposing your Ascendant for a year or more brings disruption to how you live and relate. Partners or close collaborators change suddenly, surprise you with new demands, or step away without warning. You feel on edge, as if the ground under your daily life keeps shifting just as you find your footing. Your body registers the stress as restlessness, broken sleep or a need to keep moving. Unexpected events force you to adapt quickly and improvise more than you like. The upheaval reveals where your life has grown too rigid, and it frees you to meet the world on terms that suit who you are becoming."
  },
  "neptune|sun": {
    "conj": "Neptune dissolves the edges of your Sun for a year or more. Your sense of who you are softens: goals that once defined you feel less important, and you wonder what you are here for. Energy dips, sleep changes and you become more sensitive to people, music and atmosphere, tearing up at adverts or crowded stations. Creative, spiritual or caring work draws you in, and your imagination opens wide. The fog also brings confusion and a pull to escape through drink, screens or daydreams. As it lifts, you find a truer and gentler sense of self, far less bound to what others expect of you.",
    "soft": "Neptune softens and inspires your Sun for a year or more. You feel more compassionate, intuitive and creative, and people come to you for comfort or a sense of vision. Art, music and spiritual practice appeal strongly, and you find meaning in quiet moments such as a walk by water or a long evening alone. Your identity becomes more fluid in a helpful way, less attached to status and titles. Because the influence is gentle, it passes unnoticed unless you give it room in your week. Creative or caring work you begin now carries a special glow for years.",
    "hard": "Neptune squaring or opposing your Sun for a year or more blurs your sense of direction. Plans stall, goals feel unreal, and you are unsure what you want or who you are becoming. Other people's expectations confuse you, and disillusionment arrives through someone you trusted or a role you believed in. Your energy is lower and your body more sensitive to stress, alcohol or late nights. At times you feel lost, and the urge to escape grows, into screens, fantasy or long afternoon naps. The fog eventually clears, leaving you with more compassion and a sense of self that no longer depends on illusions."
  },
  "neptune|venus": {
    "conj": "Neptune settles on your Venus for a year or more, and love takes on a dreamy, romantic glow. You fall for someone who seems like a soulmate, or you see an existing partner through a haze that feels magical. Art, music and beauty move you to tears, and your taste grows more refined and sensitive. Money slips through your fingers, spent on dreams, good causes or lovely things that feel meaningful but vanish quickly. Disappointment arrives when reality fails to match the picture in your head. The deeper reward is a compassionate, spiritual kind of love that sees the best in people without needing them to be perfect.",
    "soft": "Neptune gently inspires your Venus through a long year or more. You feel more romantic, artistic and forgiving, and love has a tender, unhurried quality. Creative projects, music and beauty bring joy, and you find inspiration in odd places: a song in a shop, light on a wall, a stranger's kindness. Relationships soften, a partner seems kinder or you do, and old resentments fade without a formal peace treaty. Because the influence is subtle, you drift in pleasant feelings without shaping them into anything. Poured into your art or your way of loving, this mood leaves something lasting behind.",
    "hard": "Love and money tangle in confusion while Neptune squares or opposes your Venus, a year or more of soft focus. You idealise someone who turns out to be less than they seemed, or a partner becomes vague, distant or unreliable. Finances blur: debts creep up, a deal is not what it appeared, or your generosity is taken advantage of. You feel a longing without being able to name what you long for. Escaping into romance, shopping or fantasy tempts you on lonely evenings. The disillusionment is painful but clarifying, and it teaches you to love and value things as they are rather than as you wished them to be."
  },
  "neptune|saturn": {
    "conj": "Neptune crossing your Saturn lasts a year or more, and the structures you relied on start to dissolve. Work, routines or long-held ambitions feel less solid, and you question whether they still matter to you. Authority figures disappoint you or seem far less certain than you thought, and your own rules stop working. You feel tired, uncertain and sometimes adrift without the old scaffolding to hold you. At the same time rigid attitudes soften, and you grow more compassionate about limits, yours and other people's. What remains after this dissolving is a life built on meaning rather than fear.",
    "soft": "Neptune eases your Saturn in a supportive way for a year or more. You bring imagination to practical work, and dreams take concrete shape through steady effort: the studio gets built, the charity gets registered, the novel gets a daily hour. Rules feel less oppressive, deadlines less like threats, and you find more patience with your own limits and with the slow pace of lasting results. Creative or spiritual projects gain structure and a schedule you can keep. Because the influence is gentle, the quiet progress is easy to overlook. Something inspired built now has unusual staying power.",
    "hard": "Neptune squaring or opposing your Saturn for a year or more undermines the ground under your commitments. Plans blur, contracts turn out vague, and someone in authority proves unreliable just when you need them. Your ambition dissolves into doubt, and work that once felt meaningful now seems pointless on grey mornings. Fear and confusion mix, making it hard to decide what to keep and what to let go. The discomfort is real and tiring, and you miss the old certainty. What survives this period is what matters most to you, freed from obligations that were never yours."
  },
  "neptune|northNode": {
    "conj": "For a year or more Neptune sits on your North Node, and your sense of life direction turns mysterious. You feel called towards something you struggle to name: creative work, a spiritual path, caring for others, or a place you visited once and never forgot. Coincidences pile up, and you meet people who seem to know more about your future than you do. The pull is strong but vague, so you drift for a while or follow the wrong guide with total conviction. Some days you feel inspired and others lost, scrolling through job adverts at midnight without knowing what you are looking for. Across this stretch your purpose becomes less about achievement and more about meaning, and you begin to trust a quieter inner compass.",
    "soft": "Neptune gently guides your North Node for a year or more. Intuition about where your life is heading grows stronger, and you notice small signs in dreams, chance remarks or a song that lands at exactly the right moment. Creative and compassionate paths feel natural, and people who share your ideals turn up without effort, at a workshop, a retreat or a friend's kitchen table. You feel less pressure to have a five year plan and more trust that the route will show itself. The influence is subtle, so it is easy to dismiss as wishful thinking. Following these soft nudges leads you in a direction that feels right in your bones, even before you can explain it to anyone else.",
    "hard": "With Neptune squaring or opposing your North Node for a year or more, your sense of direction clouds over. Paths that seemed clear blur, and people offering guidance turn out to be confused, or quietly serving their own agenda. You feel pulled between the familiar and a vague longing for something more, unsure which way to step. Escapism tempts you, and whole evenings disappear into distraction when you meant to make a plan. Disappointment in a mentor, a group or a cause you believed in stings more than you admit. The confusion is uncomfortable, but it slowly teaches you to tell a true calling from a borrowed dream."
  },
  "pluto|mercury": {
    "conj": "Pluto settles on your Mercury for a year or more, and your mind turns deep and intense. You become obsessed with understanding things fully, reading late into the night, researching every angle, digging beneath polite surfaces. Conversations grow heavier because you say what others avoid, and some people are shaken by your bluntness. Secrets come to light, your own or ones you uncover in others, sometimes through a letter or a message never meant for you. Your thinking fixes on a single problem and refuses to let it go, which is exhausting at three in the morning. By the end of this long stretch your mind is sharper, more penetrating and far harder to fool.",
    "soft": "Pluto lends power to your Mercury for a year or more. You think with unusual focus and depth, and research, writing or investigative work goes well, the kind of task where you disappear for hours and surface with the answer. People listen when you speak, sensing that you mean every word. Hidden information comes your way, through a document, a quiet confession or an insight that arrives in the shower. You grow more persuasive without raising your voice. Because the influence is steady rather than dramatic, it is easy to underuse. Concentration poured into a serious project now gives you lasting authority in your field.",
    "hard": "Pluto squaring or opposing your Mercury for a year or more turns words and ideas into a battleground. Arguments grow intense, and someone tries to control what you say, what you know or what you are allowed to question. You feel pressured to prove your point and catch yourself digging in rather than listening, even with people you love. Secrets, gossip or quiet manipulation surface in conversations at work or at home. Your mind runs obsessively over one issue at night, rehearsing replies to people who are fast asleep. The pressure is draining, yet it teaches you to speak with honesty and force, and it strips away beliefs you had never examined."
  },
  "pluto|jupiter": {
    "conj": "Pluto sits on your Jupiter for a year or more, and your ambitions and beliefs grow enormous. You want more influence, more success and a bigger stage, and for once you feel capable of reaching them. Openings to power appear through money, study, travel or a far larger role than you expected. Your faith in something transforms, sometimes after a crisis that forces you to rethink everything you believed. The drive tips easily into obsession, and you overreach or clash with people who hold more power than you. Handled with care, this period grows your life in ways that remain transformative for decades.",
    "soft": "Pluto steadily strengthens your Jupiter across a year or more. Growth comes through depth rather than luck: you commit fully to a cause, a course of study or a business, and the results compound month by month. Influential people take an interest in your plans, and money, contacts and resources gather around what you care about. Your beliefs feel stronger and more personal, forged through lived experience rather than borrowed from books. You notice you are less interested in small wins and more in lasting impact. The support is steady, so it rewards effort far more than waiting. What you invest now keeps multiplying long after Pluto moves on.",
    "hard": "Pluto squaring or opposing your Jupiter brings a year or more of struggle over power, money or belief. You feel driven to expand, yet rivals, regulations or plain bad timing block your way. Arguments about religion, politics or values turn fierce at the dinner table, and you defend positions harder than you intended. Financial gambles look tempting and backfire badly when made in a hurry. Someone in authority wants to control your growth, or you push against limits that were there for a reason. The pressure transforms your idea of success, leaving you with beliefs that have survived a hard fight."
  },
  "pluto|mc": {
    "conj": "Pluto sits on your MC for a year or more, and your career and public role go through a deep transformation. Jobs end, promotions arrive, or you walk away from a path you once thought permanent, sometimes all within the same year. You feel a hunger for power and meaning in your work, and small roles no longer satisfy you. Power struggles with bosses or institutions are common, and some of them turn bruising. You attract attention, and not all of it is welcome: gossip, envy and scrutiny come with the visibility. By the end of this stretch your public life stands on a foundation you have chosen with full intent.",
    "soft": "Pluto supports your MC in a low key but powerful way for a year or more. Your influence at work grows steadily, and people in positions of authority notice your depth and determination, often long before they say so. Chances to take on more responsibility, change direction or build something lasting appear without a fight. You feel focused and resolute about where your career is going, and distractions fall away. Colleagues come to you in a crisis because you stay calm when others panic. Because the support is steady rather than flashy, it rewards patience and commitment. Choices made now reshape your reputation for years to come.",
    "hard": "A year or more of Pluto squaring or opposing your MC puts your career and home life under deep pressure. Power struggles with bosses, institutions or family members intensify, and you feel forced to choose between competing demands. A job ends, a move is forced on you, or a family matter swallows your attention just as work asks for more. Your ambitions are tested at the root, and you question whether you ever wanted what you were chasing. The stress is heavy and at times frightening in the small hours. What emerges is a clearer sense of what you stand for publicly and privately, and the strength to build it."
  },
  "chiron|moon": {
    "conj": "For many months Chiron sits on your Moon, and old emotional wounds rise to the surface. Memories of childhood, family or times you felt uncared for return, triggered by a smell, a song or an offhand comment from someone close. You feel tender, more easily hurt and more aware of needs you have ignored for years. Home life brings up old patterns, and you notice how you care for others the way you once wished to be cared for. The ache is real, and some days it is hard to shake. This period also opens a deep kind of healing, and you learn to give yourself the comfort you once went without.",
    "soft": "Chiron gently touches your Moon for many months, and emotional healing comes more easily than usual. Conversations with family, a good therapist or a wise friend help you understand feelings that once seemed too tangled to name. You feel more compassionate towards your own needs, and you find ways to nurture yourself that actually work, whether an early night, a proper meal or a call to your sister. Caring for others feels meaningful rather than draining. You notice that someone else's grief no longer knocks you over in the same way. The change is quiet, yet the comfort you learn to give yourself now stays long after Chiron moves on.",
    "hard": "Chiron squaring or opposing your Moon for many months presses on old emotional bruises. A family member, partner or friend says something that lands on the sore spot, and you react more strongly than you expect, sometimes hours later in the kitchen. Home life feels uneasy, and old patterns of neglect or over-caring resurface. You feel raw, needy or guarded, sometimes all in one day. The discomfort is hard to explain to others, which makes it lonelier. Slowly you see how your early wounds shaped what you need now, and you start meeting those needs yourself instead of waiting for rescue."
  },
  "chiron|mars": {
    "conj": "For many months Chiron sits on your Mars, and old hurts around anger, drive and desire come up. You notice where you hold back, where you push too hard, or where you once learnt that wanting things was dangerous. Conflicts touch sore spots, and a small argument about the washing up opens something much older. Your body registers the tension through tiredness or strain in the same familiar places. Your confidence wobbles, and some days you cannot find the energy to start anything. This stretch helps you reclaim your right to want, to act and to fight for yourself cleanly, without apology or excess.",
    "soft": "Chiron gently supports your Mars through many months. You find healthier ways to express anger, pursue desire and use your energy, often through sport, bodywork or an honest conversation you have avoided for years. Old fears about being too much or not enough loosen their grip. You feel braver standing up for yourself and for others, and you notice your voice stays steady when you do. Physical effort becomes a kind of therapy, a run or a boxing class clearing more than your head. The shift is quiet and easy to overlook. Courage you practise now becomes a lasting part of who you are.",
    "hard": "Old wounds around drive and conflict get pressed while Chiron squares or opposes your Mars for many months. Arguments turn painful quickly, and you feel either too aggressive or strangely unable to defend yourself when it matters. Someone pushes a button you did not know you had, and you are shaking for an hour afterwards. Your energy runs unevenly, strong one day and gone the next, which makes plans hard to keep. The frustration is real, and you feel misunderstood by people who only see the reaction. Bit by bit you learn where your anger came from and how to use it in ways that heal rather than harm."
  },
  "chiron|asc": {
    "conj": "For many months Chiron sits on your Ascendant, and old wounds about how you look, move or come across rise up. Comments about your appearance sting more, and you feel self-conscious in photos, mirrors or rooms full of strangers. Your body asks for attention, through small aches, tiredness or a need for different care. You notice how you learnt to hide or perform certain parts of yourself, and the performance starts to feel heavy. The vulnerability is uncomfortable, most of all in public. Yet this stretch lets you show up as you are, and people respond to that honesty with surprising warmth.",
    "soft": "Chiron gently touches your Ascendant for many months, and you feel more at ease in your own skin. Old insecurities about appearance or first impressions soften, and you find clothes, habits or forms of movement that feel like your own. People sense your openness and trust you faster than usual. You become a quiet source of comfort for others who struggle with self-image, the friend who says the kind thing in the changing room. You stop apologising for taking up space. The change is subtle, so it is easy to overlook, yet the self-acceptance built now outlasts the transit by years.",
    "hard": "Chiron squaring or opposing your Ascendant for many months presses on wounds about how others see you. A partner or colleague's remark lands hard, and you feel exposed or misjudged for days afterwards. Relationships bring up old feelings of not fitting in or of being seen wrongly, like the new child in a playground again. Your body shows the strain through tiredness or tension in the shoulders and jaw. Social settings leave you raw, unsure how to present yourself or whether to bother. The work of this period is learning to be seen as you are rather than as you think you should be."
  },
  "uranus|uranus": {
    "conj": "Uranus returning to its own place happens around age 84, and the cycle lasts a year or more. You feel a late burst of independence, curiosity and freedom, surprising the people around you. Old rules matter less, and you do things your own way without apology, from a new hobby to a frank opinion at a family lunch. Sudden changes in living arrangements, health routines or relationships reshape daily life. You look back over a whole lifetime of change and see how far you have travelled. The return brings a sense of completion and a lightness that younger versions of you never quite managed.",
    "soft": "Uranus in easy aspect to itself, at around ages 14, 28, 56 and 70, brings a lively chance to break from routine. You feel freer, more curious and more willing to experiment, with new friends, hobbies or ways of living. Change arrives without much disruption, and you find yourself open to ideas you once dismissed with a roll of the eyes. The mood lasts a year or more, lightly, like a window left open. Because it is easy, the restlessness can pass without leading anywhere. Choosing one fresh direction now keeps your life feeling like your own rather than a habit.",
    "hard": "Uranus square or opposite its own place, around ages 21, 42 and 63, shakes up your life for a year or more. The opposition near 42 is the famous midlife stretch, when you feel a sudden urge to change career, relationship, appearance or home. The squares bring a similar restlessness at younger and older ages, often around leaving education or leaving work. Frustration with routine builds, and you catch yourself making abrupt decisions over breakfast. People around you feel unsettled by the new you. The upheaval shows you where you have lived too safely, and it frees you to live more truthfully."
  },
  "chiron|chiron": {
    "conj": "Chiron returns to its own place around age 50, and the cycle lasts many months. Old wounds you thought were healed come back for another look, often through health, family or a turning point in your work. You feel tender, reflective and newly aware of time, noticing birthdays and endings in a different way. Memories surface, and you see how early hurts shaped the whole path of your life. The ache is real, and so is the release when you finally stop fighting it. Many people become mentors or healers around this time, turning their own struggles into something useful for others.",
    "soft": "Chiron in easy aspect to itself brings a gentle chance to heal. Over many months you notice old hurts losing their grip, and helpful people, books or practices appear at the right time, as if on cue. You feel more compassionate towards yourself and others, and less ashamed of the parts of your story you used to skip. Talking about your struggles becomes easier and even useful to those around you. A younger person seeks you out for advice, and you realise you have something to give. The influence is quiet, yet healing allowed now makes the rest of your life lighter.",
    "hard": "Chiron square or opposite its own place, at ages that vary widely with your birth year but often fall in youth and again in midlife, brings old wounds to the surface for many months. You feel exposed, sensitive and unsure of yourself, especially around the same issues that have always hurt. Relationships, work or health press on these sore spots, and a setback feels bigger than its size. The discomfort is real and hard to explain, even to friends. You notice the pattern repeating and cannot pretend otherwise any longer. That recognition is where the turn begins, and your wounds slowly become sources of wisdom and compassion."
  },
  "jupiter|moon": {
    "conj": "For the next few weeks your emotional life feels roomier, as if someone opened a window in a stuffy flat. You find yourself cooking for more people than planned, saying yes to the family visit, lingering on the phone with your mother or an old friend. Home is a big theme: a move, a new sofa, a relative staying over, or wanting the kitchen full. Your moods swell too, so joy runs high and so does the urge to comfort yourself with one more glass or one more pudding. Feelings you normally keep private come out easily now, and people respond warmly. This stretch gives you permission to need things and to be looked after without apology.",
    "soft": "Over these few weeks life at home feels easier and kinder than usual. A small domestic worry sorts itself out, a housemate becomes more reasonable, or a family member offers help before you have even asked. You sleep better, eat with more pleasure and notice yourself humming while you tidy. Friends seek you out for comfort, and you have enough to give without feeling drained. Nothing here arrives with fanfare, so you can miss it if you are busy chasing bigger things. The mood is soft and generous, and it rewards anything you do to make your surroundings feel like yours: a new plant, a proper dinner, a Sunday left unplanned.",
    "hard": "For several weeks your feelings run larger than the situation calls for. A minor slight from a relative becomes a whole evening of brooding, or a lovely weekend tips into overspending and overeating because more feels like the answer. Family members want more from you, or promise more than they deliver, and you swing between generosity and resentment. Home can feel too small, too crowded or too quiet, and you keep reaching for fixes: a bigger place, a holiday, another online order. The pull is towards emotional honesty about what feeds you. Once you see the difference between comfort and nourishment, this period leaves you with a truer sense of your own needs."
  },
  "jupiter|mars": {
    "conj": "For the next few weeks your energy is up and your appetite for action is enormous. You start the training plan, pitch the idea, book the trip and fire off the email you have been sitting on for a month. Competition feels fun rather than threatening, and you notice people following your lead without much persuasion. Desire runs hot as well, in love and in ambition. The catch is overreach: you commit to three projects when one would do, lift too much at the gym, or push an argument further than it deserves. Channelled well, this is one of the best windows you get for a bold move, because courage and luck arrive together.",
    "soft": "Across these weeks effort pays off more readily than usual. You get up, get going and find that doors open when you push them: the landlord agrees, the team backs your plan, the run feels light. Your temper stays even, and you can be direct without anyone taking offence. It is a lovely time for sport, physical projects, a clear-out of the garage or a push on work that needs stamina. Desire and confidence feel natural rather than forced. Because nothing blocks you, it is tempting to coast, yet the momentum here is real, and whatever you start with energy now keeps rolling long after Jupiter moves on.",
    "hard": "For a few weeks you feel restless, impatient and slightly too big for the room. You interrupt, overcommit, drive faster than you should and take on a fight that was never yours to pick. Someone in authority or a rival pushes back, and within a day a small disagreement becomes a matter of principle. Energy is plentiful, so it spills: into late nights, extra coffee, an impulse purchase or a workout that leaves you sore for days. Beneath all the heat sits a stubborn wish to do something that matters. When that fire goes into one clear aim instead of every passing provocation, this period hands you measurable progress and a stronger sense of your own nerve."
  },
  "jupiter|asc": {
    "conj": "For the next few weeks you are noticed. People compliment your haircut, strangers smile at you in the queue, and invitations arrive that would normally pass you by. You feel more confident in your body and more willing to take up space, speak first, wear the brighter coat. Travel, courses and new circles all beckon, and a fresh start in how you present yourself feels natural. Weight and appetite tend to rise along with optimism, so the waistband is a good barometer. This transit marks the beginning of a roughly twelve-year cycle of growth, and what you start now carries a bright, open quality you will look back on fondly.",
    "soft": "Over these weeks you come across as warmer, easier and more approachable than usual. Conversations with new people flow, and you find yourself chatting to the neighbour you have only ever nodded at. A small upgrade to your appearance lifts your mood out of proportion to its cost. Opportunities come through introductions: a friend of a friend, a chance meeting on a train, a group you join on a whim. Your body feels resilient and you recover quickly from late nights. Little here feels dramatic, which is the point. You are more yourself in public, and people respond to that ease with trust and goodwill.",
    "hard": "For a few weeks the way you come across feels slightly out of step with how you feel inside. You overpromise at a meeting, laugh too loudly at a party, or discover your partner or a close colleague is pulling in a completely different direction. Relationships ask for room: someone needs more from you, or offers more than you can comfortably receive. Your body is prone to excess, so late dinners and extra drinks show quickly. The tension points to growth that has to include other people rather than steamroll them. When you let others be as large as you are, this period broadens your life instead of just your plate."
  },
  "saturn|sun": {
    "conj": "Saturn sits on your Sun for most of a year, and you feel it in your bones. Energy is lower, the to-do list heavier, and every shortcut you have relied on seems to close. You notice who you are once praise, novelty and adrenaline are stripped away. Commitments made now are serious: the mortgage, the business, the decision to leave a role that has become a costume. Tiredness and self-doubt are constant companions, and some mornings the effort feels relentless. What emerges is authority that belongs to you, earned rather than borrowed, and a clear sense of the structure you intend to live inside for the next three decades.",
    "soft": "For several months effort turns into results at a steady, reliable pace. Your manager notices your consistency, a mentor offers useful advice, or an older relative becomes an ally. Routines stick: the early alarm, the budget spreadsheet, the weekly long walk. You feel grounded rather than flat, capable of carrying responsibility without resentment. Nothing arrives as a windfall, and there are days it feels a little dull. Yet the foundations you lay now are solid, and people start treating you as someone who can be relied upon. Quiet respect is the reward of this stretch, and it lasts well beyond it.",
    "hard": "For most of a year you meet resistance at every turn. A boss questions your judgement, a project stalls on paperwork, or someone close tells you a hard truth you did not want to hear. Confidence dips, you feel older than your years, and stress lands in your shoulders, teeth or back. It is easy to read every delay as a verdict on your worth. The friction is sorting what you have built into what holds and what was propped up by hope. By the end you know which efforts deserve your life, and your sense of self rests on firmer ground than before."
  },
  "saturn|venus": {
    "conj": "For several months love and money both ask to be taken seriously. A relationship reaches a point where it either commits or ends, and you feel the weight of that choice. Pleasures that once came easily seem thinner: the evening out costs too much, the flirtation feels hollow. You notice loneliness sharply, even in company, and you start asking what you value. Financially this is a time for budgets, paying down debt and resisting the treat purchase. Underneath the austerity lies something precious: a clearer, more mature sense of whom you love and what you are willing to invest in, which makes the bonds you keep far stronger.",
    "soft": "For a few months your affections settle into something steady and dependable. A partner shows loyalty in practical ways, an older friend offers wisdom about love, or a long-standing connection deepens. Money habits improve: you save without feeling deprived, negotiate a fair price, or sort out the pension. You enjoy simple, lasting pleasures more than flashy ones, like a well-made coat or a dinner cooked slowly. Romance here is less fireworks and more commitment. It suits anyone looking to formalise a partnership or build shared plans, because what you agree on now tends to hold.",
    "hard": "Across several months relationships and finances feel strained. A partner seems cold or distant, a friend lets you down, or you realise you have been giving far more than you receive. Bills arrive at awkward moments, and saying no to spending feels like a punishment. You feel unlovable some days, or unseen, and that ache is hard to talk about. The pressure shows you where affection rests on duty, fear or habit rather than warmth. Connections that survive this come out sturdier, and your sense of your own worth stops depending quite so much on other people's approval."
  },
  "saturn|saturn": {
    "conj": "Your Saturn return lasts roughly a year and arrives around ages 29, 58 and 87. Life asks you to become the adult of your own story. Choices made to please parents, partners or employers stop feeling acceptable, and you find yourself ending the relationship, changing careers, having a child or signing up to something for the long haul. It feels heavy, sometimes lonely, and you notice every consequence of past decisions landing at once. Friends describe you as more serious, and they are right. What you build during this passage becomes the structure of the next three decades, so its demands, though sobering, are worthwhile.",
    "soft": "For several months your sense of duty and your ambitions line up well. The work you have put in over the past years starts to be recognised through a promotion, a qualification or more trust from people who matter. Planning feels natural, and long-term goals seem achievable rather than daunting. You handle responsibility calmly, and others lean on you without it becoming a burden. It is a sound moment to review structures in your life and reinforce the ones that work. Maturity feels less like a weight and more like a quiet strength you have grown into.",
    "hard": "Saturn squaring or opposing its own place marks a checkpoint in your life, roughly every seven years, lasting several months. Commitments made at the last turn of the cycle are tested. A job, a home or a routine that once fitted now pinches, and outside pressures demand adjustment. You feel frustrated, stuck or oddly exposed, as though you are being graded. Authority figures push back, or you find yourself becoming the one who must hold the line. This checkpoint separates structures worth maintaining from those that were only habit, and you leave it with a clearer, more honest plan."
  },
  "saturn|northNode": {
    "conj": "For several months your sense of direction is under the spotlight. You feel a clear call towards the path you are meant to walk, yet every step costs effort, and there is little room for dabbling. Commitments made now carry weight: the course you enrol in, the move towards a new field, the mentor you choose. You notice how often you slip back into familiar comfort, and how heavy that comfort has become. Some days feel lonely or slow. Still, the direction you choose during this stretch becomes a solid foundation, and years from now you recognise it as a turning point.",
    "soft": "Across a few months the practical and the purposeful cooperate. Opportunities that fit your deeper direction come with structure attached: a proper contract, a steady mentor, a timetable you can actually keep. You feel less torn between security and growth, because this time the responsible choice and the meaningful one are the same. Older or more established people help you along. Progress is gradual, and it asks for patience, yet each step feels solid underfoot. You notice fewer evenings spent wondering whether you are wasting your life, because the calendar itself now reflects what matters to you. Something solid is taking shape towards the life that calls you.",
    "hard": "For several months duties and old obligations pull against your sense of purpose. A job demands more hours just as you want to retrain, family expects you to stay put, or you feel too old or too tired to begin. Frustration builds when you see others moving freely towards what you long for. It is tempting to give up on the bigger path entirely. The friction is showing you which responsibilities belong to you and which you carry out of guilt or fear. As you set down the second kind, direction returns with a stronger, more deliberate footing."
  },
  "uranus|mercury": {
    "conj": "Your mind feels electrified for a year or more while Uranus sits on your Mercury. Ideas arrive in the shower, on the bus, at three in the morning, and you want to learn something completely new: coding, a language, a strange subject nobody around you understands. Your speech becomes sharper and quicker, and you surprise people with opinions you did not know you held. News and messages arrive without warning and change plans overnight. Concentration suffers, and nerves run high, so sleep and screens need watching. You come out of this period thinking in a new way, with a voice that sounds more like your own.",
    "soft": "Over a year or so you find yourself curious, inventive and pleasantly restless in your thinking. A new app, course or group of friends opens your mind in ways that feel exciting rather than unsettling. Solutions to old problems pop up out of nowhere, and you explain things with a freshness that people enjoy. Short trips and unexpected conversations bring useful surprises. It is a wonderful time to write, study, update your technology or change how you work. You notice you have outgrown some old opinions without any fuss, and you speak more freely than you used to.",
    "hard": "For a long stretch your mind feels jangled. Plans change at the last minute, emails go astray, and conversations with siblings, neighbours or colleagues turn abrupt and prickly. You blurt out things you meant to keep to yourself, or someone else does, and the fallout shakes up a routine. Anxiety shows up as scrolling late into the night, forgetting keys, or feeling unable to settle into one task. Underneath, rigid ways of thinking are being broken open. Once the noise calms you realise you now see a familiar situation from an entirely new angle, and that clarity was worth the disruption."
  },
  "uranus|jupiter": {
    "conj": "For roughly a year luck arrives from unexpected directions. A job offer out of nowhere, a sudden chance to travel, a windfall or an idea that takes off faster than you imagined. You feel expansive and restless, hungry for freedom and new horizons. Beliefs you held for years now seem too small, and you find yourself drawn to different philosophies, teachers or places. The risk lies in leaping at everything shiny and scattering your good fortune. Yet this is a rare opening, and when you say yes to the right surprise, your world gets permanently bigger.",
    "soft": "For a year or more, fortunate surprises keep turning up. A friend introduces you to an opportunity, a course sparks a new passion, or a trip reshapes your sense of what is possible. You feel optimistic and adventurous without being reckless. New ideas about faith, education or travel open up easily, and you enjoy stretching into them. Small bets tend to work out, and you find yourself freer to follow what interests you. Someone remarks that you seem younger lately, and they are right. This period widens your life in ways that feel exciting and right, and the freedom you taste now becomes hard to give back.",
    "hard": "Your hunger for freedom and growth clashes with the life you have built while Uranus pulls against your Jupiter, often for a year or more. You feel restless, want to quit, move abroad, or throw everything into a sudden plan. Sometimes the upheaval comes from outside: a promised opportunity collapses, or a belief system you trusted lets you down. Overconfidence leads to impulsive decisions about money or travel. The pressure exposes where your idea of success has become too narrow or too borrowed. Making room for a more honest, independent vision lets the growth that follows fit you far better than anything you chased before."
  },
  "uranus|mc": {
    "conj": "Uranus crosses your Midheaven for a year or more, and your career and public life are shaken up. You feel an urgent need for independence at work: to go freelance, change industries, or stop playing a role that bores you. Sudden changes arrive: a restructure, a new boss, a surprising offer. Your reputation shifts too, as people start seeing you as the original or the rebel. It is unsettling, and some days you wonder what on earth you are doing. Yet the path that opens now is far closer to your own nature, and the risk is well worth taking.",
    "soft": "Over a year or two your working life gains fresh air. Innovative projects, flexible arrangements or new technology open doors, and you find it easier to shape your role around your strengths. Colleagues respond well to your ideas, and you feel free to experiment without jeopardising your standing. A side interest turns into something professional, or an unusual contact leads to a new opportunity. Change here feels exciting rather than threatening, and your reputation grows as someone who brings a different perspective. You catch yourself enjoying Monday mornings, which surprises you. This is a good time to modernise how you work and to let your reputation catch up with the person you have become.",
    "hard": "For a year or more your career feels unpredictable and your home life pulls against it. A job disappears, a boss clashes with you, or a sudden family matter forces you to rethink your ambitions. You feel restless in a role that once seemed secure, and impatience with authority grows sharp. At times it seems every plan gets overturned just as you settle. The disruption is loosening a career path that had become too rigid or too dutiful. Once you let it shift, work appears that allows far more of your own character to show."
  },
  "neptune|moon": {
    "conj": "Your emotional world grows porous and dreamy while Neptune sits on your Moon, a stretch of a year or more. You cry at adverts, pick up on a friend's mood before they have taken their coat off, and feel homesick for a place you cannot name. Family boundaries blur: you absorb a relative's troubles, or someone at home needs looking after and you slide into the carer's role without deciding to. Dreams turn vivid, and some mornings you wake foggy and drained for no clear reason. Wine, box sets and daydreams about another life all call more loudly than usual. Beneath the haze, compassion and imagination are growing, and you come out of it with a softer, more spiritual relationship with your own heart.",
    "soft": "Your feelings open in gentle, lovely ways while Neptune eases your Moon, a mood that lasts a year or two. Music, the sea, a candlelit bath or an hour alone with a sketchbook restore you more than a night out ever could. Intuition sharpens, and you know what a loved one needs before they say it, whether that is soup, silence or a long hug. Home becomes a sanctuary, with new colours, softer lighting or a garden you tend at dusk. Caring for someone feels natural rather than draining. Creative and spiritual pursuits nourish you, and you remember your dreams more often. This long, quiet stretch teaches you to trust your inner life and treat your own needs with tenderness.",
    "hard": "Neptune squaring or opposing your Moon leaves your emotional footing uncertain for a year or more. Sadness or anxiety arrives without an obvious cause, or you discover that a family situation was never quite what you believed. Someone close leans on you heavily, and you keep rescuing people who leave you depleted. Escape is tempting: another glass, another hour scrolling in bed, another fantasy about moving to the coast and starting again. Old confusion around your mother or your childhood home drifts back into view. The fog is dissolving emotional patterns that once protected you and now only blur things. When it lifts, you feel kinder towards yourself and far clearer about what you need."
  },
  "neptune|mars": {
    "conj": "For a year or more your drive feels strangely soft. You sit down to tackle the task and find yourself staring out of the window, and the competitive edge you once relied on seems to evaporate. Anger comes out sideways, as sulking, sighing or vague exhaustion rather than a clean argument. Desire turns romantic and idealistic, pulling you towards art, causes, rescue missions or someone who seems to need saving. Misreading what you want, or being misled by someone else, is easy now. Slowly, though, your actions reorganise around inspiration instead of willpower. When your effort serves something larger than your own ambition, it flows with a grace that surprises you.",
    "soft": "Over a year or two your actions feel guided by something gentler than ambition. You find yourself volunteering at the food bank, joining a dance class or throwing your weekends into a creative project that lights you up. Intuition tells you when to move, so you stop forcing doors and find they open anyway. Arguments soften, and you handle a prickly colleague with more compassion than you expected of yourself. Flowing movement suits your body beautifully: swimming, yoga, long walks beside water. You achieve a surprising amount while barely feeling the strain. This period shows you that effort can be inspired rather than grinding, and that lesson stays with you.",
    "hard": "For a long stretch your energy feels scattered and your aims keep slipping out of focus. You start projects with great enthusiasm and drift away within weeks, or push hard towards a goal that turns out to be a mirage. Someone seems to be quietly undermining you, and it is hard to tell whether that is real or your tiredness talking. Temper curdles into passive resentment, and your body feels more fragile than usual, so rest counts for more than willpower. Fantasy lures you away from the hard graft. Through all of it you learn which desires are truly yours, and your drive becomes cleaner, kinder and far more trustworthy."
  },
  "neptune|asc": {
    "conj": "Neptune crossing your Ascendant makes you softer, harder to pin down and far more sensitive to your surroundings, and the effect lasts a year or more. People project onto you: one friend sees a muse, a colleague sees a saviour, a new acquaintance sees someone you do not recognise at all. Your appearance shifts too, through a looser style, a change in weight or a dreamy quality others comment on. Crowded shops and loud offices leave you wrung out, because your skin feels thinner. Losing track of who you are is easy when everyone reflects a different version back. Yet an old, rigid self-image is dissolving, and in its place comes a gentler, more intuitive way of meeting the world.",
    "soft": "Over a year or two you come across as warmer and more magnetic. Strangers tell you their life story at the bus stop, and you read the mood of a room within seconds of walking in. Artistic and spiritual interests seep into how you dress, and you enjoy softer colours, flowing fabrics or a scent that feels like you. Relationships take on a romantic, intuitive quality, and you drift easily into the company of people who share your ideals. Your body responds beautifully to gentle care: swimming, massage, earlier nights. Nothing here is loud. You move through daily life with more grace, and people find you easy to trust.",
    "hard": "For a long stretch your relationships and your sense of how you come across both feel blurry. A partner turns evasive, or you idealise someone new who later proves quite different from the picture you painted. You leave conversations unsure what impression you made, and low energy makes it harder to show up fully. Misunderstandings multiply because you say one thing and others hear another. People pleasing and quiet escape both tempt you, since saying yes is easier than being seen clearly. As the haze thins, you learn to see others as they really are, and you present yourself with far more honesty and a gentle, settled confidence."
  },
  "pluto|sun": {
    "conj": "Your identity goes through something like a rebirth while Pluto sits on your Sun, a passage of a year or more. The role you played at work, the way you chased approval, the version of you your family expects: none of it fits any more. Power struggles break out with bosses, partners or parents, and you feel a fierce urge to take control of your own life. Endings arrive in career, relationships or routines, and some weeks feel like a crisis. Buried parts of you surface, including ambition, anger and raw desire. By the far side of this passage you have become a stronger, more authentic person who knows what they stand for.",
    "soft": "Over a year or two your personal power grows steadily, month by month. You handle challenges with more depth and resilience, and people start taking you more seriously in meetings and at family gatherings alike. Chances to transform your life arrive in manageable doses: a role with influence, therapy that finally helps, the decision to walk away from an old habit for good. Change comes from the inside out, and you feel equal to it. Your presence becomes stronger without needing to be loud. You renew yourself profoundly during this stretch, and the change holds.",
    "hard": "For a year or more you feel pushed and tested by forces bigger than you. A controlling boss, a domineering partner or an unyielding institution puts you under sustained pressure, and every conversation feels like a negotiation. Confidence and vitality both take a knock, and on bad days you wonder whether you are losing yourself altogether. Buried fears and resentments surface, sometimes dramatically, in a slammed door or an unexpected resignation. Fighting everything and giving up entirely both tempt you. This intensity strips away what was false in your sense of self, and what survives is a core that is tougher, clearer and entirely your own."
  },
  "pluto|venus": {
    "conj": "Pluto sits on your Venus for a year or more, and love and money become intense and transformative. A relationship arrives that grips you completely, or an existing bond goes through a deep crisis and emerges changed beyond recognition. Jealousy, longing and desire run stronger than you have known, and you find yourself checking your phone at midnight or replaying a conversation for days. Money shifts dramatically too, through debts, an inheritance, a joint account or a bold new venture. You see with new clarity what you value and what you have tolerated for far too long. It is unsettling and sometimes painful. The love and self-worth you claim during this passage run far deeper than anything before.",
    "soft": "Your relationships deepen in ways that feel powerful and rewarding while Pluto supports your Venus, over a year or two. You meet someone who sees straight past your surface charm, or an existing bond turns more honest and more intimate after a long, late conversation. Your sense of your own worth strengthens, and asking for what you want, a raise, a better deal, more affection, becomes easier. Money improves through shrewd decisions and a franker look at where it goes each month. Pleasure takes on a richer, more sensual quality. This stretch teaches you to love more fully and to value yourself with conviction, and those lessons hold for years.",
    "hard": "Love and money feel fraught while Pluto squares or opposes your Venus, often for a year or more. Jealousy or control creeps into a relationship, or you realise a partnership has always rested on unequal power. Shared finances become a battleground: who pays for what, whose name is on the lease, what was promised and never delivered. Fear of losing someone or something you treasure keeps you awake. Old wounds around being wanted and being enough rise to the surface, raw and insistent. Facing these patterns honestly is exhausting. What you keep afterwards, in love and in money, is deeper, fairer and far more your own."
  },
  "pluto|saturn": {
    "conj": "Pluto on your Saturn puts the structures of your life through deep renovation, a process that lasts a year or more. A career, a marriage or a set of rules you have lived by starts crumbling, and you feel pressure to rebuild from the ground up. Authority figures loom large, or you find yourself suddenly holding serious power over other people's livelihoods. Old fears about failure, control and not being good enough surface with force. Weeks go by that feel heavy and bleak, and you carry them in your jaw and shoulders. Yet what you construct from here rests on far firmer foundations, and your ambition gains a strength and depth it never had before.",
    "soft": "Over a year or two you gain lasting power to reshape your responsibilities. You restructure a business, overhaul a household budget or redirect a career, and the changes hold firm. Discipline deepens without turning harsh, so committing to long, demanding goals feels natural. People with influence notice your seriousness and back your efforts. Problems that once looked too large to touch, an old debt, a failing system at work, now yield to patient, strategic pressure. You enjoy the feeling of steady control. What you rebuild during this stretch lasts a very long time, and you know it.",
    "hard": "For a year or more you feel squeezed between forces demanding change and structures refusing to budge. Work turns into a battleground, a manager seems bent on control, or commitments you once chose freely now feel like a cage. Fear of failure sharpens, and you catch yourself becoming rigid or controlling in turn. Some weeks the pressure feels relentless, and you come home too tired to talk. This grinding period reveals what in your life must be dismantled so that something stronger can replace it. Once you accept that, your resilience grows immensely and your authority becomes real."
  },
  "pluto|northNode": {
    "conj": "Your life direction intensifies while Pluto sits on your North Node, a stretch of a year or more. You feel an almost fated pull towards a new path, and events keep pushing you away from old comforts whether you are ready or not. People arrive who change your trajectory: a mentor, a rival, a lover, a stranger with one crucial piece of advice. Half measures stop working, and every choice feels loaded with consequence. The pace is powerful and at times frightening, and you lie awake weighing what you are about to give up. Yet this passage aligns you with your deeper purpose in a way you cannot deny, and you emerge certain of where you are going.",
    "soft": "Over a year or two your growth accelerates in natural, empowering ways. Opportunities to follow your true direction arrive with enough support behind them that stepping forward feels possible rather than reckless. You find the nerve to drop habits that kept you small, like saying yes to every favour or hiding your real ambitions. Influential people and deep experiences steer you well. Other people's expectations lose their grip. You notice that you talk about the future with more conviction, and friends start to believe in it too. This stretch moves you towards your purpose with a quiet confidence that lasts.",
    "hard": "For a year or more you feel pulled between old habits and a new direction, with power struggles complicating both. Someone tries to steer your choices, a parent, partner or employer with firm views on what you should do next. Alternatively you wake up to the fact that you have been following a path built for someone else. Frustration and intensity rise, and the pressure to change feels overwhelming. Clinging harder to what feels safe is tempting, even as it chafes. This struggle is clearing ground for your true direction, and once you let go, the way forward becomes strikingly clear."
  },
  "chiron|mercury": {
    "conj": "For many months old wounds around being heard and understood come to the surface. Memories return of being called slow at school, of stammering in front of the class, of adults talking over you at the dinner table. Conversations feel tender, and a throwaway comment from a colleague stings for days. You notice how often you apologise before speaking. At the same time you discover a wisdom in you, and it pours out when you teach, write or sit with someone who struggles the way you once did. Feeling this exposed is uncomfortable. By the end your voice has become a source of healing, for you and for the people around you.",
    "soft": "Over many months your words take on a healing quality. You explain something difficult to a frightened friend and watch their shoulders drop, or you write about an experience that once felt unspeakable and find it lighter afterwards. Learning feels less anxious, so you sign up for the course or tackle the skill that used to intimidate you. People seek your advice, and you give it gently, without lecturing. Old stories about your own intelligence loosen their hold. You understand your history more fully now, and the insights you gain during these months turn out to be useful to others.",
    "hard": "For many months communication feels painful and awkward. Misunderstandings keep cropping up, criticism cuts deeper than usual, and you feel self-conscious about every word. You rewrite a simple email six times, rehearse phone calls in your head, or go quiet in meetings rather than risk sounding foolish. Old memories of being mocked, dismissed or silenced resurface without warning. A sibling or neighbour touches a nerve you thought had healed. As these hurts are acknowledged rather than argued with, you build a gentler relationship with your own mind. Your voice comes through this stretch steadier and more your own."
  },
  "chiron|jupiter": {
    "conj": "For many months your beliefs and hopes brush against old hurts. Faith in a teacher, a religion, a guru or a grand plan falters, or you realise your cheerful optimism has been covering a long disappointment. You notice where you promised yourself more than life delivered, and it aches. Generosity has a sore edge too, as you see how often you gave to be liked. At the same time, wisdom grows out of these wounds, and you feel drawn to share what you have learned through teaching, travel or mentoring someone younger. This period is tender and humbling. The meaning you find now is far deeper and more honest than any borrowed creed.",
    "soft": "Over many months growth and healing work hand in hand. A course, a long trip or a wise mentor helps you make peace with something painful from the past. Old disappointments lose their sting, and you catch yourself speaking about them with humour rather than bitterness. Generosity towards others deepens, because you remember what it was like to need help. Guiding a friend through a rough patch feels natural and even joyful. Your beliefs grow more compassionate and more inclusive. These months help you turn hard experience into wisdom that genuinely lifts the people around you.",
    "hard": "For many months old disappointments around luck, faith and opportunity resurface. You feel cheated by life when a friend lands the break you wanted, or a belief you leaned on for years stops holding up. Overspending, overeating or overpromising cover a deeper ache you would rather not name. A teacher, institution or spiritual figure lets you down, and the loss of trust hurts more than you expected. Cynicism is tempting. As you face these hurts honestly, you build a grounded optimism, one that no longer needs to look away from pain in order to keep hoping."
  },
  "chiron|mc": {
    "conj": "For many months your career and public image bring old wounds into view. You feel exposed at work, doubt your competence in meetings, and remember past failures and rejections with sharp clarity. A performance review or a public moment touches a nerve that runs back to childhood expectations. Alongside the discomfort comes a pull towards work that heals: counselling, teaching, caring, or bringing more humanity to the job you already do. Being visible feels uncomfortable yet meaningful. What emerges over this period is a vocation shaped by what you have survived, and a reputation built on genuine empathy rather than polish.",
    "soft": "Over many months your working life gains a healing dimension. Colleagues come to you in difficult moments, closing your office door or messaging late at night, and you find the right words. You feel drawn towards work that helps people directly, or towards mentoring someone who reminds you of your younger self. Past professional setbacks start to make sense, and some even turn into strengths you talk about openly. Your reputation grows as someone wise and trustworthy rather than merely capable. These months let you bring your whole experience, including the painful chapters, into your public role with grace.",
    "hard": "For many months career and home life pull on old wounds. A boss triggers a familiar feeling of never being good enough, a public mistake stings far longer than it should, or family expectations clash painfully with your ambitions. You feel unsure of your standing and hypersensitive to feedback, replaying a single comment on the drive home. Imposter feelings grow loud. The tension brings buried hurts about success, failure and parental approval into the open where they can be tended. As you do that work, your sense of vocation becomes more honest and more resilient, and you stop needing the job title to prove your worth."
  },
  "neptune|neptune": {
    "conj": "Neptune takes about 165 years to circle back to its own place, so a full return never arrives in a human life. What you feel instead is the long, slow unfolding of your dreams and your spiritual hunger across decades. Some years you notice it sharply: a sudden longing for the sea, a pull towards music, prayer or meditation, a sense that ordinary success is not quite enough. You feel your ideals shifting under the surface of daily life. None of this is dramatic. It colours the whole of your life, and looking back you see how your deepest hopes have ripened.",
    "soft": "Neptune's sextile to its own place, around your late twenties, and its trine in your mid fifties each bring several years of gentle spiritual deepening. You find yourself lingering in galleries, keeping a dream journal or drawn to a quiet practice that settles your mind. Intuition becomes easier to trust, and you notice meaningful coincidences more often. Compassion flows towards strangers as well as friends. Ambition softens a little, making room for beauty, music and meaning in ordinary days. These stretches help you trust your inner compass, and the ideals you clarify now guide you for years afterwards.",
    "hard": "Neptune squares its own place around your early forties, and the effect lingers for a few years. You feel disillusioned with dreams you have chased for decades, and a quiet voice asks what any of it was for. Fatigue, vagueness and a longing to escape are common: a fantasy of chucking in the job, a crush that feels like salvation, another glass on a weekday. Plans that once inspired you now look faintly unreal. This midlife fog is dissolving illusions you no longer need. What remains afterwards is a humbler, more authentic sense of meaning that belongs to you rather than to anyone's expectations."
  },
  "jupiter|mercury": {
    "conj": "For a few weeks Jupiter sits on your natal Mercury, and your mind feels like a window thrown open. You read three books at once, sign up for the course you have eyed for a year, and talk with a fluency that surprises you in meetings. Ideas arrive in the shower and on the bus, and people actually want to hear them. Letters, contracts and applications sent now land well, and a chat with a stranger turns into a job lead. The catch is scale: you promise more than a normal week holds, skim the small print and say yes to every interesting thread. Your thinking grows bigger here, and the best of these ideas will still look good once the weeks have passed.",
    "soft": "Over the next few weeks your thinking moves with an easy tailwind. Emails get answered quickly, the pitch you were nervous about comes out clear, and someone who teaches or publishes notices what you have to say. Explaining something complicated to a friend over dinner, you realise you understand it better than you thought. Short trips, workshops and chance reading turn up the one piece of information you needed. Because it all flows, you can drift into pleasant chatter and leave the harder writing untouched. Nothing forces your hand in this window, yet the confidence it lends your voice is real, and whatever you put into words now carries further than usual.",
    "hard": "For a few weeks your mind runs ahead of your facts. You feel certain about a plan, an argument or a purchase, and then someone asks one plain question that exposes the gap. Meetings stretch as you overexplain, you commit to three deadlines that overlap, and a friend gently points out that you said the same thing yesterday with a different conclusion. Arguments about beliefs, politics or who is right flare more easily than usual. Underneath is a hunger to think bigger than your current setting allows. Once you slow down enough to check the details, this stretch shows you which of your opinions deserve to grow and which were only enthusiasm."
  },
  "jupiter|jupiter": {
    "conj": "Your Jupiter return comes round roughly every twelve years, near 12, 24, 36, 48, 60 and 72, and its peak lasts a few weeks with echoes across the year. You feel a pull to widen your life: a move, a degree, a trip you keep postponing, a new faith in your own direction. Offers arrive that match who you are becoming rather than who you were twelve years ago. Sketching plans on a napkin at a café table, you catch yourself meaning every line. Excess is part of it too, from overspending to overbooking to believing every opportunity is the one. The choices you make here set the tone for the next twelve years, which makes this a clean start.",
    "soft": "Jupiter is making a friendly angle to its own natal place, which happens at points through each twelve-year cycle and lasts a few weeks. Life feels generous. A colleague recommends you, a small bet on yourself pays off, and a plan that stalled last year finds its people. There is more laughter at home and less worry about money, even when the numbers have barely changed. This is growth by momentum rather than drama, so it slips past unnoticed if you are busy. Doors open a crack rather than being flung wide, and the ones you walk through now lead somewhere that suits your nature.",
    "hard": "Around three, six and nine years into each twelve-year cycle, Jupiter squares or opposes its own place, and for a few weeks your appetite for more meets the limits of what you already have. You want the bigger flat, the new course, the second business, and the budget or the calendar says not yet. Someone else's success stings, and you wonder whether your beliefs still fit the life you are living. Promises made in a rush at your last return come due. Restlessness runs through all of it, along with honest information about where you have outgrown your plans. Whatever feels too small now is showing you the next size of your life, provided you resist inflating it overnight."
  },
  "jupiter|mc": {
    "conj": "For a few weeks Jupiter crosses the top of your chart, and your working life steps into the light. People with influence notice what you do, a promotion or public role comes up, and your name travels further than your usual circle. You find yourself in the room where decisions are made, or asked to speak at the event instead of just attending it. Often this recognition comes from years of steady work paying off. The trap is taking on every visible role at once and overreaching on a reputation that is still forming. This transit marks a high point in a twelve year career cycle, and the steps you take in public now shape how you are seen for years.",
    "soft": "Over the next few weeks your reputation works for you without much pushing. A former boss mentions you to someone useful, a proposal gets approved faster than expected, and people you respect start treating you as the person who knows. Even on a dull Tuesday you feel steadier about where your career is going. Opportunities arrive through goodwill rather than competition, often from teachers, mentors or contacts abroad. Coasting is tempting because nothing feels urgent. Still, this is a lovely window for raising your profile, and professional doors opened in these weeks have a habit of staying open.",
    "hard": "For a few weeks your ambitions pull against the rest of your life. Work offers something bigger while home, family or your own body wants you to stay put. You say yes to the extra project and then end up answering emails at the kitchen table at midnight. A boss or public figure promises more than they deliver, or you promise more than you can. Your sense of what you deserve professionally inflates faster than the path to get there. The friction is useful, because it reveals where your career has grown out of balance with your private needs and which opportunity is worth the cost."
  },
  "saturn|moon": {
    "conj": "For several months Saturn sits on your natal Moon, and your emotional life turns serious and heavy. You feel tired in a way sleep does not fix, and home asks more of you than usual: a parent needing care, a lease ending, a household that runs on your effort. You cry less and brood more, and comfort food and old routines stop doing their job. Loneliness visits even in a full house. Underneath the weight, you are learning to hold yourself instead of waiting to be held. By the time Saturn moves on, your inner life is sturdier, simpler and far more honestly your own.",
    "soft": "Over these months Saturn lends your feelings a steady frame. You sort out the home that has been chaotic, set a bedtime you keep, or have the calm conversation with family that you avoided for years. People lean on you, and for once it feels manageable rather than draining. An older relative or a patient friend offers practical help instead of opinions. The mood is quiet, even a little flat, and you miss some spontaneity. Anything you build emotionally during this period lasts, whether that is a secure home, a kinder routine or a relationship with clearer boundaries.",
    "hard": "For some months your needs collide with your obligations. Work demands late nights while someone at home needs you, or a responsibility you took on out of love starts to feel like a weight. You snap at a partner over the washing up and realise the anger is exhaustion in disguise. Old feelings of not being looked after resurface, sometimes around a parent or a house move. Moods run low and criticism lands harder than usual. This pressure shows you precisely where you have been giving without receiving, and the arrangements you change now leave you better supported for years."
  },
  "saturn|mars": {
    "conj": "For a few months Saturn sits right on your natal Mars, and your drive meets a wall. You push hard at a project and it moves at walking pace, or a boss, a rule or a physical limit stops you just as you want to charge. Frustration builds in the body: jaw clenched in traffic, a short fuse at the gym, anger swallowed at work. The same transit also turns raw energy into discipline. You train, practise and grind in a way that produces measurable results. Energy that used to come in fits and starts becomes stamina, and that stamina stays with you long after Saturn moves on.",
    "soft": "Over the coming months your effort and your patience line up. You stick with the training plan, finish the renovation, or keep chipping at a long task with unusual consistency. Someone in authority respects how hard you work and hands you more responsibility. Anger feels more contained, and you can say a firm no without it turning into a fight. None of it is thrilling, and some days feel like pure graft. You notice the satisfaction of ticking off a task at the end of a long day, and it feels earned. The ambitions you back with steady action during this window turn into measurable achievements that nobody can take from you.",
    "hard": "For several months you feel blocked every time you move. A manager overrules you, a regulation stops the plan, or an injury slows the body you rely on. Irritation leaks out in small ways: a slammed cupboard, the sharp email, pushing through fatigue until something gives. Other people seem to hold the power you need. This is a hard test of patience and of how you handle anger when it cannot simply be released. Learning where to push and where to wait is what this period teaches, and the strength you build under it is quieter, deeper and far more reliable."
  },
  "saturn|asc": {
    "conj": "For several months Saturn crosses your Ascendant, and you feel the full weight of being yourself in the world. In the mirror you see more maturity, a new line around the eyes or a quieter expression. People take you more seriously, and you dress, speak and carry yourself with more reserve. Energy dips, and you need more rest than your diary allows. A new chapter of personal responsibility starts here, often with a clear decision about who you will be for the next few years. Roles that no longer fit fall away, and you step into your own authority with both feet.",
    "soft": "Over these months you come across as steady, reliable and grounded, and people respond to it. A new habit sticks: the morning walk, the simpler plate, the earlier night. In interviews and difficult meetings you carry a quiet confidence, and older or more senior people trust you with something important. Your style simplifies into something classic that suits you. Life feels slower, occasionally dull, with fewer spontaneous adventures. Friends start asking how you manage to stay so calm when things go wrong at work. The self you shape through small, repeated choices now becomes the self you wear comfortably for years.",
    "hard": "For some months you feel judged, watched or held back in how you present yourself. A partner questions who you have become, a boss critiques your manner, or your body signals that it needs more care than you have been giving it. You catch yourself shrinking in a room where you used to shine. Relationships and personal freedom pull against each other, and commitments feel heavier than usual. The pressure is real, and it is also clarifying. Working through it, you drop the version of yourself you performed for others and settle into one that can hold its ground."
  },
  "uranus|sun": {
    "conj": "Uranus sits on your Sun for a year or more, and your identity gets shaken awake. Suddenly you cannot keep living the same way: the job, the look, the relationship or the city feels too tight. Unexpected events arrive, from surprise offers to abrupt endings, and your plans shift week by week. Friends notice you are different, braver and less predictable. The restlessness makes you impulsive and, at times, hard to live with. This is one of the great liberations of a lifetime, and the person you become through it feels far more like you than the one who went in.",
    "soft": "Change comes to you in a form you can use while Uranus supports your Sun, across a year or more. A chance meeting, a new technology or an unexpected offer opens a path that suits who you are now. You try the class, the haircut or the side project you once thought was not for you, and it clicks. Friends say you seem lighter and more original. Because the shifts feel so easy, you can let them pass without acting. A throwaway idea over coffee with a friend turns into a plan you are still excited about a month later. Seize even one, and your life gains a freedom that outlasts the transit by many years.",
    "hard": "For a year or more, life keeps jolting your sense of who you are. A restructure at work, a relationship ending or a sudden move arrives with little warning, and plans made in good faith collapse. You feel restless and rebellious, quick to quit or to break a pattern before anyone else breaks it for you. People around you find you harder to predict. Stress runs through your nerves, and sleep often suffers. All this pressure strips away a self that had grown too narrow, and what replaces it is freer and more your own."
  },
  "uranus|venus": {
    "conj": "Uranus sits on your Venus for a year or more, and your love life, tastes and finances wake up. You fall for someone completely unlike your usual type, or a relationship that used to feel safe starts to feel suffocating. Your style changes overnight: a bold haircut, a new wardrobe, music you never listened to before. Money comes and goes in surprising ways. The rush of excitement makes you reckless with hearts and budgets alike. The discovery is what you want rather than what you were taught to want, and that knowledge reshapes your relationships for good.",
    "soft": "Over a year or more, love and pleasure bring welcome surprises. You meet someone through an unusual channel, an existing relationship finds a fresh spark, or a creative hobby turns unexpectedly profitable. Asking for space within a partnership becomes possible without drama. Friendships widen to include people from very different worlds, and weekends fill with things you have never tried. These openings are easy to treat as passing fun. Underneath, though, they update your idea of what a good relationship looks like, and the changes you make now bring a lighter, more honest kind of intimacy.",
    "hard": "Your relationships and money feel unstable while Uranus squares or opposes your Venus, often for a year or more. A partner wants more freedom, or you do, and the tension breaks out in sudden arguments or long silences. Attraction arrives out of nowhere and threatens what you already have. Spending swings between impulsive treats and late night panic over bills. Comfort starts to bore you and you crave excitement. You find yourself scrolling through old photos, wondering who you were trying to please back then. The disruption forces an honest look at whether your love life still reflects who you are, and whatever survives this period is stronger for having been freely chosen."
  },
  "uranus|saturn": {
    "conj": "For a year or more Uranus sits on your Saturn, and the structures you built your life on start to crack. A secure job becomes a cage, a rule you lived by stops making sense, or an authority figure you trusted lets you down. You feel torn between the safety you worked for and a sudden urge to walk away. Some days you defend the old order fiercely; on others you want to tear it down. The upheaval is uncomfortable, and it lets you rebuild a career and a set of commitments that fit who you are now.",
    "soft": "With Uranus in easy aspect to your Saturn for a year or more, you find ways to update your life without blowing it up. A job adds flexible hours, a long commitment gets renegotiated on better terms, or you bring fresh methods into a system that has run the same way for years. Older colleagues back your new ideas, and your own sense of duty loosens just enough to let you breathe. Change feels practical rather than frightening. Because the window is gentle, reform happens gradually and without headlines. Even the tedious admin of changing arrangements feels oddly satisfying, like opening a window in a stuffy room. Your rearrangements give you a stability that includes some freedom.",
    "hard": "The need for security and the need for freedom pull hard against each other while Uranus clashes with your Saturn, a strain that lasts a year or more. You feel trapped by the mortgage, the contract or the role you agreed to, and then frightened by the thought of leaving it. A boss, parent or institution resists your changes, or sudden events undermine a plan you relied on. Nerves run tight and you swing between rebellion and rigid control. Working through the strain, you learn which responsibilities belong to you and which were only fear. Your life then reorganises around the ones worth keeping."
  },
  "uranus|northNode": {
    "conj": "Uranus sits on your North Node for a year or more, and your sense of direction gets a sudden jolt forward. You meet someone who opens a completely new path, or an unexpected event pushes you towards the life you have secretly wanted. Plans that felt fixed start to look optional. Unusual groups, causes or technologies draw you in and feel strangely familiar. The speed unsettles you and leaves some people behind. Friends say you seem like a different person, and they are half right. This transit points you at your future with rare clarity, and the leaps you take now look, in hindsight, like destiny.",
    "soft": "Over a year or more, surprising encounters nudge you along your path. A new community, an online group or a collaborator appears just when you need them. Stepping away from old habits that kept you circling feels easier, and your choices start to feel fresher and more your own. Opportunities come in sideways rather than through the front door, often via a friend of a friend. Because they arrive without fuss, they are easy to overlook in a busy month. The odd coincidences of this period are pointing you towards growth that suits your life direction.",
    "hard": "For a year or more, sudden changes seem to pull you off course. A move, a job loss or a restless partner disrupts the direction you were building, and you are unsure whether to fight for the old plan or follow the new chaos. Under stress you slip back into comfortable old patterns. Other people's upheavals spill into your path and demand your time. The frustration is real, and the disruption is also testing whether your chosen direction is truly yours. Once the dust settles, what remains is closer to your real purpose than the plan you started with."
  },
  "neptune|mercury": {
    "conj": "Neptune sits on your Mercury for a year or more, and your thinking goes soft at the edges. You forget appointments, misread emails and drift mid sentence while your mind wanders somewhere lovely. Imagination flourishes: you scribble poems in margins, dream vividly and sense what people mean before they say it. Facts, figures and contracts need extra care because details slip through. Some people mislead you, and sometimes you mislead yourself. Across this period your mind learns to hear intuition and images as clearly as logic, and the way you speak gains new depth and tenderness.",
    "soft": "Your mind becomes more intuitive and creative while Neptune eases your Mercury, a gentle stretch of a year or more. You find the right words to comfort a grieving friend, write or sketch with unusual flow, and pick up on the mood of a room before anyone speaks. Music, film and novels move you more than usual. Practical tasks still get done, just without the old rigidity. When deadlines loom, the softness slides into daydreaming. A song on the radio can stop you in the middle of the supermarket aisle. For any work that blends imagination with communication, this is a gifted season, and your voice carries a warmth people remember.",
    "hard": "Confusion creeps into your conversations and decisions while Neptune squares or opposes your Mercury, a haze that lasts a year or more. You sign something without reading it properly, believe a story that turns out to be false, or find your own words misunderstood in painful ways. Focus drifts, and you reread the same paragraph three times before it sinks in. Someone's charm hides an agenda. Much of the time you feel foggy and unsure of what you think. The fog is also a teacher: it shows you where you leaned on a certainty that was never real, and your judgement grows wiser for having been tested."
  },
  "neptune|jupiter": {
    "conj": "Neptune sits on your Jupiter for a year or more, and your hopes swell into something almost spiritual. Faith, art, retreats, travel to places that feel sacred or a cause bigger than yourself start calling. Generosity pours out of you, sometimes faster than your bank account can manage. You believe in people and plans with a wide open heart. That same idealism leaves you open to schemes, gurus and promises that sound too good to be true. What you gain here is a larger sense of meaning, and it serves you best with one foot kept firmly on the ground.",
    "soft": "Over a year or more, your beliefs deepen gently. A practice, a teacher or a community appears that nourishes you, or your compassion grows through volunteering or caring work. Creative projects feel touched by inspiration, and you finish a painting or a piece of writing that surprises you. Luck arrives through kindness rather than strategy. The mood is so pleasant that you drift without much direction. Strangers open up to you on trains and in queues, sensing somehow that you will listen. The spiritual and imaginative growth of this period stays with you as a lasting sense of trust in life.",
    "hard": "For a year or more, your hopes and your reality refuse to match. You invest in a dream that dissolves, trust a promise that goes nowhere, or overspend chasing a vision you cannot yet afford. Faith in people or ideals gets shaken, and you feel lost about what you believe. Escape tempts you nightly: another episode, another glass, another grand plan. Disappointment is part of the picture, and so is a necessary pruning of illusions. A friend's blunt honesty stings at the time and later feels like the kindest thing anyone said to you. The faith that survives this period is humbler, more personal and far more reliable."
  },
  "neptune|mc": {
    "conj": "Neptune crosses the top of your chart over a year or more, and your career goals blur and dissolve. The ambition that once drove you starts to feel empty, and you long for work that carries meaning: healing, art, service or spirit. Your public image softens, and people project onto you whatever they want to see. Plans at work shift without explanation, and roles become unclear. For a while you drift professionally, unsure what to say when someone asks what you do. Beneath the fog runs a calling, pulling your working life towards something that feeds your soul.",
    "soft": "Inspiration flows into your working life while Neptune supports your MC, over a year or more. Creative or caring work starts to feel possible, a mentor recognises your sensitivity, or your reputation gains a gentle glow. Colleagues come to you for empathy as much as expertise, lingering at your desk to talk. Art, music, film or healing work finds a place in your career path. The pace is slow, and practical ambition takes a back seat. Some evenings you lose track of time on something that pays nothing and matters enormously. The direction you drift towards now suits a deeper part of you than any job title ever could.",
    "hard": "Career and home life feel muddled while Neptune squares or opposes your MC, often for a year or more. You cannot decide whether to stay in a job or leave, and instructions at work seem vague or contradictory. Someone undermines you quietly, or rumour touches your reputation. At home, a family member needs care in ways that are hard to pin down. You feel tired and uncertain about your direction, and Monday mornings are heavy. You open a half-written application every Sunday evening and never send it. The disillusionment strips away goals that were never yours, and what grows afterwards is a vocation with substance."
  },
  "pluto|moon": {
    "conj": "Pluto sits on your Moon for a year or more, and your emotional life goes through deep renewal. Feelings buried since childhood rise to the surface, often through a parent, a house move or an intense bond. You feel things with unusual force: jealousy, grief, a love that grips. Some relationships end, and others become far closer than before. The intensity is exhausting and hard to explain to anyone who has not felt it. A single song, a smell from your childhood kitchen or an old photograph can undo you for an afternoon. When it finally passes, your emotional core is stronger, freer and much more honest.",
    "soft": "Over a year or more, you find the strength to heal old emotional patterns. Therapy, late night talks or a meaningful family reconciliation help you understand why you react the way you do. Home life transforms for the better: you renovate, move, or make your space your own. Old fears lose their grip, and you bounce back from upsets faster. The work is quiet but powerful, rarely visible from outside. You catch yourself responding calmly to a family remark that once would have ruined your whole weekend. Every change inside you now alters how you care for yourself and others for good.",
    "hard": "Emotional power struggles take centre stage while Pluto squares or opposes your Moon, often for a year or more. A parent, partner or housemate tries to control you, or you catch your own need to control things whenever you feel unsafe. Family secrets surface, a home situation turns intense, or a relationship reaches breaking point. You feel raw and exposed, and old wounds reopen at awkward moments. It is a hard stretch, and it forces you to face what you have avoided for years. You find yourself saying things to family that you have held back for decades, and the room goes very quiet. The emotional freedom waiting on the other side is profound."
  },
  "pluto|mars": {
    "conj": "Pluto sits on your Mars for a year or more, and your drive becomes volcanic. You work with an intensity that astonishes people, training harder, fighting harder and wanting harder. Desire and ambition take on a single-minded edge. Anger runs close to the surface, and you feel it in your chest and fists before you can name it. Power struggles with bosses, rivals or partners are hard to avoid. Sleep grows restless, and you wake at dawn already planning your next move. Channelled, this energy lets you achieve something that once seemed impossible and reclaim power you gave away long ago.",
    "soft": "With Pluto supporting your Mars for a year or more, you have access to deep reserves of stamina and willpower. You tackle a goal that needs sustained effort, whether a physical challenge, building a business or a long overdue confrontation, and you keep going when others would stop. Your presence in a room feels stronger. People who once intimidated you now seem manageable, even small. Focus can tip into obsession, with every evening given over to the project. You say the difficult thing to the person who has pushed you around for years, and your voice does not shake. The change you drive through now goes deep and lasts.",
    "hard": "For a year or more, you run into power struggles wherever you push. A boss, rival or partner blocks you, and conflict escalates quickly from a tense email to a slammed door. You feel anger that frightens you, or you face someone else's rage. Pushing harder only makes the resistance stronger. Your body carries the strain, and rest matters more than usual. You notice how often you clench your jaw or grip the steering wheel when someone cuts in. Through all this you learn how to wield power wisely, and you come out with a far clearer sense of what you will and will not fight for."
  },
  "pluto|asc": {
    "conj": "Pluto crosses your Ascendant over a year or more, and you go through a transformation that others can see. Your appearance changes, sometimes dramatically, and people react to a new intensity in how you carry yourself. You shed an old persona: the people pleaser, the quiet one, the one who never took up space. Relationships reshape around the new you, and some do not survive it. At points it feels like losing yourself before you find yourself. Old friends remark that you seem sharper, more serious, harder to read. What emerges is a more powerful, magnetic and authentic presence.",
    "soft": "A quiet power gathers in how you come across while Pluto supports your Ascendant for a year or more. People take you seriously, fall silent when you speak and respond to your presence without quite knowing why. You feel ready to change your appearance, habits or health in lasting ways, and this time the changes hold. Relationships deepen through honesty rather than charm. The transformation is gradual rather than dramatic, noticed first by old friends. You walk into a room of strangers and feel, for once, entirely at ease in your own skin. The person you become during this time carries a calm strength that stays.",
    "hard": "Pressure from other people forces you to change how you show up while Pluto squares or opposes your Ascendant, often for a year or more. A partner, rival or authority figure challenges you, or someone tries to control how you look, speak or live. You feel exposed and scrutinised, as if every choice is being watched. Your body asks for attention you have been putting off. Old roles no longer work, however hard you try to slip back into them. Intense as it is, the pressure pushes you to stop performing for others, and the self you emerge with is your own."
  },
  "chiron|sun": {
    "conj": "For many months Chiron sits on your Sun, and an old wound around your identity rises to the surface. You feel unsure of your worth, question what you are here to do, or relive an early sense of not being seen. A setback, a loss or a stretch of low energy touches your sense of self. This is also a healing time. Telling your story, finding the right teacher or helping others with similar pain turns the wound into wisdom. You come through more compassionate with yourself and far more able to shine without apology.",
    "soft": "Over many months, healing around your identity comes gently. You find a therapist, mentor or book that helps you understand yourself better, and old insecurities soften. You feel drawn to help others with struggles you know well, and your words land because they come from experience. Creative expression becomes a way to heal, whether writing, singing or speaking up. The process is quiet and easily missed by the people around you. A compliment you would once have brushed off lands, and you let yourself believe it. Your new understanding of yourself brings a lasting self acceptance.",
    "hard": "For many months, old wounds around your worth and identity get pressed. Someone's criticism cuts deeper than it should, or a failure reminds you of childhood hurts you thought were settled. You feel vulnerable and tired of trying to prove yourself. Confidence and recognition feel fragile, and you replay conversations long after they end. The pain is real, and it points directly at what needs healing. A friend's simple kindness brings you close to tears in a way that surprises you. By facing it rather than hiding it, you build a gentler, stronger relationship with who you are."
  },
  "chiron|venus": {
    "conj": "For many months Chiron sits on your Venus, and old hurts in love and self-worth come up to be healed. Patterns become obvious: choosing unavailable people, feeling unlovable, spending to feel better. A relationship triggers an old wound, or an ex reappears with uncanny timing. Alongside the ache you discover a deeper capacity for love and compassion. Beauty, art and honest connection become ways to heal. You find yourself crying at films you would once have mocked, and it feels like thawing. The lessons you learn in love now make your relationships kinder and more honest.",
    "soft": "Over many months, love becomes a source of healing. A partner or friend helps you feel accepted as you are, or beauty and art soothe old pain on a Sunday afternoon. You grow gentler with yourself about money and pleasure, and treats stop carrying guilt. Relationships feel safer, and you risk showing a softer side. The healing is quiet but profound, visible mostly in how you speak to yourself. A photograph of yourself that you once would have deleted now looks lovely to you. Everything that softens in you now opens the door to more nourishing connection.",
    "hard": "For many months, love and self worth feel tender. A partner's offhand words hurt more than intended, or you feel rejected in ways that echo old wounds. Money worries tap into deeper fears of not being enough. Jealousy or insecurity you thought you had outgrown returns, sometimes over a message left unanswered. The pain is uncomfortable, and it is also illuminating. You check your phone more than you would like to admit, waiting for reassurance that does not come. Facing these feelings honestly, you learn to value yourself at a deeper level than approval ever reached."
  },
  "chiron|saturn": {
    "conj": "For many months Chiron sits on your Saturn, and old wounds around authority, failure and responsibility come up. You feel you are never good enough at work, or an older person's criticism echoes something you heard as a child. Limits in your body or career demand respect, and pushing through stops working. This is a healing time too: you learn to set boundaries with compassion, accept imperfection and build routines that support rather than punish you. Rest stops being something you earn and becomes something you allow yourself. Rebuilding now gives you a steadier foundation for the rest of your working life.",
    "soft": "Over many months, your relationship with discipline and authority begins to heal. A patient mentor takes you under their wing, or you find work that turns old struggles into strengths. Responsibilities feel lighter, and you stop apologising for needing time. You forgive yourself for past failures, including the exam, the job or the marriage that did not work out. The healing is slow and undramatic. You catch yourself saying no to an extra task without a flood of guilt afterwards. What it leaves behind is a lasting ease with your own limits and a quieter kind of competence.",
    "hard": "For many months, old fears of failure and inadequacy get pressed. A boss criticises you, a project falls apart, or your body sets limits you cannot ignore. You lie awake running through everything you should have done better. Feeling judged and tired, you are tempted to either overwork or give up. Even a small mistake on an email feels like proof of something bigger, and you spend too long fixing it. The pain is real. It also shows you where you have been too hard on yourself, and learning compassion here builds a stronger, kinder foundation."
  },
  "chiron|northNode": {
    "conj": "For many months Chiron sits on your North Node, and your life direction becomes tied to healing. You feel called towards work, relationships or causes that help others with pain you know well. Old wounds surface as signposts rather than obstacles, pointing at where you are meant to grow. A conversation with a stranger who shares your story leaves you shaken and oddly clear. The process feels vulnerable and deeply meaningful. You notice the same themes appearing in books, films and chance remarks, as if life is underlining them for you. Choices made now align your path with your deepest purpose.",
    "soft": "Over many months, healing experiences nudge you towards your path. A teacher, a support group or a wise friend helps you grow in the direction you have been reaching for. You notice that what once hurt now helps you understand others, and people start seeking you out for exactly that. Small steps towards your future feel supported rather than risky. The shifts are gentle and easy to miss. A painful chapter you rarely mention becomes something you can talk about openly and even with humour. Looking back, you will see that this period turned your pain into purpose.",
    "hard": "For many months, old wounds seem to block your direction. You feel stuck in patterns you thought you had left behind, reaching for the familiar comfort that keeps you small. Other people's needs pull you away from your own growth. Frustration builds when progress stalls just as it seemed within reach. The pain points at what needs healing before you can move forward. You keep being asked for the same kind of help, even when you feel least able to give it. Tending to it, rather than running from it, clears the path you are meant to walk."
  },
  "pluto|pluto": {
    "conj": "A Pluto return takes around 248 years, so no one lives to see it, and for you this line describes the slow, lifelong turning of your own deepest cycle. What you feel instead are the square, the sextile and the trine, each lasting a couple of years. Across them, you face power, control, loss and rebirth in ways that reshape who you are. Old identities fall away when they no longer serve you. You discover strength you did not know you had. A move, a career change or the end of a long relationship often marks these turning points. Each passage leaves you more honest and more fully your own.",
    "soft": "Pluto sextiles its natal place for recent generations somewhere in your twenties, and trines it decades later, each contact lasting a year or two. During these stretches you find the strength to leave an unhealthy situation, commit to therapy, or pursue a goal with unusual determination. Change comes from inner resolve rather than crisis. You feel more in control of your life, and choices made now go deep and last. Friends remark on a new steadiness in you. Money, sexuality and trust all become areas where you quietly take back control. This is transformation you choose rather than transformation that chooses you.",
    "hard": "Pluto squares its natal place somewhere between your mid thirties and about fifty for recent generations, often over two years or more. You feel pressure to confront buried issues around power, control, money, sexuality or mortality, sometimes triggered by a crisis at work or in a relationship. Identities built in your twenties start to crumble so that something truer can emerge. Nights feel longer, and certainty gives way to raw honesty. The stretch demands courage. You find yourself examining where your money goes, who holds power in your relationships and what you are afraid of losing. What reaches the roots now changes you permanently, and for the better."
  },
  "moon|sun": {
    "conj": "The Moon sits right on your Sun today, and for a few hours what you feel and who you are line up so closely that everything shows on your face. You notice your mood colouring small decisions: the lunch you pick, the message you answer first, the tone you take with a colleague. People read you easily, and a friend says word for word what you were thinking before you had the chance. There is a pleasant sense of being at home in yourself, as though the day fits you. Sensitivity runs high too, so a careless remark lands harder than it should and you take it as a verdict on you rather than a passing comment. By evening the feeling eases, leaving a clearer sense of what you want this month.",
    "soft": "Today your feelings and your sense of purpose pull in the same direction, and ordinary jobs go more smoothly than usual. You find the right words for a phone call you had been putting off, and the person on the other end warms to you. Small comforts matter for these few hours: a proper breakfast, a walk at your own pace, a tidy corner of the kitchen. A partner or family member is easy company, and an old tension between you softens without anyone naming it. Nothing dramatic happens, which is part of the gift. What stays with you afterwards is a quiet confidence, the feeling of being yourself without effort, and it carries into the next few days.",
    "hard": "What you need and what you are trying to do stop agreeing with each other for a few hours today. You want to push on with a plan, yet a restless, tired or tearful mood keeps pulling you back, and the gap between the two makes you short with people. A small domestic friction flares: a dish left in the sink, a partner's tone, a parent ringing at the wrong moment. You catch yourself defending your choices more hotly than the situation needs. Underneath, a basic need is asking for room, usually rest, food or reassurance. Once it gets that room, the irritation drops quickly, and by tomorrow the whole episode looks much smaller than it felt at the time."
  },
  "moon|venus": {
    "conj": "Today the Moon crosses your Venus and your heart opens a little wider for a few hours. You want softness: good food, a warm jumper, a song you love on repeat, someone's hand on your shoulder. Affection comes easily, and you send the message saying you miss someone before you can talk yourself out of it. Shop windows pull at you, and a pretty thing on a shelf feels as if it already belongs to you. You look and sound gentler, so people are kinder in return, and a stranger holds a door with a smile. The one snag is a wish to keep everything pleasant, which makes you swallow a small complaint you meant to raise. The glow fades by tonight, but the warmth it leaves is real.",
    "soft": "Your moods and your sense of pleasure work together today, and the easy feeling lasts a few hours. A coffee with a friend runs long because the conversation keeps turning tender and funny. Beauty jumps out at you in ordinary places: late light on a wall, a well-laid table, the smell of rain on warm pavement. Money choices feel intuitive, and you pick the gift or the purchase that is right rather than merely impressive. Someone close shows you affection in a small, practical way, such as making you tea without being asked. Your warmth reaches people without effort, so a recent awkwardness smooths over almost by itself. Tonight you feel looked after, and you look after others in turn.",
    "hard": "Today your need for comfort and your wish for love or pleasure rub against each other for a few hours. You want to be held, yet you also feel oddly touchy, and a partner or friend misreads a small signal and pulls back just when you wanted them closer. Comfort spending tempts you: the takeaway, the extra pudding, the online basket you fill and half regret. A feeling that you give more than you receive rises up, sharpened by tiredness. It is uncomfortable to see how much your mood depends on how others treat you today. Once you say what you want, simply and without sulking, the air clears. The sting has gone by tomorrow, and the affection underneath is still there."
  },
  "moon|saturn": {
    "conj": "Your mood turns sober for a few hours today as the Moon sits on your Saturn. The weight of your responsibilities presses harder than usual: the bills, the unfinished report, the relative who depends on you. Pleasure seems slightly out of reach, and you find yourself tidying, sorting or ticking off a list because that feels safer than resting. A conversation with an older person or a manager lands heavily, even though the words were mild. You also have unusual stamina for dull work, and you clear something that has hung over you for weeks. The loneliness of this mood lifts by evening, leaving a solid, grounded feeling and a few proper jobs done.",
    "soft": "Today your feelings settle into a steady, practical groove for a few hours. You are calm enough to face paperwork, a tight budget or a family arrangement without getting rattled. People lean on you, and you quietly like being the one who holds things together for an afternoon. An older relative or senior colleague offers sensible advice, and you take it without bristling. Your need for fuss or reassurance drops, and simple routines comfort you: cooking a proper meal, folding the laundry, getting to bed on time. Serious conversations go well in this calm. By evening you feel sturdier, as if a small foundation has been laid under the rest of the week.",
    "hard": "Low, flat and held back: that is the flavour of a few hours today while the Moon presses on your Saturn. Duty and need clash: you want comfort, yet the day keeps handing you chores, criticism or someone else's demands. A remark from a parent, partner or manager sounds colder than it was meant, and you replay it on the way home. You are tempted to conclude that nobody supports you, which is the mood talking rather than the facts. Small practical wins make a difference, such as finishing one task, eating properly or getting to sleep early. The heaviness passes within the day, and what remains is a clearer view of which obligations are yours to carry."
  },
  "moon|pluto": {
    "conj": "Today the Moon passes over your Pluto and your feelings run deep and strong for a few hours. A small trigger, a look, a slow reply, a scene in a film, stirs something far older than the moment. Suspicion or possessiveness rises, and you want to know exactly where you stand with someone. Intimate conversations go further than usual, and you hear a truth you did not expect, or say one. There is power in this mood: you see through pretence instantly and feel ready to cut away something that no longer belongs in your life. The intensity drains by tonight, but the insight about what you feel stays with you for days.",
    "soft": "Your emotions have depth without drama for a few hours today. You sense what is going on beneath the surface of a conversation, and you say the one thing that helps someone open up. Clearing out feels satisfying: a drawer of old letters, a lingering grudge, an app you check out of pure habit. You feel resilient, able to face a hard topic about money, family or closeness without flinching. Someone trusts you with a confidence and you hold it well. There is a quiet strength in you that others lean on. By evening you feel emotionally lighter, as though a small piece of old weight has been let go.",
    "hard": "Today, for a few hours, the Moon clashes with your Pluto and a small incident brings up a big feeling. A partner's offhand comment, a relative taking over a plan, or a jealous twinge at a friend's good news hits a nerve you forgot you had. Part of you wants to take charge of everything, and part of you wants to withdraw and give nobody anything. Power games show up in tiny forms: who texts first, who chooses the restaurant, who apologises. You see your own reactions in sharp focus, including the parts you would rather not see. When the intensity drains, which it does by tomorrow, you understand something honest about what you fear losing."
  },
  "moon|asc": {
    "conj": "Today the Moon crosses your Ascendant and your feelings show on the outside for a few hours. People notice your mood before you mention it, and a stranger in a queue starts a friendly chat. You are more sensitive to your surroundings: noise, crowds and harsh lighting wear on you, while a quiet café restores you quickly. Your body wants care, whether that is a long bath, a nap or your softest clothes. You come across as approachable and open, which draws people close and makes small talk easy. The flip side is feeling exposed, so a comment about how you look lands deeper than usual. That raw, visible feeling fades by evening, and you feel more like yourself again.",
    "soft": "Warmth is what people meet in you for a few hours today, and you are easy to be around. Small encounters go well: the neighbour stops to chat, the shop assistant goes out of their way, a colleague asks how you really are and waits for the answer. You feel comfortable in your own skin, and you reach for clothes that suit your mood perfectly. First impressions work in your favour, because your warmth reads as genuine rather than polished. You pick up on how others feel and adjust gently without losing yourself. Even a short errand turns into a pleasant exchange. By evening you feel more connected to the people around you than you did this morning.",
    "hard": "Today, for a few hours, your inner mood and the face you show the world pull apart. You feel one thing and are expected to look another, smiling in a meeting while something at home bothers you, or staying cheerful when you are worn out. A partner or relative reacts to how you come across rather than to what you meant, and a small disagreement about plans or space flares up. You feel self-conscious and more affected by your surroundings than usual, bothered by clutter, noise or a cramped seat. Once you stop pretending the mood is not there, people meet you more kindly. The day settles by evening and the friction is quickly forgotten."
  },
  "sun|moon": {
    "conj": "Your private feelings come into the light as the Sun shines on your natal Moon over the next couple of days. What you need, at home, in your closest relationships and in your body, becomes plain to you. A family matter or domestic decision moves forward, and you find yourself clearing a cupboard, rearranging a room or phoning a parent you have not spoken to in a while. Emotions sit close to the surface, but in a clarifying way rather than an overwhelming one. The people who matter to you notice your needs and respond. Pretending to be fine becomes almost impossible now, which is uncomfortable for a moment and a relief after. These days leave you feeling more at home, inside and out.",
    "soft": "These couple of days bring an easy agreement between your will and your feelings. You know what you want and it sits comfortably with what you need, so decisions about home, family or your daily rhythm come without inner argument. Relationships feel supportive: a partner shows up for you, a parent is easy company, a friend turns up to help with a chore. You are generous with your care and people answer warmly. Cooking for others, hosting a small evening or finishing a home project you have planned all feel natural. Sleep improves and your appetite steadies. You come through the stretch nourished and more balanced than before.",
    "hard": "Over the next couple of days what you want to do clashes with what you need, as the Sun presses on your natal Moon. Work or ambition pulls you out while home, family or plain tiredness pulls you back, and you feel guilty whichever way you turn. A partner or relative wants more of your time on the very evening you have other plans. Old emotional habits flare: the urge to please everyone, or the urge to withdraw and sulk. Sleep and appetite are a little off. This friction shows you plainly where your life has tipped out of balance. When the Sun moves on, you know which need you have been ignoring and why it matters."
  },
  "sun|mars": {
    "conj": "Energy runs high today and tomorrow while the Sun lights up your Mars. You want to get moving: start the project, go for the run, send the bold email, say what you have been holding back. Confidence is strong and people notice your drive, some admiring it and some stepping out of your way. Physical effort helps, and you get more done in one afternoon than you managed all last week. Your temper is shorter than usual, so a slow driver or a queue at the till irritates you out of all proportion. There is desire in the air as well, a sharper appetite for whatever or whoever you want. Used well, these days give you a strong push towards something that matters to you.",
    "soft": "Right now, and for a couple of days, you get a clean, confident surge of energy. Action and intention match, so you start something and actually finish it. A workout feels good, a competitive moment goes your way, and you speak up at work without overthinking it. People respond well to your directness because it comes across as enthusiasm rather than aggression. Fixing the broken shelf, making the call you keep postponing or pushing a stalled plan forward all happen almost by themselves. Your body feels strong and willing. You come through braver than you went in, and that courage carries you through the rest of the week.",
    "hard": "Friction is in the air for a couple of days while the Sun pushes against your Mars. You feel impatient, restless and quick to snap, and other people seem to be standing deliberately in your way. A disagreement with a colleague, sibling or partner flares over something small, like who does what or who gets the final say. You want to prove a point, and you drive, walk or work faster than you should, so bumps, burns and small cuts are more likely. The energy itself is valuable, because it shows you what you are angry about. Poured into effort rather than argument, it clears a surprising amount of work before the week is out."
  },
  "sun|uranus": {
    "conj": "Restless, wide awake and hungry for something different: that is you for a couple of days while the Sun sits on your Uranus. Routines bore you, and you change your hair, move the furniture or say yes to an unusual invitation. Surprises arrive: a message from someone unexpected, a sudden change of plan, a flash of insight about the shape of your life. You feel strongly that you want to be yourself rather than what others expect. Some people find your independence exciting and others find it unsettling. Impulses run fast, so resigning, booking or buying on a whim is tempting. These days show you where you need more freedom.",
    "soft": "A pleasant spark of originality lights up the next couple of days. A fresh solution to a stuck problem comes to you in the shower or on a walk, and colleagues or friends are open to trying it. Small, welcome surprises turn up: a cancelled meeting frees your afternoon, a new contact offers something interesting, a spontaneous plan becomes the best part of the week. You feel free to be a little unconventional, whether that means a new outfit, a different route home or an app you have ignored for months. Change feels exciting rather than threatening. More seems possible now than you had allowed yourself to believe.",
    "hard": "Life feels jumpy while the Sun clashes with your Uranus, and the mood holds for a couple of days. Plans fall through at short notice, people behave unpredictably, and you feel an urge to break away from whatever is holding you in place. Rules, managers or partners who seem to limit you get the sharp end of your tongue, and a small rebellion is tempting. Technology misbehaves, trains are cancelled and schedules get scrambled. Your nerves hum, and sleep is lighter than usual. Underneath the disruption is a pointed message about where you feel trapped. Things settle once the Sun moves on, yet the knowledge of what needs to change stays with you."
  },
  "sun|chiron": {
    "conj": "An old sore spot comes into view today, with the Sun sitting on your Chiron for the next couple of days. A remark, a memory or a situation touches the place where you have always felt not quite enough, whether about your body, your mind, your family or your sense of belonging. You feel tender and more exposed than usual, and a small slight stings for hours. At the same time you have a capacity to help others now, and someone opens up to you because they sense you understand. Being honest about your own hurt, even briefly and to one person, brings relief. These days leave you gentler with yourself and with the people you meet.",
    "soft": "Today and tomorrow bring a quiet chance to heal a little. You feel more accepting of the part of yourself you usually hide or criticise, and you talk about it more openly than usual, often over a late coffee with someone you trust. A conversation with a friend, therapist or mentor goes deep and leaves you lighter. You are good at supporting others now, and your own experience of struggle becomes useful to someone else. Small acts of self-care, like keeping an appointment or letting someone help you carry something, feel easier. By the end you can see how far you have already come.",
    "hard": "Something touches an old wound over the next couple of days, as the Sun presses on your Chiron. You feel criticised, overlooked or left out, even if the actual slight is small, like being forgotten in a group chat or talked over in a meeting. Your reaction surprises you with its strength. You want to defend yourself hard, or to hide away and nurse the hurt. Someone else's pain becomes visible too, and you are pulled into helping even while you are sore. These days are uncomfortable, but they show where you still need care. Once they pass, you carry a little more understanding of your own sensitivity."
  },
  "sun|mc": {
    "conj": "Your working life steps into the spotlight for a couple of days as the Sun crosses your Midheaven. You are noticed: someone senior asks your opinion, your name comes up in a meeting, or a piece of your work gets praised in front of others. Ambition sharpens, and you picture more precisely what you want your career to look like in a few years. Putting yourself forward feels natural, whether that means sending the application, raising your hand or sharing your work publicly. Greater visibility means mistakes are seen too, and you feel that pressure. You come out of these days with a stronger sense of your direction and of the reputation you are building.",
    "soft": "The next couple of days put a gentle wind behind your career. Work tasks flow, and people in authority are supportive or at least easy to deal with. A small piece of recognition arrives: a thank you from a client, a good review, a colleague mentioning your contribution in a meeting you missed. You feel confident about your professional direction and happy to share your ideas. Interviews, pitches and meetings with someone who can help your plans go well. Even the commute feels lighter. There is a growing sense that your efforts are being seen and that your path is heading somewhere good.",
    "hard": "Work and personal life compete for you as the Sun pushes against your Midheaven through tomorrow. A boss wants more at the moment home needs you, or private feelings make it hard to perform in public. You feel judged, and a comment about your results or your choices hits harder than it should. A disagreement with an authority figure is likely, and the urge to prove yourself runs strong. Late nights at the desk or a missed family dinner become points of tension. These days highlight where your career and your inner life are out of step. Afterwards you know what kind of recognition you want."
  },
  "mercury|mercury": {
    "conj": "Mercury returns to its own place in your chart this week, and for a few days your mind feels unusually sharp and busy. Ideas arrive in quick bursts, and you jot notes in your phone at odd moments, in the shower or halfway through dinner. Conversations flow, and you say plainly something you have struggled to put into words for months. Emails, forms and bookings get sorted, and an errand across town goes smoothly. You also notice how you habitually think and talk, the phrases you repeat and the worries you rehearse. Mental overload is real, with too many tabs open and sleep a little restless. Your head feels clearer once it passes, and a fresh line of thought has begun.",
    "soft": "Your thinking has an easy, lively rhythm this week. You find the words fast in a meeting, write a message that lands exactly right, and a friend laughs properly at your joke. Paperwork that normally drags gets done in an afternoon. Curiosity is high: you read an article to the end, pick up a podcast, or ask a neighbour a question that turns into a proper conversation. Short trips and errands go smoothly, and a missing item turns up in the last place you look. Siblings or old classmates are easy company. For these few days learning and explaining feel effortless, and you pick up a skill or a fact that proves useful later.",
    "hard": "Your mind feels crowded and scattered this week while Mercury clashes with its own place in your chart. You say something clumsily and spend the evening rewording it in your head. Messages cross, a delivery goes astray, and a chat with a sibling, colleague or neighbour turns into an argument about the facts. Small decisions become agonising, and you switch between options until you are sick of both. Nervous energy makes it hard to settle to one task or to fall asleep. The friction is useful, because it shows where your way of thinking has become stuck. The noise quietens as Mercury moves on, and a clearer view arrives."
  },
  "mercury|jupiter": {
    "conj": "Your mind expands this week as Mercury sits on your Jupiter. You think big, talk with enthusiasm and see possibilities everywhere: a course to take, a trip to plan, a business idea that starts to look doable. Conversations are generous and encouraging, and someone hands you useful advice or a promising lead. You are persuasive now, so a pitch, a proposal or a request for help lands well. Overpromising is the catch, agreeing to three things when you have time for one, or skimming the small print on a contract. Used well, these days leave you with a hopeful plan and a wider view of what you can do.",
    "soft": "This week good news and good ideas arrive with ease. A message brings an opportunity, a teacher or mentor says something that sticks, or a book opens a door in your thinking. You explain yourself patiently and generously, and people respond with warmth. Planning travel, study or a larger project feels natural, and the details fall into place faster than expected. Your optimism is well founded for these few days, built on concrete openings rather than wishful thinking. Conversations with people from other backgrounds or countries are rewarding. A bigger picture opens up, along with a little more faith in your own judgement.",
    "hard": "Mercury clashes with your Jupiter this week, and your mind races ahead of the facts. You make grand plans, promise too much, or talk so confidently that an important detail slips past you. A disagreement about beliefs, politics or principles flares at dinner or online, and everyone is certain they are right. Enthusiasm tempts you to overcommit, signing up for a course, a trip or a side project in a single excited evening. Big ideas are not the problem; the gap between the vision and the practical steps is. As the week closes, you see which plans are worth pursuing, and a few of them hold up well."
  },
  "mercury|neptune": {
    "conj": "Thinking goes soft at the edges this week while Mercury sits on your Neptune. You daydream through meetings, lose your keys twice and send a message to the wrong person. At the same time your imagination is wonderfully alive: you write, draw, play music or come up with an idea that feels as if it arrived from somewhere beyond you. You hear what people mean rather than what they say, and your intuition is sharp. Confusion is the price, so a vague promise sounds solid and an arrangement gets muddled. A booking detail or a time slips through the cracks. These days are rich for creative and spiritual thinking and poor for contracts.",
    "soft": "Imagination and intuition work together gently for the next few days. You read between the lines easily, sensing that a friend is upset before they say so, and you find exactly the right kind words. Creative work flows: a piece of writing, a playlist, a photograph or a sketch comes together more beautifully than you planned. Music, films and quiet moments near water move you more than usual. You speak with compassion, and a tense conversation softens because of the way you frame things. Dreams are vivid and sometimes surprisingly helpful. For these few days your mind is a softer, more inspired place to live.",
    "hard": "Clarity is hard to come by this week, with Mercury clashing against your Neptune. Plans are vague, messages are misread, and someone tells you a half-truth, or you tell yourself one. You feel foggy and distracted, drifting through tasks and forgetting why you walked into the room. A misunderstanding with a friend or colleague grows because neither of you says plainly what you mean. You are more suggestible now, open to flattery, a poor deal or a persuasive story. The fog carries a message of its own: something in your life is not as clear as you have been telling yourself. Next week the details come back into focus."
  },
  "mercury|northNode": {
    "conj": "The conversations you have this week point you towards your future, because Mercury is sitting on your North Node. You meet someone, read something or overhear a remark that clarifies where your life wants to go. Ideas about a new direction come thick and fast, and you talk about them more openly than usual, surprising even yourself. A class, a message or a chance meeting on the bus feels oddly significant. Old habits of thinking pull you back into familiar grooves, and you notice the pull sooner than before. You come away with a plan that stretches you and the words to say out loud what you want next.",
    "soft": "Your thoughts and words support the direction your life is heading this week. A conversation with a new contact opens a door, or an email arrives with an invitation that fits your growth perfectly. You learn quickly from people who are ahead of you on a path you want to walk. Writing your plans down or sharing them with a friend makes them feel real and achievable. Small signs and coincidences cluster, a name that keeps coming up, a book recommended twice, and you pay attention. Your next step sharpens, and so does your confidence in the choices you are making.",
    "hard": "Pulled between the familiar and the new, you spend the next few days with Mercury clashing against your North Node. Old conversations and habits of thinking resurface, and you catch yourself repeating the same complaints or the same safe opinions at the same kitchen table. Someone's advice points you backwards, or you hear news that makes you doubt your direction. You feel restless and mentally torn, rehearsing both sides of a choice late into the night. The friction is a sign that your usual way of thinking no longer fits where you are going. Before the week is done, a clearer thought emerges about what to let go of."
  },
  "venus|sun": {
    "conj": "Attractive, sociable and easy in yourself: that is how Venus on your Sun leaves you for a few days. People are drawn to you, compliments arrive, and invitations fill your calendar. You want pleasure and beauty: a new outfit, a long lunch, a day out with someone you like. Your love life gets a lift, and a partner or crush responds warmly to the smallest gesture. Creative work flows and you feel generous with your time and money. Because you want everything to stay nice, a necessary conversation gets postponed and the card gets used a little too freely. These days remind you how good it feels to enjoy being yourself.",
    "soft": "This week a gentle warmth surrounds you. Social life is easy, conversations are friendly and you feel more at home in your own skin. Someone pays you a compliment, you hit it off with a new person, or an old friend gets in touch out of the blue. You are in the mood for pleasure and comfort, and you give yourself a treat without guilt. Relationships feel harmonious, and small gestures of affection mean a lot, a note, a shared playlist, a hug at the door. These are lovely days for dating, making something, decorating or spending time with people you like. You feel appreciated and more confident in your own charm.",
    "hard": "What you want in love or pleasure rubs against who you are over the next few days, as Venus clashes with your Sun. You feel pulled between pleasing others and pleasing yourself, and resentment rises when you give in too easily. A partner, friend or date wants something different, and a small disagreement about plans, money or attention flares. Overindulgence tempts you: the extra glass, the second dessert, the jacket you did not need. Underneath sits a question of values, what you are willing to trade for approval. The tension eases as Venus moves on, and you know more about what you want."
  },
  "venus|venus": {
    "conj": "Venus comes back to its own place in your chart this week, and your year of love and pleasure gets a fresh start. You feel more attractive and more in tune with what you like: the clothes, the music, the people, the kind of evening that makes you happy. A new attraction begins, or an existing relationship feels renewed, as if you are seeing your partner with fresh eyes. You are drawn to spend on beauty and comfort, and some of it is money well spent. Old patterns in love show up too, the way you chase, cling or hold back. These few days set the tone for the next twelve months of your affections and pleasures.",
    "soft": "Your taste and your sense of pleasure are in lovely form for a few days. You choose the right gift, the right outfit or the right restaurant, and people enjoy your company. Relationships feel easy: a partner is affectionate, a friend is fun, a date goes well and ends later than planned. Money flows a little more smoothly, and a small purchase or payment turns out well. Art, music and small luxuries delight you, and you let yourself enjoy them without apology. The sweetness of these few days reminds you of the good things already in your life.",
    "hard": "Your desires feel out of step this week as Venus clashes with its own place in your chart. What you want and what you have do not match, and a low hum of dissatisfaction runs through love, money or pleasure. A partner or friend disappoints you, or you disappoint yourself by overspending on something that does not make you happy after all. Scrolling through other people's lives leaves you feeling you are missing out. Underneath is a signal that your tastes and values have shifted and your life has not caught up yet. By the end of the week you can name what brings you pleasure."
  },
  "venus|saturn": {
    "conj": "Love and pleasure turn serious this week while Venus sits on your Saturn. You take stock of your relationships, noticing which ones are solid and which feel like hard work. A partner's coolness or a friend's distance stings, and you feel lonely even at a crowded table. Money feels tight, so you count the cost of every outing and skip the treat. There is commitment available too: a promise made now tends to last, and a sober talk about the future of a relationship brings clarity rather than drama. Loyalty matters more than fun for these few days. You come out knowing which bonds deserve your time and which you have been keeping out of duty.",
    "soft": "Steady, grounded affection marks the next few days. You appreciate the people who have stood by you, and you show it in practical ways: helping with a move, remembering an anniversary, paying for dinner without fuss. Relationships with older people or colleagues are warm and supportive. Money decisions are sensible, and you buy something built to last rather than something that dazzles for a day. Simple, quality pleasures suit you better than flashy ones. A serious talk with a partner or a long-term plan for your savings goes smoothly. Security settles in, the kind that comes from knowing who and what you can rely on.",
    "hard": "Love and money feel restricted while Venus clashes with your Saturn over the coming days. You feel unappreciated, as though you give more than you get, and a partner or friend seems cold or critical. Plans for pleasure are cancelled by work or duty, and you spend Saturday on chores instead of the outing you wanted. A bill or expense arrives at the worst moment. You are tempted to withdraw and decide nobody cares, which only deepens the loneliness. This friction shows you where you have been settling for less than you need. What has to change becomes obvious before Venus moves on."
  },
  "venus|pluto": {
    "conj": "Desire runs deep this week, with Venus sitting on your Pluto. Attraction is intense, and you feel magnetic, drawn to someone or something with unusual force. Jealousy, possessiveness or a fear of losing someone rise up and surprise you with their heat. Money and shared resources become a live topic, and a talk about who pays for what goes deeper than expected. A strong urge to transform takes hold: to change your look, clear out old clutter or end something that has run its course. You feel your own power in love now. These days bring intimacy and an honest reckoning with what you want.",
    "soft": "This week your capacity for deep connection is strong. A conversation with a partner or close friend goes past small talk into something real, and you feel closer afterwards, sometimes after years of circling the subject. You are drawn to people and experiences with depth, and anything shallow bores you. Money matters, especially shared ones, sort themselves out through honest discussion. You feel attractive in a quiet, powerful way, and people respond to it. Healing a strained relationship or releasing an old resentment comes more easily than it has in a long time. Your affections feel renewed, stripped back to what is true.",
    "hard": "Love feels charged with power struggles for a few days while Venus clashes with your Pluto. Jealousy, control or emotional games show up, either in you or in someone close. A partner withholds affection, or you do, and a small disagreement turns into a battle of wills over who gives in first. Shared money becomes a battleground, and a talk about the joint account turns tense. You find yourself fixated on a person or a desire, checking their profile or replaying a conversation. The intensity reveals what you most fear losing. By the time Venus moves on, you understand what needs to transform in the way you love."
  },
  "venus|asc": {
    "conj": "You look and feel your best this week as Venus crosses your Ascendant. People notice you, compliments come more often, and you feel at ease in your body. You want to dress up, try a new haircut or buy something beautiful to wear, and the mirror is kinder than usual. First impressions go well, so dates, interviews and introductions are favoured. You come across as warm, charming and approachable, and people want to sit next to you. Vanity is the small trap, too long choosing an outfit or too much spent on appearance. These days are made for socialising and letting yourself be admired.",
    "soft": "This week you come across with an easy grace. Small social moments go well: a barista remembers your order, a new acquaintance laughs at your story, a colleague compliments your jacket. You feel comfortable in your body and relaxed about how you look, which makes you more attractive to others. Dates, parties and meetings flow, and you smooth over awkward moments with a smile. It is a good few days for a photograph, a fresh style or turning up and letting people enjoy your company. Everyday interactions feel warmer, and that warmth follows you home.",
    "hard": "How you look and how you want to be loved feel at odds for a few days while Venus clashes with your Ascendant. You feel self-conscious, fussing over an outfit or a photo, and a partner or friend's comment about your appearance lands badly. Someone close wants more attention than you have to give, or you feel invisible next to a more polished person in the room. Spending on your looks tempts you, often in a way that does not bring the satisfaction you expected. A small relationship tension flares over plans or presentation. Venus moves on quickly, and with it goes this touchiness about how you come across."
  },
  "mars|moon": {
    "conj": "Your feelings run hot for a few days to a week while Mars sits on your natal Moon. Small things at home set you off: a messy kitchen, a noisy neighbour, a family member who will not listen. You feel protective and fierce about the people and places you love, ready to defend them against anything. Energy for domestic jobs is high, and you tackle the garden, repaint a wall or clear out a room in one furious burst. Your temper is closer to the surface, and tears and anger mix more easily than usual. Sleep is restless and your stomach reacts to stress. Once the heat passes, you know what at home needs to change.",
    "soft": "Your emotions give you energy rather than draining it this week. You act on what you feel, and it works: you sort out a family arrangement, stand up for a friend or make a bold change to your living space. Home projects move forward quickly, and you have the drive to finish them. Your instincts are sharp, and you know when to push and when to hold back. A partner or relative appreciates your decisiveness. You feel emotionally brave, willing to say what you need without apology. A small but lasting improvement to your home or daily life is in place before Mars moves on.",
    "hard": "Emotions boil over at home this week as Mars clashes with your natal Moon. Irritation builds fast, and a small disagreement about chores, money or plans turns into a proper row. You feel defensive and quick to take offence, and people close to you seem to push every button. Old family tensions resurface, often over a phone call with a parent or sibling. Your body carries the tension too, in a tight jaw, a restless night or a churning stomach. This friction exposes needs you have been ignoring. What remains afterwards is a clearer sense of what makes you feel unsafe and what you need in order to feel settled."
  },
  "mars|mars": {
    "conj": "Mars returns to its own place in your chart this week, and your drive gets a fresh start that lasts a few days before settling into the months ahead. You wake up restless and keen to begin something: a training plan, a job hunt, a campaign for what you want at home or at work. Energy surges, and you get through physical work or long hours with surprising stamina. Patience runs thin with anyone who wastes your time, and you say so more bluntly than usual. Desire is strong too, in love as much as in ambition. A new two-year cycle of action begins here, so whatever you start now carries momentum.",
    "soft": "Energy flows cleanly and confidently for a few days to a week. You start things and finish them, and a project that has sat stalled for weeks finally moves. Exercise feels great, whether you set a personal best or enjoy a long walk in the cold air more than usual. You speak up for yourself without heat, and people respect your directness. Competitive situations go your way, at work, in sport or in a negotiation over a price. Desire and action line up, so you go after what you want with focus instead of frustration. You end this stretch capable, fit and more in charge of your own direction.",
    "hard": "Your drive meets resistance all week while Mars clashes with its own place in your chart. Plans stall, people block you, and frustration builds until you want to slam a cupboard door. You are more combative than usual, picking arguments or rising to bait you would normally ignore, especially in traffic or in a group chat. Rushing brings bumps, strains and small burns. Underneath is a test of how you use your energy: pushing harder at the wrong door, or finding a smarter route round. The anger itself is information about what you want and cannot yet have. Once the pressure lifts, you know where your effort was wasted and where it counts."
  },
  "mars|uranus": {
    "conj": "You feel electric for a few days to a week while Mars sits on your Uranus. Sudden urges hit: quit, move, book a flight, say the thing you have held back for years. Surprises arrive, some welcome and some jarring, and your plans get scrambled. Your patience is thin, and restrictions of any kind feel unbearable. You are brave, original and ready to take risks, which helps you break out of a rut. Accidents and rash decisions are more likely when you rush, so the kitchen knife and the motorway both demand care. This energy shows you where you have been holding yourself back too long.",
    "soft": "Your drive is inventive and quick for the next few days. You find a clever, unexpected way through a problem that has stumped everyone, and people are impressed by your originality. Changes you make now turn out well: a new morning routine, a different approach to a stubborn client, a spontaneous day trip decided over breakfast. You feel free and bold, willing to try what you normally would not. New tools and gadgets work in your favour, and a piece of software clicks into place. Other people respond to your independence and even join in. A small, stale pattern breaks, and you feel lighter for it.",
    "hard": "Mars clashes with your Uranus for the next week or so, and life feels unpredictable and tense. Plans are disrupted, people behave erratically, and you feel an explosive urge to break free. Arguments flare suddenly, and you say something sharp before you think it through. Accidents and mishaps are more likely with machines, cars or anything electrical. Your nerves are on edge, and sleep suffers. Underneath the chaos is a need for more freedom and less restriction. Once Mars moves on, you see where your life has become too tight and what you want to change."
  },
  "mars|chiron": {
    "conj": "An old wound flares into action while Mars sits on your Chiron for the next few days. A remark about your work, your body or your family triggers a familiar hurt, and you snap or go cold before you understand why. You feel driven to fight for yourself, or for someone else who has been hurt in the same way, and you speak up in a meeting or a family argument with unexpected force. An old injury or sore spot in your body grumbles. There is courage here as well: you face something painful head on rather than avoiding it. By the time Mars moves on, you have taken a small but solid step towards healing.",
    "soft": "Courage to deal with an old hurt arrives this week. You take practical action on something that has long held you back: booking the appointment, having the honest conversation, going back to the exercise class you abandoned. Anger turns into useful energy on behalf of yourself or someone else, and you stand up for a friend who is being treated unfairly. You are good at helping others fight their battles, because you know that fight from the inside. Physical recovery goes well, and a stubborn ache eases. You feel stronger in exactly the place you once felt weakest.",
    "hard": "Something rubs on an old wound this week, with Mars clashing against your Chiron. You feel attacked, humiliated or dismissed, and your reaction is far bigger than the moment. A critical email, a rejection or a competitive colleague reopens a familiar sense of not being good enough. You want to lash out, or to retreat completely and refuse to try again. An old injury or weak spot in your body tightens up. The friction is painful, but it shows where you still carry hurt. Afterwards you understand your triggers better and hold them more gently."
  },
  "mars|mc": {
    "conj": "Career ambition fires up for a few days to a week as Mars crosses your Midheaven. You want to push forward at work, take charge of a project or go after the promotion you have been circling. Energy for professional goals runs high, and you clear a backlog that has sat on your desk for a month. You are more visible and more assertive, which impresses some people and irritates others. A clash with a boss or rival flares if you push too hard or too publicly. Used well, this stretch lets you make steady progress towards something that matters for your reputation, and people remember that you acted.",
    "soft": "Your drive and your career goals line up well for the next week or so. You take decisive action at work and it pays off: a pitch lands, a deadline is met early, a bold idea gets the green light. People in authority notice your energy and back you, sometimes with more responsibility. You feel competitive in a healthy way, enjoying the chase rather than fearing it. Launching something, applying for a role or leading a team through a tough week all come naturally. Even a difficult client meeting turns in your favour. Visible progress on your professional path is what this stretch leaves behind.",
    "hard": "Work becomes a battleground this week as Mars clashes with your Midheaven. You clash with a boss, a colleague or a rival, and a dispute about who is in charge flares in a meeting or over email. Home and career pull against each other, and you feel you cannot give enough to either. Frustration builds when your efforts are blocked or taken for granted. You are tempted to quit on the spot or make a rash move you have not thought through. The tension shows where your ambitions and your circumstances are out of step. When Mars moves on, you know what you want to change about your working life."
  },
  "moon|moon": {
    "conj": "For a few hours today the Moon returns to where it sat when you were born, and your feelings come right up to the surface. You notice exactly what you need, whether that is a proper meal, your own bed or a voice on the phone that knows you. Small things land harder than usual: a curt message from a friend or a song in a shop can bring a lump to your throat. You want to be home, or somewhere that feels like it, and crowded plans look like hard work. This is a monthly reset rather than a crisis, so the heaviness passes by evening. What it gives you is an honest reading of your emotional fuel gauge, and permission to top it up before the month runs on.",
    "soft": "Your mood and your circumstances fall into step today, and for a few hours you feel more like yourself than you have all week. Comfort comes easily: the kettle, a familiar route home, a chat with someone who does not need things explained. You are quick to read the room and quicker to soothe it, so people drift towards you when they are rattled. It is a good few hours for cooking something from memory, sorting the house or replying to your mother's message. The ease is quiet, and you can overlook it because nothing dramatic happens. These gentle hours refill you in a way that carries you through the busier days that follow.",
    "hard": "Today your feelings pull against what the day is asking of you. You want to curl up at home while the diary insists on meetings, errands or someone else's crisis. Little irritations take on more weight than they deserve: the partner who forgets the milk, the colleague who talks over you. You notice an old habit of mood flaring, snapping first and feeling sorry later, or going silent and waiting to be noticed. The friction is real but short, lasting a few hours, and it is mostly about needs you have been ignoring for weeks. By tonight you know precisely what you have been going without, and that knowledge is useful long after the mood lifts."
  },
  "moon|mars": {
    "conj": "The Moon lands on your Mars today and turns feelings straight into action for a few hours. You are quick, warm and a little hot under the collar, ready to fix the leaking tap, clear the inbox or tell someone exactly what you think. Patience runs thin in queues and in family group chats. Desire comes up fast too, for food, for touch, for a win. The heat makes you brave, and you find yourself saying the thing you have been swallowing for days. It also sharpens your tongue beyond what you intend, so a sentence can land like a slammed door. By evening the charge has burnt off, and whatever you started while it lasted is usually worth finishing.",
    "soft": "For a few hours today your energy and your mood pull in the same direction, and getting things done feels almost pleasurable. You tackle the job you have been avoiding, go for the longer run, or ring the landlord, and it goes better than expected. Feeling protective of the people close to you comes out as practical help rather than worry. Your temper is there but well handled, giving you a firm voice without the edge. It is a good window for a frank talk at home, because you can be direct and kind at once. What opens up is a small sense of momentum that makes the rest of the week feel easier to push through.",
    "hard": "Tired and restless at once, you spend a few hours today with your feelings and your drive grinding against each other. You want to act, yet everything that slows you down irritates you. A partner's tone, a child who will not put their shoes on, a driver who cuts in: any of it can set you off. Anger arrives before you have worked out what hurt, so you slam a cupboard rather than say you feel unsupported. Home is where the friction shows most, because that is where you let your guard down. The sting fades quickly, and underneath it sits a clear signal about which of your needs has been running on empty."
  },
  "moon|uranus": {
    "conj": "The Moon crosses your Uranus today, and for a few hours your mood turns electric and unpredictable. You wake up wanting something different: a new route to work, a spontaneous plan, a haircut you did not book. Routines that normally comfort you feel suffocating, and you jump at any excuse to break them. Plans change at short notice, a friend cancels or an unexpected call rearranges your evening. You are more detached than usual, needing space even from people you love, and they notice. The restlessness is honest, though, and shows you where life has become too tidy. By tonight the jolt has passed, leaving a lively sense that you are allowed to surprise yourself.",
    "soft": "A pleasant jolt of freshness runs through your mood today, lasting a few hours. You are open to doing things differently, and small changes feel exciting rather than unsettling. An unexpected message, a chance meeting in the shop or a last-minute invitation brightens the day. You find yourself rearranging the furniture, trying a recipe you have never cooked or taking the long way home just because. Friends find you easier company, lighter and more curious than usual. Nothing here asks for a big decision, which is part of the charm. It is a reminder that your emotional life has more room in it than your routines suggest.",
    "hard": "Your need for security collides with a sudden urge to break free for a few hours today. Plans fall through, someone changes the arrangement at the last minute, or you are the one who suddenly cannot face the thing you agreed to. Your nerves feel jangled, and small disruptions, a late train, a noisy neighbour, make you disproportionately jumpy. You swing between wanting to be held and wanting everyone to leave you alone. People close to you get mixed signals and struggle to keep up. The unease passes by nightfall, and it points straight at a part of your home life that has grown too rigid to breathe."
  },
  "moon|chiron": {
    "conj": "Today the Moon touches your Chiron, and for a few hours an old tenderness sits close to the surface. A throwaway remark, a photo from years ago or a scene on television can open a feeling you thought you had filed away. You find yourself remembering what it felt like to be left out, overlooked or not quite enough. The instinct is to hide it behind being busy or helpful. Yet you are also unusually gentle today, and someone else's hurt meets you with understanding. A quiet conversation with a friend who gets it does more good than any distraction. By evening the ache has softened, and you carry a little more compassion for your younger self.",
    "soft": "Your feelings and your old wound sit side by side without a fight for a few hours today. You can talk about something that once hurt, and your voice stays steady. People seem to bring you their troubles, and you know what to say because you have been there. A small act of care, a message to someone struggling or a cup of tea made without being asked, lands deeply. Kindness towards yourself comes a little easier too: fewer harsh inner remarks, more patience with your mistakes. It is a quiet day rather than a dramatic one, and it opens a sense that your sore places have also made you wise.",
    "hard": "You feel thin-skinned today in a way that surprises you, and it lasts a few hours. A friend's joke lands like criticism, being left out of a plan stings more than it should, and an ordinary disagreement stirs something much older. You want comfort and you also push it away, worried that needing it makes you weak. Old patterns show up: over-apologising, looking after everyone else so you do not have to feel your own sadness. The pressure is emotional rather than practical, and it eases by the evening. Underneath it sits a clear glimpse of where you still expect to be hurt, and seeing it plainly is the beginning of it hurting less."
  },
  "moon|mc": {
    "conj": "For a few hours today your private feelings step into public view. At work you are more visible than usual, and what you feel shows on your face whether you want it to or not. A manager notices your mood, a client picks up on your warmth, or a colleague sees you rattled. You care deeply about how you are received, and praise or criticism lands with extra weight. It is a good time for work that needs heart: looking after people, pitching something you believe in, speaking up for your team. The catch is taking professional moments personally. By tonight the spotlight moves on, and you know better what kind of work feeds you.",
    "soft": "Feelings and ambitions support each other today for a few hours. You feel at home at work, or at least in the role you are building, and people respond to your natural warmth. A friendly word from someone senior, an easy phone call or a thank-you from a customer lifts your mood. Family and career stop competing for once, and you manage to leave on time without guilt. You read what people need and respond gracefully, which adds to your reputation. None of it is showy, yet it reminds you that you do your best work when you feel emotionally settled.",
    "hard": "Home and work tug you in opposite directions for a few hours today. A family matter needs you just as a deadline lands, or you are at your desk while your mind is on a sick parent or a sulking partner. You feel judged from both sides and short on patience with each. Moods leak into professional exchanges, so an email reads colder than you meant or you well up in a meeting over something small. The tension is brief but pointed. It shows you where your private needs have been squeezed out by public duties, and by tonight you have a much clearer sense of which one needs attention first."
  },
  "sun|mercury": {
    "conj": "For a day or two the Sun crosses your Mercury, and your mind feels switched on and lit from within. You have ideas and you want them heard: in meetings, in messages, over dinner. Conversations flow, and you find the right words for something you have struggled to explain for weeks. It is an excellent window for writing, pitching, interviews or the conversation you keep postponing. People listen to you, which is gratifying and also a little intoxicating. The shadow is talking over others or treating every opinion as a statement of who you are. Used well, these two days leave you with a clearer head and one or two things said out loud.",
    "soft": "Your thinking and your sense of purpose line up nicely for a day or two. Paperwork gets done, emails come out clear, and a tricky explanation makes sense to the person who needed it. You feel confident enough to share an idea without over-preparing, and it is well received. A useful conversation with a mentor, a sibling or a neighbour points you in a helpful direction. Short trips and errands go smoothly. Nothing here shouts for attention, so it slips past easily. Thoughts you put in writing now come out closer to what you mean than they have in a while.",
    "hard": "Your words carry more heat than you intend for a day or two while the Sun presses on your Mercury. You feel a need to be right, and discussions turn into debates before you have noticed the shift. A comment about your work or your opinions lands as a comment about you. Emails need a second read before sending, and a colleague or relative challenges your version of events. Your mind races at night, replaying what you said and polishing what you should have said. The friction is useful, though. It shows where your views are firmly yours and where you have been repeating someone else's."
  },
  "sun|jupiter": {
    "conj": "The Sun lights up your Jupiter for a day or two, and you feel bigger, luckier and more generous than usual. Good news has a way of arriving now: a yes to an application, an invitation, a friend with a spare ticket. You are in the mood to say yes back, to plans, to dessert, to the weekend away. People enjoy your company because you are expansive and upbeat. The only danger is overdoing it: agreeing to too much, spending freely, promising what next week cannot deliver. Even so, this brief window of warmth reminds you how much is possible when you let yourself believe in it.",
    "soft": "Things go your way with less effort than usual for the next day or two. A conversation with someone influential flows, a small risk pays off, and you find yourself in the right place for a lucky break. Your confidence is steady rather than loud, which makes others trust you. It is a lovely window for travel plans, study, a job application or asking for a favour. You feel generous and it shows: you pick up the bill, offer your time, cheer on a friend. The ease is quiet and passes unnoticed unless you use it. Whatever you begin now carries a pleasant tailwind into the weeks ahead.",
    "hard": "Your appetite for more outruns your sense of proportion for a day or two. You say yes to three plans on the same evening, order the bigger option, or promise a deadline you cannot meet. Confidence tips into overconfidence, and someone points it out, which stings. You clash with a person whose beliefs or big ideas rub against yours, and the argument becomes about principle. There is optimism under all this, but it needs a floor beneath it. Once it passes, you have a clearer sense of which hopes are worth backing and which were just enthusiasm talking."
  },
  "sun|neptune": {
    "conj": "For a day or two the Sun lands on your Neptune, and the edges of your world go soft and dreamy. You feel drawn to music, films, the sea, a long bath, anything that lets you drift. Your sensitivity is high, so you pick up on other people's moods before they say a word. Creative work flows and a small act of kindness feels unusually meaningful. The difficulty is focus: you lose your keys, miss the email, forget what you went upstairs for. Your sense of self goes misty too, easily swayed by whoever you are with. These two days are made for imagining and feeling, far more than for hard decisions.",
    "soft": "Imagination and your sense of self work together beautifully for the next day or two. You feel inspired, gentle and in tune with the people around you. A song, a book or a conversation touches something deep and leaves you softer. It is a good window for creative work, for prayer or meditation if that is your thing, and for helping someone without needing thanks. Intuition is reliable now, so the hunch about who to call or which way to go is worth trusting. Very little happens on the surface. Underneath, you reconnect with a gentler, more hopeful version of yourself.",
    "hard": "Your energy and clarity both run low for a day or two as the Sun pulls against your Neptune. You feel tired without knowing why, easily hurt, or vaguely disappointed in someone you had built up. Messages get misread, plans go hazy, and a promise from someone else turns out to be softer than it sounded. Escape looks tempting: extra wine, endless scrolling, a nap that becomes an afternoon. People lean on you for rescuing and you find it hard to say no. The fog lifts soon enough, and what it leaves behind is a sharper eye for where you have been seeing what you wanted to see."
  },
  "sun|northNode": {
    "conj": "For a day or two the Sun crosses your North Node, and you feel a strong pull towards the future you are meant to grow into. Choices that normally feel murky look obvious. You meet someone, read something or get an offer that seems to point straight at the path ahead. Old comfortable habits look a little stale, and you notice how often you default to them. People see you more clearly as you are becoming, not as you used to be. Stepping forward carries some discomfort, because the new direction always feels less familiar than the old one. Even so, the nudge these days offer is unusually clear.",
    "soft": "You feel lined up with where your life is heading over the next day or two. A conversation, an opportunity or a small decision moves you a step closer to the person you want to become. Things that usually take nerve, such as speaking up, starting something new or reaching out to a stranger, feel almost ordinary. You recognise helpful people when they appear and respond to them warmly. Friends notice you seem lighter and more certain. Nothing dramatic is required: following the natural pull of these days leaves you further along than you expected, with a quiet sense that you are on the right road.",
    "hard": "Old habits and new growth pull you in two directions for a day or two. People from the past reappear, or familiar roles tug at you just when you want to move forward. Someone close disagrees with the direction you are taking, and their doubt echoes your own. You notice how much easier it is to slip into what you already know, even when it no longer fits. The friction is uncomfortable but brief. When it settles, you know better which parts of your past to honour and which to let go, and that clarity is worth the tension."
  },
  "mercury|sun": {
    "conj": "This week Mercury passes over your Sun for a few days, and your mind is busy with you: your plans, your image, your next move. Conversations centre on you, whether you are explaining yourself, interviewing, or chatting about your week. Your phone is busier than usual, with calls, texts and small admin tasks arriving in a stream. It is a strong window for writing, presenting or arguing your case, because words come easily and people listen. The catch is overthinking your own story, going round and round on a decision until it loses shape. Something important about who you are gets said out loud this week, and it sticks.",
    "soft": "Your thoughts and your sense of self are on friendly terms for the next few days. You express yourself clearly, and people understand what you mean the first time. It is an easy window for emails, applications, sorting paperwork or making plans that suit you rather than everyone else. Short trips and errands go smoothly, and a chat with a sibling, neighbour or colleague lifts your spirits. Your mind feels bright and curious, ready to learn something new. Nothing forces the issue, so the chance is easy to waste on small talk. Picked up, it leaves you with a clear head and a sorted to-do list.",
    "hard": "Mercury needles your Sun for a few days, and your thoughts get busy and a little combative. You are more defensive than usual, hearing criticism in ordinary feedback. Messages cross, someone misunderstands a plan, and you spend energy explaining what you meant. Late at night you rehearse arguments with people who are not in the room. Admin and details pile up just when you want to focus on the bigger picture. The strain is mostly mental and it passes quickly. It sharpens your sense of what you believe, and where your ego has been doing the talking."
  },
  "mercury|venus": {
    "conj": "Sweet words come easily for a few days while Mercury sits on your Venus. You find yourself writing the thoughtful message, paying the compliment, or saying the loving thing you usually leave unsaid. Flirting is light and fun, and conversations with friends drift towards art, beauty and pleasure. It is a lovely window for negotiating money, smoothing over a disagreement or planning a date. You notice what is attractive in everything, from a well-made cup of coffee to a clever sentence. The one catch is saying what people want to hear rather than what you mean. Otherwise, these are gentle days that make connection feel effortless.",
    "soft": "Over the next few days your words carry warmth and charm without effort. You say the right thing to a friend who is down, and your texts land with the intended tone. Social plans come together nicely, and a casual chat turns into a lovely afternoon. It is a good time to talk money, whether you are asking for a better rate or sorting a shared bill, because you strike a fair, friendly note. Creative ideas arrive easily, especially for writing, design or anything with a pleasing shape. The mood is light rather than profound, and it leaves you feeling that people are glad to hear from you.",
    "hard": "Conversations about love or money get awkward for a few days as Mercury rubs against your Venus. You say something meant kindly that comes out wrong, or a partner hears criticism where you intended a joke. A disagreement about spending, plans or who does what drags on longer than it should. You are tempted to smooth things over by agreeing, then resent it later. Your taste feels out of step with the people around you, and small choices, a restaurant, a gift, cause friction. The irritation is brief. Underneath, it reveals where affection and honesty have drifted apart, so you can bring them back together."
  },
  "mercury|saturn": {
    "conj": "Your mind turns serious for a few days as Mercury meets your Saturn. You find yourself making lists, reading the small print and thinking hard about responsibilities. Conversations with people in authority, a boss, a bank, a landlord, take up your attention and demand care. Your words come out slower and more measured, which lends them weight. It is an excellent window for contracts, planning and anything that needs discipline. The heaviness is real, though: you worry more, hear doubt in your own thoughts and struggle to switch off. What you get done now is solid and practical, the kind of work your future self thanks you for.",
    "soft": "Steady, patient and grounded: that is how your thinking runs for the next few days. You can focus for longer than usual and finish the tedious job you have been putting off. Conversations with older people, mentors or anyone in charge go well because you come across as sensible and prepared. It is a strong window for studying, organising finances, planning a project or putting agreements in writing. Your worries shrink once you write them down and make a plan. Nothing here feels exciting. Yet the quiet, careful work you do these days builds a foundation you can lean on for months.",
    "hard": "For a few days Mercury presses on your Saturn, and your thoughts feel heavy and critical. Delays pile up: the reply that does not come, the form rejected, the call put on hold for forty minutes. You hear a harsh inner voice telling you that your ideas are not good enough. Conversations with authority figures feel stiff, and you come away sure you said the wrong thing. Going quiet feels safer than risking judgement. The pressure eases within days, and it leaves you with a much clearer picture of where your plans need more structure and where your self-doubt has been too loud."
  },
  "mercury|pluto": {
    "conj": "Mercury crosses your Pluto for a few days, and your mind goes deep. Small talk bores you; you want to get to the heart of things. You notice what is not being said, read between the lines of emails and pick up on hidden motives. A conversation turns intense, a secret comes out, or you research something you have avoided. Your words carry unusual power, persuasive and piercing, so people either lean in or get defensive. The shadow is obsessive thinking, turning one comment over for hours. Something you learn in these few days changes how you see a situation for good.",
    "soft": "For a few days your mind is sharp, focused and powerful. You can concentrate on a difficult problem and see straight through to what matters. Conversations that usually feel risky, about money, sex, trust or change, go surprisingly well because you speak honestly without overwhelming anyone. It is a good window for research, therapy, detective work of any kind or clearing out old files and messages. People confide in you and you handle it with care. Nothing feels dramatic on the surface. Underneath, you let go of an old way of thinking and feel lighter for it.",
    "hard": "Conversations turn into power struggles for a few days while Mercury squares or opposes your Pluto. Someone tries to control the narrative, or you catch yourself pushing too hard to win a point. You pick up on manipulation, real or imagined, and struggle to let a suspicion go. A piece of information surfaces that changes how you see a person or a plan. Your thoughts circle obsessively in the small hours. The intensity is short but sharp, and it cuts through a lot of pretence, leaving you with a truer understanding of a situation even if it is uncomfortable to face."
  },
  "mercury|asc": {
    "conj": "You come across as quick, chatty and switched on for a few days while Mercury crosses your Ascendant. People notice your ideas and ask your opinion. Your phone buzzes more, errands multiply, and you seem to be running from one small conversation to the next. It is a good window for interviews, first meetings, presentations or anything where you need to explain yourself well. You feel restless in your body too, fidgety and keen to move. The only downside is scattering your energy across too many threads. Somewhere in all that chatter, you make a sharp impression on someone who matters.",
    "soft": "Bright, clear and easy to talk to: that is how you come across over the next few days. Strangers strike up conversations, and you find yourself chatting in queues and on the bus. It is an easy window for networking, a first date, a job interview or catching up with neighbours. Your wit is sharp without being cutting, and people enjoy your company. Small tasks go smoothly: the call to the doctor, the booking, the form. A walk that lets your mind wander does you more good than usual. These days leave you feeling more connected to the world outside your front door.",
    "hard": "The way you come across gets misread for a few days as Mercury rubs against your Ascendant. A quick remark lands badly, or someone seems to have formed the wrong impression of you. Partners and close colleagues challenge what you say, and conversations feel like negotiations. Your nerves are jumpy, and you talk too fast or too much when you are anxious. Small mix-ups, the wrong address, the missed call, add to the sense of friction. The irritation passes quickly. It teaches you something useful about how your words sound to others, and where a little more care would change the outcome."
  },
  "venus|moon": {
    "conj": "Life feels softer and more affectionate for a few days while Venus sits on your Moon. You want comfort and beauty: flowers on the table, a good meal, a cosy evening with someone you love, a film you have seen ten times. Your home looks more appealing, and you have the urge to tidy, decorate or invite people round. Feelings flow easily, and you find it simple to show love and to receive it. A friend or partner is unusually sweet to you, and small kindnesses stay with you all day. The only danger is indulgence, one more biscuit, one more purchase. These are lovely days for nurturing yourself and the people closest to you.",
    "soft": "Over the next few days your feelings are warm and settled, and relationships flow gently. You feel appreciated by the people around you and quick to appreciate them back, with a hug, a small gift or a message that simply says you are thinking of them. It is a good window for a family meal, a heart-to-heart or making your home prettier. Money matters linked to home or family go smoothly. You notice pleasure in simple things: sunlight through a window, clean sheets, a favourite song. There is nothing dramatic to report. What these days give you is a gentle reminder of how much sweetness already lives in your ordinary life.",
    "hard": "Your need for love clashes with what you are getting for a few days, as Venus squares or opposes your Moon. You feel slightly neglected, oversensitive to a partner's distraction or a friend's late reply. Comfort eating, comfort shopping and comfort scrolling all beckon. A small disagreement about home, money or who does what flares into hurt feelings. You want to be looked after and are frustrated when people do not read your mind. The mood lifts within days. It shows you plainly which needs you have been expecting others to meet, and which you can meet yourself."
  },
  "venus|mars": {
    "conj": "Desire comes alive for a few days as Venus meets your Mars. You feel attractive and bold, drawn to people and pleasures you would usually hold back from. Flirting is easy, chemistry sparks, and a relationship heats up in the best sense. It is a lovely window for dates, creative projects and anything that combines passion with pleasure. You also want things faster than usual, so patience wears thin when a crush is slow to reply. Arguments can turn into passion, or passion into arguments. Acting on something you want, for once without apology, feels very good.",
    "soft": "Your charm and your drive work together gracefully for the next few days. You go after what you want without seeming pushy, and people respond with warmth. Romance flows easily, whether it is a new spark or a renewed closeness with a partner. It is a good window for creative work, exercise that feels like play, or asking for something you want at work. You find a balance between giving and taking that usually eludes you. The ease is pleasant and easily missed. These days remind you that desire and kindness can sit happily side by side.",
    "hard": "Desire gets tangled with friction for a few days while Venus squares or opposes your Mars. You want closeness and conflict at the same time, snapping at a partner then wishing they would hold you. Attraction flares towards someone unsuitable, or an old tension about who pursues whom resurfaces. Small disagreements carry a charge that feels almost electric. Impulse spending on treats or clothes is hard to resist. The irritation is short-lived, but it is revealing. It shows you where your wants and your values have fallen out of step, and gives you the chance to bring them back together."
  },
  "venus|uranus": {
    "conj": "Love and pleasure take an unexpected turn this week as Venus crosses your Uranus for a few days. You feel drawn to someone different from your usual type, or a relationship surprises you with a sudden shift. Spontaneity feels delicious: a last-minute date, a change of look, a new hobby picked up on a whim. You want freedom and excitement, and routine affection seems dull by comparison. Money can move suddenly too, either a windfall or an impulsive purchase. The only caution is mistaking novelty for depth. These days shake up your heart in ways that often point towards what you have been missing.",
    "soft": "Pleasure comes with a pleasant spark of surprise over the next few days. A friend introduces you to someone interesting, an unexpected invitation arrives, or you discover a new place you love. You feel free to be yourself in relationships and less worried about fitting in. It is a lovely window for trying a new creative style, a new hairstyle or a spontaneous day out. Your partner or friends see a lively side of you. None of this asks you to overturn anything. It reminds you that love can be fresh and fun without losing its roots.",
    "hard": "Relationships feel unsettled for a few days as Venus pulls against your Uranus. Plans with a partner change abruptly, or someone blows hot and cold with you. You swing between craving closeness and needing space, confusing the people who care for you. A friend cancels at the last minute, and you are more relieved than you expected. An impulse buy or a sudden attraction tempts you to act without thinking. Old frustrations about feeling trapped in routine come to the surface. The disruption is brief but lively, and it reveals where your love life needs more freedom and where you need more steadiness."
  },
  "venus|chiron": {
    "conj": "Love brings old tenderness to the surface for a few days while Venus touches your Chiron. A kind word from a partner, a friend or even a stranger moves you almost to tears. Old insecurities about your looks, your worth or whether you are truly loved come back into view. Yet you are also unusually good at soothing others, and people open up to you. It is a healing window for honest conversations, therapy, or treating yourself gently. You find small ways to repair a relationship, or at least to understand what went wrong. You come out of it carrying a little more self-acceptance than before.",
    "soft": "For a few days affection and healing flow together. Someone offers you the kind of care you have always wanted, and you let it in. You find yourself talking about an old hurt without it feeling raw, even laughing about it. It is a good window for making amends, reconnecting with someone you lost touch with, or spending money on something that restores you. Your compassion for others runs deep, and your presence comforts. These are quiet days, easily overlooked. What they give you is a gentler relationship with yourself, and a sense that old wounds can become sources of warmth.",
    "hard": "Love feels tender in an uncomfortable way for a few days as Venus rubs against your Chiron. A careless comment about your appearance or a moment of being overlooked stings far more than it should. Old stories about not being good enough, not being wanted or always giving more than you get come back to the surface. You notice how quickly you shrink to make yourself easier to love. Buying comfort or chasing reassurance looks easier than sitting with the feeling. Someone close touches a sore spot without meaning to. The ache passes, leaving clearer insight into where you still expect rejection."
  },
  "venus|mc": {
    "conj": "You shine at work and in public for a few days while Venus crosses your MC. People like you, your charm opens doors, and even the receptionist seems pleased to see you. A compliment from your boss, a good review or a friendly meeting with someone influential brightens the week. It is a lovely window for presentations, networking, interviews or asking for a raise. Your career feels more pleasurable, and you enjoy your role more than usual. The trap is relying on charm when effort is needed. Your reputation grows a little warmer this week, and people remember you fondly.",
    "soft": "Work runs more smoothly over the next few days, and people respond to you warmly. A colleague offers help, a client is pleased, or you receive a small appreciation that means a lot. Even a tense meeting ends with laughter, which surprises you. It is a good window for collaboration, making your workspace nicer or planning a career move that fits your values. You feel comfortable being seen and valued for what you do, and money connected to work flows more easily. Nothing dramatic happens. Yet these days build goodwill that pays off for months.",
    "hard": "Private affections and your public role tug at each other for a few days as Venus presses on your MC. A relationship matter distracts you from work, or a work commitment clashes with a date or family event. You want to be liked at work and find yourself people-pleasing more than you would like. Someone challenges your taste, your values or your standing. Spending on appearances, clothes, a work dinner, feels tempting and slightly excessive. The friction is short. It reminds you that what you love and what you do both need space, and neither thrives when the other is ignored."
  },
  "mars|mercury": {
    "conj": "Your mind is fast, sharp and ready for a fight this week while Mars sits on your Mercury for a few days. You speak quickly, decide quickly and get impatient with anyone slow to follow. It is an excellent window for debates, deadlines, writing sprints and cutting through admin. Your words have force, and people listen, though they can also feel bruised. Arguments break out over small things, in the group chat, at the dinner table, on the road. Your nerves run hot, and sleep can be restless. A mental task you had been avoiding for weeks finally gets done.",
    "soft": "Your thinking is energetic and decisive for the next few days. You tackle problems head-on and find solutions quickly. It is a good window for tough conversations, negotiations, studying for an exam or clearing your inbox. Your words carry conviction without aggression, and people respect your directness, even the colleague who usually argues with everything you say. You are happy to say no to requests that would waste your time, and nobody minds. A plan that had stalled starts moving again because you made the call. These days leave you feeling capable and clear, having got more done than you expected.",
    "hard": "Conversations heat up fast for a few days to a week as Mars pressures your Mercury. You are irritable, sharp-tongued and quick to take offence. A disagreement at work or at home escalates, and you say something you regret. Emails sent in anger, road rage and snapping at family are all tempting outlets. Minor mishaps, a cut finger, a dropped phone, come from rushing. Your mind races and struggles to settle, making it hard to sleep. The friction is intense while it lasts, and it shows you where frustration has been building so you can address it directly rather than letting it leak out sideways."
  },
  "mars|jupiter": {
    "conj": "You feel bold, energetic and ready to take a risk for a few days as Mars meets your Jupiter. Big plans seem achievable, and you have the drive to start them. It is a great window for sport, travel, launching a project or asking for something ambitious. Your enthusiasm is infectious, and people want to join you. The trap is overdoing it: too much spending, too many commitments, too fast. You feel invincible, which is exhilarating and occasionally reckless. By the end of the week you have taken a concrete step towards something you have wanted for a while.",
    "soft": "Energy and optimism work well together for the next few days. You have the confidence to go after what you want and the stamina to see it through. It is a good window for exercise, learning a new skill, a job application or planning a trip. Luck seems to favour action, so taking the first step pays off. Your generosity shows up practically, helping a friend move house or backing a colleague's idea. Small wins pile up, and you begin to trust your own judgement a little more. These days give you a sense of momentum that lasts beyond the transit itself.",
    "hard": "Your appetite for action outruns your good sense for a few days as Mars pushes against your Jupiter. You take on too much, spend too freely or push too hard in the gym. You sign up, book or commit before checking the diary. Arguments about beliefs, politics or fairness flare up, and you feel morally certain in a way that irritates others. Impatience with rules and limits leads to risky shortcuts. There is energy here, but it needs direction. The week teaches you where your ambition needs a clearer plan and where your confidence has run ahead of the facts."
  },
  "mars|neptune": {
    "conj": "Your energy goes misty for a few days to a week while Mars crosses your Neptune. You feel motivated one moment and drained the next, unsure where your drive has gone. Ideals come alive, and you are inspired to fight for a cause or help someone vulnerable. Creative work flows, especially music, dance or anything that uses the body poetically. The difficulty is clarity: you act on vague impulses, misjudge situations or get pulled into someone else's drama. Anger goes underground and comes out as quiet resentment. Once the haze clears, you see more plainly what is worth your effort.",
    "soft": "Drive and imagination blend gracefully over the next few days. You act on intuition, and it proves right. It is a good window for creative projects, gentle exercise like swimming or yoga, or helping someone without expecting thanks. You feel inspired to work towards a dream and find the energy to take a first step. Conflicts soften, and a tense situation at home eases without anyone forcing it. A late evening walk clears your head better than any to-do list. These days bring a sense of flow, where effort and inspiration feel like the same thing.",
    "hard": "Energy slips through your fingers this week as Mars pulls against your Neptune for a few days. You start things and lose interest, feel tired for no clear reason, or find yourself confused about what you want. Someone disappoints you, or you suspect you are being misled. Plans with a friend fall through vaguely, and nobody quite says why. Escapism beckons: too much wine, television, daydreaming. Anger feels muddled, and you struggle to stand up for yourself directly. The fog lifts within a week, showing you where you have been chasing an illusion rather than a solid goal."
  },
  "mars|northNode": {
    "conj": "You feel pushed towards your future for a few days as Mars crosses your North Node. You have the drive to take a step you have been putting off, and circumstances seem to demand it. A decision, a confrontation or a bold move sets you on a new path. You find yourself saying yes to the course, the job or the move that scares you a little. Old excuses sound thin even to you. The challenge is impatience, forcing things before they are ready. By the end of the week you have acted with courage in a direction that genuinely matters.",
    "soft": "Your energy supports your growth over the next few days. You find the courage to try something new, and it feels natural rather than forced. A conversation with someone ahead of you on the same road leaves you fired up. You sign up, send the email or book the first session without the usual dithering. People back you, and small steps build momentum faster than you expected, so within days the new thing already feels partly yours. Exercise that challenges you feels more rewarding than draining. These days give you a clear sense of progress towards the person you are becoming.",
    "hard": "Old reflexes and new growth pull against each other for a few days to a week while Mars pressures your nodal axis. You react from habit, fighting the familiar battles, even though you know they lead nowhere. An argument with a relative sounds word for word like one you had years ago. Someone challenges your direction, and your temper flares defensively. You notice the urge to prove yourself to people whose approval no longer matters. The friction is uncomfortable but brief, and it shows you which old patterns are holding you back from the path you want."
  },
  "moon|mercury": {
    "conj": "For a few hours today your feelings and your words run on the same wire. You say what you feel before you have finished feeling it, which makes a phone call with your sister or a message to a friend unusually honest. Small things lodge in your mind: a tone in someone's voice, a line from a song, the look on the barista's face. Thoughts drift towards home, family and old memories, and you catch yourself writing a to-do list that is a list of worries in disguise. Mood colours judgement, so a passing irritation can come out sounding like a verdict. By evening the tide has moved on, and what you said earlier reads softer than it felt.",
    "soft": "Today your head and your heart are on speaking terms, and it shows in how easily you talk. For a few hours you find the right words for something you have circled for weeks, whether that is telling your partner what you need or explaining to a colleague why a plan bothers you. Conversations with family or old friends flow, and a casual chat over tea turns into the one that settles something. You remember names, birthdays and the small preference someone mentioned once. Journalling, writing a card or sorting the kitchen drawer feels oddly satisfying, as though your mind is tidying itself too. Nothing dramatic happens, yet you go to bed feeling understood.",
    "hard": "For a few hours today your mood and your mind pull in different directions. You know the email is fine, yet something in you bristles at its tone, or you feel perfectly calm until a relative says one sentence that lands wrong. Overthinking creeps in: you replay a conversation in the shower and rewrite your side of it three times. Words come out sharper or more defensive than you meant, especially at home or with someone who knows your soft spots. Underneath all of it is a need to be heard, not just answered. Once the Moon moves on, usually by tonight, the knot loosens and the thing that felt urgent looks ordinary again."
  },
  "moon|jupiter": {
    "conj": "Today your feelings run large and generous for a few hours. You are the one who suggests ordering dessert, who texts an old friend out of nowhere, who says yes to the dinner invitation before checking the diary. Optimism comes easily, and a small kindness from a stranger lifts your whole afternoon. You feel roomy inside, with more patience for your children or your flatmate than usual. Excess is the price: an extra glass, a basket full of things you did not need, a promise bigger than your week can hold. The warmth is genuine all the same, and some of those big feelings will still be standing tomorrow.",
    "soft": "For a few hours today things feel on your side. A delayed parcel turns up, a friend offers to help without being asked, or you wake in a better mood than the week deserves. You are more forgiving than usual, and someone who annoyed you yesterday gets a second chance over coffee. Home feels like a good place to be, and cooking for others or hosting on short notice comes naturally. There is a teacherly warmth in you too, so a younger person or a struggling colleague leaves a chat with you lighter. None of it is dramatic, and that is the charm of it: a small, steady sense that life can be generous.",
    "hard": "Today your emotional appetite outgrows the moment. For a few hours you want more: more reassurance, more food, more attention, more of whatever will fill a vague restlessness. You overcommit at lunch, agreeing to host the weekend or cover a shift, then feel the weight of it by evening. Someone else's certainty rubs you up the wrong way, particularly a relative who knows best or a friend preaching their latest diet. A small feeling easily becomes a big story in your head. Beneath the overreach sits a hunger for meaning and room to breathe. By tomorrow the swell has passed and you can see which promises were yours to make."
  },
  "moon|neptune": {
    "conj": "For a few hours today your feelings go misty and porous. You pick up the mood of every room, well up at an advert, or sense a friend's sadness before they have mentioned it. Music, water, a long bath or a film pull at you more than conversation does. Your intuition is sharp: you think of someone and they ring. The same openness makes you easy to drain, and a crowded shop or a tense household leaves you tired for no clear reason. Plans blur, keys go missing, and a straight answer is hard to give. By tonight you come back to yourself, often carrying a tender insight you could never have reached by thinking.",
    "soft": "Today your imagination and your feelings hold hands for a few hours. You are gentler, more intuitive, better at reading between the lines of a message or a silence. A daydream on the bus turns into a usable idea: a sketch, a paragraph, a melody you hum all afternoon. Compassion comes easily, and you are the one who notices the colleague eating lunch alone. Quiet rituals feed you, like lighting a candle, walking by water or putting on the record that always softens you. Nothing about this window demands action. It lets you feel how connected you are, and that feeling outlasts the hours themselves.",
    "hard": "For a few hours today your feelings and reality do not quite line up. You misread a text as cold, or you trust a promise that sounds lovely and means little. A low, formless mood settles in, and you reach for the sofa, sugar, scrolling or wine to soften it. Someone close leans on you for rescue, and you give more than you have. Muddles around home or family plans are common: the wrong date, the vague arrangement, the job everyone thought someone else was doing. What is surfacing underneath is a longing for comfort that ordinary life is not providing just now. By evening the fog lifts and you see more plainly."
  },
  "moon|northNode": {
    "conj": "Today, for a few hours, your feelings point towards where your life is heading. A conversation, a chance meeting or a sudden pang of longing shows you what you want next, often faster than months of thinking managed. You feel pulled towards people who belong to your future rather than your past, and a new acquaintance seems oddly familiar. Emotional habits that keep you small become obvious, like the automatic yes to a family demand. The moment is fleeting, and it is easy to shrug it off as just a mood. The feeling that surfaces today is a true signpost, though, and you find yourself coming back to it weeks later.",
    "soft": "For a few hours today small emotional nudges line up with your bigger direction. You feel drawn to a class, a place, a person or a project that fits who you are becoming, and the pull feels natural rather than forced. A friend says something that confirms a hunch, or an invitation arrives that matches a quiet wish you had not voiced. You are more willing to try the unfamiliar: the new café, the different route home, the honest answer instead of the comfortable one. Nothing is decided today. You feel, briefly and warmly, that you are moving the right way, and the next step comes easier for it.",
    "hard": "Today your moods tug you between the familiar and the new for a few hours. Part of you wants to retreat into old comfort: the usual takeaway, the family role you know by heart, the friend who always agrees with you. Another part feels restless with all of it. An old pattern replays itself, and you rescue someone, go quiet to keep the peace, or chase approval you do not need. The friction is useful, because it shows which habits are pulling you backwards. You feel the discomfort in your stomach more than in your thoughts. By tonight the tension eases, and what stays with you is a clearer picture of the pattern you are ready to outgrow."
  },
  "sun|sun": {
    "conj": "This is your birthday window, and for a couple of days you feel more like yourself than at any other time of year. Energy returns, people remember you, and even strangers seem to notice you. You look back over the last twelve months with unusual clarity, knowing what you want to carry forward and what you are finished with. Plans made now carry weight, so the resolution scribbled on a napkin at your birthday dinner often becomes the theme of the year. Attention can also feel like pressure, and a forgotten call from someone you love stings more than it should. Underneath the cake and the messages, you feel a fresh start.",
    "soft": "For a couple of days you feel at ease in your own skin. Your energy is steady, your confidence unforced, and tasks you have been putting off get done without drama. People respond well to you, and you are more willing to take a small lead: organising the outing, speaking first in the meeting, suggesting the plan everyone ends up following. Creative play and time with children or friends feel good. It is not a spotlight moment, more a gentle tailwind that makes being yourself easy. You notice what lights you up, and you quietly give yourself permission to do a little more of it.",
    "hard": "For a couple of days you feel the pressure of being yourself in a world that wants something else. A boss questions your approach, a partner wants you to be different, or your own plans from a few months ago look off course. Your pride is touchy and your energy runs hot, then flat. This is a checkpoint in your year, showing what is not working in the way you are living. You push back, sometimes too hard, and later wish you had kept quieter over dinner. The friction brings clarity about where you need to adjust, and within a few days the pressure has settled."
  },
  "sun|venus": {
    "conj": "For a couple of days the light falls on your charm, your taste and what you love. You look good and know it, so the new haircut, the nicer shirt or the bold lipstick feels exactly right. Compliments arrive, and flirting comes easily, whether you are single or long settled. You want beauty and pleasure: a good meal, fresh flowers, the present for yourself you have eyed for weeks. Money flows outward more freely, which is lovely until you check the account on Monday. Relationships feel warmer and you are readier to say you care. Being seen like this reminds you what you truly value.",
    "soft": "The next couple of days feel sweet and easy around love, money and pleasure. Friends suggest plans, a date goes better than expected, or a small financial win lands: a refund, a good deal, a bit of extra work. You are diplomatic without effort, and a tense exchange with a partner or colleague resolves over something as simple as sharing lunch. Your eye for colour and style is sharp, so rearranging a room or choosing a gift becomes a pleasure. People like being around you and let you know it. This is a gentle, social window rather than a turning point, and it leaves you feeling appreciated.",
    "hard": "For a couple of days what you want and what you value feel slightly out of step. You want to be liked, yet you also want to be yourself, and a friend's or partner's expectations press right on that gap. Spending runs ahead of sense, from the dinner you cannot quite afford to the outfit bought to cheer yourself up. Small tensions in love surface: who always compromises, who plans the dates, who says sorry first. You catch yourself being agreeable to avoid a scene, then resenting it on the way home. The friction points to what you genuinely value, as opposed to what earns approval, and it fades within days."
  },
  "sun|saturn": {
    "conj": "For a couple of days the spotlight falls on your responsibilities. Deadlines, bills, the manager's feedback, the chore you keep avoiding: whatever you owe is plain to see. You feel older and more serious, and your patience for nonsense drops sharply. It is a strong window for serious work, filing the paperwork, having the grown-up conversation, committing to a plan with a date on it. The weight can feel lonely, as if you carry everything and nobody notices. Yet the effort you put in now is seen by the right people, often a boss or a parent figure whose respect matters to you more than you admit.",
    "soft": "The next couple of days reward steady effort. You sit down to the task and actually finish it, whether that is the tax form, the report, the difficult email or the shelf you have meant to put up for a year. Older people and those in charge are helpful, and advice from a mentor or a seasoned colleague lands well. You feel competent and quietly proud rather than flashy. Structure feels supportive instead of confining, so a new routine, an early night or a firm budget sticks. Your word carries weight right now, and a promise you make this week is one you keep.",
    "hard": "For a couple of days you run into the wall of your limits. The boss says no, the budget will not stretch, and your body wants rest just when you want to push on. Criticism stings, and you take a small setback personally, replaying the meeting on the drive home. You feel tired, underappreciated and more burdened than usual, sometimes by a parent or authority who seems set on blocking you. The frustration is real, and so is the information it carries: it shows where you have overpromised or where your structure has cracks. Once it passes you are clearer about what to drop and what deserves your commitment."
  },
  "sun|pluto": {
    "conj": "For a couple of days life turns intense and you feel it in your gut. Conversations go deeper than you planned, a secret comes out, or you suddenly want to change something in your life right now. Power dynamics become visible: who controls the money, who decides, who backs down first. You are magnetic and a little formidable, and people either lean in or step back. Old feelings of jealousy or fear stir, sometimes over something small like an unanswered message. The intensity is uncomfortable, yet it lets you cut through pretence and admit what you want. You come out of it with a sharper sense of your own strength.",
    "soft": "The next couple of days give you quiet power. You see through excuses, read what others leave unsaid, and get to the heart of a problem in minutes. A research task, a ruthless tidy-out or a frank conversation about money or intimacy goes well because depth does not frighten you. You are persuasive without pushing, and someone who usually resists your ideas comes round. There is a pleasing sense of renewal, as if you have shed a layer of skin. You clear out a cupboard, cancel a subscription or drop a habit that was draining you, and it feels like reclaiming your own energy.",
    "hard": "For a couple of days you feel pushed, and you push back. Someone tries to control the plan, the money or the story, and your will rises to meet theirs. Arguments become power struggles about something bigger than the topic on the table, and you feel a hot urge to win. Suspicion creeps in, so you read hidden motives into a delayed reply or a vague comment from a colleague. Old wounds around being overpowered or manipulated sit close to the surface. The strain is intense, yet it exposes where you hand your power away and where you grab for it. Once it eases, you know what to release."
  },
  "sun|asc": {
    "conj": "For a couple of days you are highly visible. You walk into a room and heads turn, colleagues ask your opinion, and even your photos come out well. You feel physically energised, more confident about how you look, and ready to make a first impression. A new look, a fresh start at the gym or putting yourself forward for something all feel natural now. You catch your reflection in a shop window and see a more assured person looking back. For a shy person the attention can feel exposing, yet it brings a sense of renewal, like a small birthday for your image and your body.",
    "soft": "The next couple of days make it easy to present yourself well. You feel healthy, upbeat and at ease in your body, and people respond warmly. Introductions go smoothly, from the interview to the first date to the meeting with a new client. Friends and siblings are good company, and a short trip or a walk somewhere new lifts your spirits. You say hello to strangers more readily and walk away with a new contact or a new friend. Nothing about it is forced: your outer self and inner self line up, so you come across as exactly who you are.",
    "hard": "For a couple of days your self-image meets other people's view of you, and the two do not match. A partner, client or friend pushes back on how you present yourself, or a relationship demands more than you want to give. You feel self-conscious, noticing tired eyes in the mirror or feeling overdressed at the party. Someone else takes the spotlight, and you are surprised how much that bothers you. A pull runs between wanting to stand alone and needing others' approval. All of this is honest feedback on how you come across, and within a few days you know which parts of it to keep."
  },
  "mercury|moon": {
    "conj": "For a few days your mind is busy with feelings, home and family. You talk about your emotions more than usual, ring your mother, sort through old photos, and narrate your moods in messages to friends. Memories surface in surprising detail, down to the smell of a childhood kitchen. Domestic admin piles up: repairs, bills, the shopping list, the family group chat. Your thinking is intuitive and a little subjective, so you know how you feel about a decision long before you can explain why. Worry can run in loops at night. Talking it through with someone who listens properly brings relief this week.",
    "soft": "This week words and feelings cooperate. You can say what you need without drama, which makes these few days ideal for the conversation with a partner or housemate you have been postponing. You remember the small things that matter to people, and your messages carry warmth. Writing a journal, a letter or a thoughtful review flows easily. Family calls are pleasant, and practical home matters, from booking a plumber to planning Sunday lunch, get sorted without friction. You feel mentally at home, as if your thoughts and your heart finally sit at the same table and pass each other the bread.",
    "hard": "For a few days your head and your heart argue. You know logically it was nothing, yet the comment keeps stinging, or you feel strongly about something you cannot quite put into words. Conversations at home turn prickly, and a small disagreement about dishes or plans becomes a question of who listens to whom. You overthink, drafting and deleting messages, and your sleep suffers under the chatter. Old family scripts creep into your tone of voice. The tension exposes where you have been saying yes with your mouth and no with your gut. Afterwards you speak far more honestly about what you need."
  },
  "mercury|mars": {
    "conj": "This week your mind is quick, sharp and ready for a fight. You say what you think immediately, and your words land hard, so a debate at work or a disagreement with a partner heats up faster than you expect. Energy for tasks is high: you blast through the inbox, send the complaint, argue your case to the landlord. Driving, typing and talking all speed up, which also brings minor knocks and typos. Impatience with slow people shows on your face before you can hide it. The same fire makes you brilliantly decisive, and the thing you have been too timid to say comes out.",
    "soft": "For a few days your thoughts and your drive work as a team. You decide quickly and act on it, so the job application goes out, the awkward phone call gets made, and the stalled project moves. You argue well without making enemies, and haggling over a price or pushing for a deadline goes your way. Sport, a brisk walk or a hands-on job clears your head beautifully. You are direct in a way people appreciate, and speaking up in meetings feels natural rather than brave. By the end of the week you notice how much you have achieved simply by saying it and then doing it.",
    "hard": "For a few days your words carry more heat than you intend. A short email reads as an attack, a comment at dinner starts a row, and you find yourself arguing with a stranger online at midnight. Irritability runs high and patience low with anyone who interrupts or contradicts you. You rush, which leads to slips: the wrong attachment, a burnt pan, a scrape on the car door. Underneath sits frustrated desire, something you want and have not felt free to push for. Once the heat passes you see which argument was worth having, and you pick it up again more calmly."
  },
  "mercury|uranus": {
    "conj": "This week your mind lights up with sudden ideas and unexpected news. You wake with a plan, change it by lunch and have a new one by bedtime. Messages come out of the blue: an old friend, a job lead, a surprising invitation. You say unusual things and surprise even yourself with your bluntness. Technology behaves strangely, the phone glitches, a meeting moves at the last minute. Your nerves run fast, and sleep comes in restless bursts. The rush of insight is real, though, and something you realise this week changes how you see a problem that has been stuck for ages.",
    "soft": "For a few days your thinking is fresh and inventive. Solutions pop into your head in the shower, and you see a new way to organise your work, your finances or your week. Conversations with friends, colleagues or people online spark ideas you would never have found alone. Learning a new app, a new skill or a new route home feels fun rather than tiresome. Your humour is quick and a little quirky, and people enjoy your company for it. Small surprises arrive and mostly please you. Breaking a stale routine feels exciting now, so change you have resisted for months looks easy.",
    "hard": "For a few days your nerves are jangled and your plans keep changing. Emails arrive at awkward moments, appointments get cancelled, and news lands that forces a quick rethink. You feel restless and blunt, and you blurt out something you cannot take back. Stubborn opinions collide, especially with friends or colleagues who are sure they know better. Sleep runs thin because your mind will not switch off. The disruption is tiring, yet it shakes loose thinking that had set too hard. Looking back a week later, one of those surprises was actually showing you a better way forward."
  },
  "mercury|chiron": {
    "conj": "This week words touch old wounds. Someone says something casual that hits a sore spot, or you find yourself telling a story from your past you have not told in years. Memories of being misunderstood, talked over or teased for how you spoke come back vividly. You feel self-conscious about your intelligence, rereading a message four times before sending it. At the same time you have an unusual gift for saying the healing thing to someone else who is hurting. A conversation this week, with a close friend or a therapist, helps you name a hurt you had never quite put into words.",
    "soft": "For a few days you find the right words for tender things. You open up to a friend about a struggle, and they respond with more understanding than you expected. Writing, reading or listening to someone speak about an experience like yours brings relief. You notice when others are hurting and know what to say, so people seek you out for a quiet chat. An old insecurity about learning or speaking feels lighter, and you share an idea you usually keep to yourself. The healing here is quiet: one conversation or one paragraph that shifts something inside you for good.",
    "hard": "For a few days communication rubs against an old sore. You feel dismissed in a meeting, misunderstood by a partner or criticised for something you said, and the sting runs deeper than the moment deserves. You replay the exchange, feeling like the child who was never taken seriously. Defensiveness or silence becomes the reflex, and you shut the laptop rather than reply. Anxious late-night searching about your health or your future tends to crop up too. Painful as it is, the friction shows you where the old wound still speaks for you. Once the week passes, you understand that hurt a little better and it holds you a little less."
  },
  "mercury|mc": {
    "conj": "This week your career is in the conversation. You are talking with your boss, pitching an idea, writing the proposal, updating your profile, or taking an unexpected call about work. Your words carry public weight, so what you say in a meeting or post online gets noticed by people who matter to your reputation. You think clearly about your goals and can see the next practical step. Contracts, applications and paperwork connected to your job move forward. The pace is busy, with messages stacking up faster than you can answer, yet the attention your thinking earns gives your standing a solid lift.",
    "soft": "For a few days you communicate well at work. Presentations, emails and negotiations land, and a manager or client openly appreciates your ideas. You network without trying, chatting to the right person at the right moment, and a small introduction leads somewhere useful. Planning your career feels easy, whether you are updating a CV, researching a course or mapping out the next quarter. Your reputation benefits from your clarity, and people start quoting your phrasing back to you. It is a light, productive stretch in which well-chosen words open professional doors that had seemed firmly shut.",
    "hard": "For a few days work talk and home life pull against each other, or your words at work misfire. An email to your manager is misread, a meeting veers off track, or you are asked to explain yourself in front of others. Family demands interrupt professional plans, and you feel torn between answering the office and answering the house. Worry about your status or your next move fills your mind at odd hours. You rehearse what you should have said while brushing your teeth. The friction shows where the way you talk about your ambitions needs sharpening, and afterwards you speak up for your work more firmly."
  },
  "venus|mercury": {
    "conj": "This week your words turn charming. You find the lovely thing to say, write a sweet message, and smooth over a tense exchange with a well-timed joke. Flirtation lives in texts and conversations, so a chat with someone you fancy runs long into the night. Your taste is sharp, and choosing a gift, rearranging a shelf or polishing a piece of writing feels like a pleasure. Negotiations about money or plans go well because you are gracious and persuasive. The catch is a habit of saying what people want to hear rather than what you think. Mostly, though, you connect easily and enjoy every minute of it.",
    "soft": "For a few days conversations are warm and easy. You get along with colleagues, catch up with old friends, and a call with a sibling or a neighbour turns into a pleasant hour. Writing and speaking carry a natural grace, so a thank-you note, a pitch or a love letter comes out beautifully. You persuade gently, and a small deal or agreement falls into place without haggling. Art, music and good books feed your mind, and you want to share what you are enjoying. This is a sociable, soft stretch in which your ideas and your affection pull in the same direction.",
    "hard": "For a few days what you think and what you want to feel do not quite agree. You say something to keep the peace and wince at its dishonesty later, or you overanalyse a romantic message until all its charm drains away. Small misunderstandings with a partner or friend arise over plans, favours or money. You feel torn between being nice and being truthful. Shopping decisions wobble, and you add a jacket to the basket, remove it, then add it again. The tension points to where your values and your words need to line up. Before Venus moves on, you manage to say the real thing more kindly."
  },
  "venus|jupiter": {
    "conj": "This week life feels generous. You treat yourself and others, say yes to invitations, and enjoy good food, good company and a touch of luxury. Love grows warmer: a partner turns more affectionate, or someone new sweeps you up in a big romantic gesture. Money arrives more easily, as a bonus, a gift or a lucky find, though it leaves just as easily. You feel optimistic about the people in your life and see the best in them. Overindulgence is the only snag, from the second dessert to the expensive impulse buy you justify on the spot. Mostly, you feel lucky, loved and well fed.",
    "soft": "For a few days good things drift gently towards you. A friend offers help, a thoughtful gift arrives, or a social evening turns out far better than you expected. You feel expansive and kind, and your generosity comes back to you in small ways. Love flows easily: a date, a weekend away, a long shared laugh with your partner over nothing much. Money matters look brighter, and a sensible purchase feels satisfying rather than guilty. You are more open to people from different backgrounds, and a new friendship begins. The whole week carries a warm, unhurried glow that people around you pick up on.",
    "hard": "For a few days you want more than is good for you. Spending runs high, portions grow, and you promise more affection or time than you can give. In love you expect too much, or someone else overpromises and underdelivers, leaving you flat. You feel restless with the ordinary, craving a bigger, shinier version of your life and scrolling through other people's holidays. Friction arises over values, particularly political or moral differences with someone you care about. The excess points to a hunger for joy that your routine has been starving. When the week ends, you know which pleasures actually fed you and which only filled a gap."
  },
  "venus|neptune": {
    "conj": "This week love and beauty take on a dreamy glow. You fall for a song, a film, a face in a café, or you see your partner through soft-focus lenses. Romance feels magical, and your imagination happily fills in whatever is missing. Art, music, dance and water nourish you, and you are more compassionate than usual. The same haze leaves you open to illusion, so a charming stranger or an unrealistic purchase can lead you astray. Money turns slippery and you are never quite sure where it went. The week leaves you tender, inspired and a little starry-eyed, with a memory you keep.",
    "soft": "For a few days you feel soft, romantic and inspired. Creative work flows, whether painting, writing, cooking or putting outfits together, and you notice beauty in ordinary things like light through the curtains. Love feels tender and almost spiritual, and you forgive easily. You are drawn to help someone, and a small kindness from you means a great deal to them. A dreamy date, a concert or a day by the sea fills your heart right up. The glow lingers after the week is over, and it reminds you why you love the people and things you love.",
    "hard": "For a few days love and reality blur. You idealise someone who is not showing up, or you feel let down that a relationship falls short of the fantasy in your head. Money leaks through vague plans, late fees or a purchase that looked much better online. You are tempted to escape into romance novels, sweets, shopping or television rather than face a disappointment. Someone takes advantage of your kindness, and you notice only afterwards. The confusion reveals where you have been hoping instead of seeing. What remains afterwards is a clearer, gentler view of what you want."
  },
  "venus|northNode": {
    "conj": "This week love and pleasure point you towards your future. Someone new arrives who feels meaningful, or an existing relationship takes a step that matters for where your life is heading. You are drawn to people, places and pastimes that fit the person you are becoming. A party or a class introduces you to someone you will remember. You also notice which comforts keep you stuck in the past, like the ex you still text or the circle you have outgrown. The sweetness of these days is directional as well as pleasant, and a small choice made purely for joy shapes more than you expect.",
    "soft": "For a few days your relationships and pleasures support your growth. A friend encourages you, a group or a course feels like the right fit, or a creative project lines up with your deeper aims. Stepping into something new feels good rather than frightening. Money choices fall in line with your long-term direction, so the purchase you make is an investment in who you are becoming. Harmony comes easily with people who share your values, and you find yourself laughing with them within minutes of meeting. This is a gentle nudge forward, a stretch where love and purpose walk side by side.",
    "hard": "For a few days what feels good and what helps you grow pull apart. You crave the familiar comfort of an old relationship, an old habit or a safe social circle, even when you know it holds you back. A partner's wishes seem to clash with your path, and you feel torn between pleasing them and following your own direction. Money spent on comfort feels like a small betrayal of bigger plans, and you notice the takeaway boxes stacking up. The friction shows where your pleasures have become a hiding place. You wake one morning this week knowing it. Afterwards you choose your comforts far more deliberately."
  },
  "mars|sun": {
    "conj": "For several days your energy surges and your will runs strong. You want to act, compete and win, so you start projects, train harder at the gym and push through tasks you usually dodge. Courage rises, and you ask for what you want without apologising. Temper flares too, especially with anyone who blocks you, and arguments turn personal fast. Rushing makes you prone to bumps, spills and small cuts. The surge gives you a sense of vitality in your whole body, and it hands you the push to begin something you have waited far too long to start.",
    "soft": "This week you have energy to spare and the confidence to use it. Work gets done quickly, exercise feels great, and you take the initiative in a way people welcome rather than resist. You stand up for yourself without starting fights, so asking for a raise, leading a project or setting a boundary goes well. Physical activity lifts your mood, and a new routine sticks for once. You feel capable, alive and firmly in charge of your own life. Friends notice the spring in your step. By the end of the week you have made visible progress on something you care about.",
    "hard": "For several days you feel challenged and combative. Someone pushes against you at work or at home, and you push back hard. Your temper is short, you overwork, and your body shows the strain in tight shoulders, headaches or a sudden wave of tiredness. Ego clashes make small disagreements feel like attacks on who you are. You want to prove yourself and get frustrated when others will not cooperate. The friction shows where your drive is blocked and where you are fighting the wrong battle entirely. Once it cools, sometimes after a long run or a good night's sleep, you know which fights actually matter."
  },
  "mars|venus": {
    "conj": "This week desire runs high. Attraction is strong and immediate, and flirting turns physical quickly. You pursue what you want in love, making the first move or saying exactly what you feel. Passion can spill into arguments with your partner, yet even those crackle with spark and end in making up. Spending on pleasure climbs, mostly on impulse buys that make you feel attractive. Creative energy is lively, and you want to make something beautiful with your own hands. You feel alive, wanted and hungry for more, and the people around you feel that heat too.",
    "soft": "For a few days love and desire flow together. Romance feels exciting yet easy, and your partner or someone new responds warmly to your advances. You feel attractive and confident, so a date or a night out goes well from the first drink. Creative and social projects get a boost from your energy. Money you earn through effort comes in smoothly, from a side job or a sale. You are affectionate and playful, and your charm carries an edge people find hard to resist. The days feel warm, lively and full of pleasure, with laughter spilling late into the evening.",
    "hard": "For several days passion and harmony clash. You want closeness, yet arguments with a partner flare over small things like money, chores or who is on their phone at dinner. Jealousy or frustrated desire surfaces, and you feel it in your body as restlessness. You spend on impulse to fill a gap, then regret it when the parcel arrives. Someone you are attracted to plays hot and cold, and it gets under your skin. The tension shows where your needs and your partner's needs are out of step. Out of the sparks comes a much clearer grasp of your own desires."
  },
  "mars|saturn": {
    "conj": "For several days you feel like you are driving with the handbrake on. Effort meets resistance: a project stalls, a boss says no, your body is tired just when you need it most. Frustration builds, and you feel angry at rules, delays and the people who enforce them. Yet this is also a time of disciplined effort, when slow, steady work pays off. You finish the tedious job, stick to the training plan and prove your stamina to yourself. The pressure is heavy, but it shows you what you can build with patience, and you end the week proud of what you carried.",
    "soft": "This week your energy is focused and your effort efficient. You work steadily, plan carefully and finish what you start, which feels unusually satisfying. Physical training, practical jobs around the house and long projects go well because you pace yourself instead of sprinting. Authority figures respect your diligence, and a boss or mentor notices how hard you have been working. You feel competent and grounded, with none of the usual rush. Setbacks that would normally rattle you barely register. The progress you make is solid and lasting, the kind that still stands months from now.",
    "hard": "For several days your drive keeps hitting walls. Deadlines press, rules block you, and someone in charge seems determined to slow you down. Frustration turns into irritability or a heavy, stuck feeling in your limbs. Pushing harder only makes it worse, and strains or small injuries show up if you ignore fatigue. You feel tested and underpowered, snapping at the queue or the slow website. The friction reveals where you have been forcing things that need time instead. When it eases, you know which efforts deserve the struggle, and you drop the rest with relief."
  },
  "mars|pluto": {
    "conj": "For several days your drive turns intense and all-consuming. You want to transform something now: clear the house, end the argument, overhaul your fitness overnight. Power struggles arise, and you meet them head-on, sometimes too fiercely. Desire runs deep and physical, and you know exactly what you want. You can be ruthless in pursuit of a goal, and other people feel your force before you say a word. The intensity is exhausting, and you sleep hard afterwards. It also gives you the strength to tackle something you have been afraid of for a long time, and you tackle it.",
    "soft": "This week you draw on deep reserves of energy. You tackle a big project, dig into research, or push through a hard workout with surprising stamina. Your will is strong but controlled, so you get things done without drama or fuss. Situations that usually intimidate you, like confronting a landlord or asking for what you are owed, feel manageable. You can clear out, repair or rebuild something that has been broken for months. People sense your quiet strength and step aside. You feel powerful, focused and fully able to change what needs changing in your own life.",
    "hard": "For several days you run into power struggles. Someone tries to dominate, corner or manipulate you, and your anger rises sharply and stays. Conflicts escalate quickly, and a disagreement about a small thing turns into a standoff. You feel compulsive, unable to let something go, checking their messages or rehearsing the argument at three in the morning. Stress builds in your jaw, your stomach, your sleep. The friction exposes where control and fear shape your choices. When the pressure passes you have a far clearer sense of your own strength and where its limits lie."
  },
  "mars|asc": {
    "conj": "For several days you come across as bold, energetic and direct. People notice your drive, and you take the lead without thinking twice. Physical energy runs high, so exercise, dancing or a hands-on project suits you perfectly. Your temper is quick, and you snap at anyone who slows you down in traffic or at the till. Minor bumps, cuts and rushed mistakes are more likely than usual. You look flushed, alive and ready for anything. Overall you feel strong in your body, impatient with waiting, and eager to make things happen on your own terms.",
    "soft": "This week you feel physically lively and sure of yourself. You take initiative easily, start conversations with strangers, and put yourself forward for new things. Exercise feels good, and your body responds well to effort, whether that is a longer run or a heavier lift. People see you as capable and energetic, and you enjoy the attention. Small decisions come quickly and turn out well. You carry yourself differently, straighter and more purposeful. Any fresh start that needs a push, from a new sport to a new job, gets going easily now, and you surprise yourself with how much you get done before the week is out.",
    "hard": "For several days other people push against you and you push back. A partner, client or rival challenges you, and arguments become heated before you notice. You feel irritable and restless in your body, and tension shows in your jaw and shoulders. Rushing leads to clumsiness: a stubbed toe, a dropped glass, a sharp word you did not mean. Sparring with the people closest to you feels oddly compulsive. The friction shows where you need to stand your ground and where you are simply reacting. Afterwards you understand your own fire better, and how to aim it."
  },
  "jupiter|uranus": {
    "conj": "For a few weeks Jupiter sits on your natal Uranus, and the part of you that has always wanted something unusual gets a gust of wind behind it. You sign up for the course, book the solo trip or tell your manager you want to work differently, sometimes before you have thought it through. Lucky breaks arrive sideways: an unexpected email, a chance meeting at a party, an offer from someone you barely know. Routines that felt tolerable last month now fit like a coat two sizes too small. The trap is leaping for the thrill alone, so the freedom lasts only as long as the novelty. Something genuinely new starts here, and the version of you that walks out of these weeks is freer.",
    "soft": "Over the next few weeks change comes to you on good terms. A new app, a different working pattern or an idea from a younger friend clicks into place, and you adapt without the usual resistance. You feel lighter about being a little different: you wear the odd jacket, voice the unpopular opinion at dinner, and people like you more for it. Opportunities turn up through networks, online groups or a friend of a friend, often at short notice. The only catch is that easy excitement scatters you across five fresh projects at once. Chosen well, one of these openings reshapes your year and gives you room to breathe.",
    "hard": "For several weeks the pressure to break free builds faster than you can manage it. You wake up certain that the job, the flat or the arrangement with your partner has to change today, and every small rule grates. Plans shift at the last minute, people cancel, and the freedom you crave arrives in untidy bursts. You overreach, announcing a radical change to friends before checking whether it is workable. Other people push back, and part of you enjoys the argument more than you admit. Beneath the noise is a signal: some corner of your life has grown too narrow. Whatever change survives the excitement is the one worth keeping."
  },
  "jupiter|neptune": {
    "conj": "For a few weeks Jupiter meets your natal Neptune, and your inner life opens like a window in summer. Dreams turn vivid, a song in the supermarket brings you close to tears, and you feel unusually tender towards strangers. You give generously, sometimes too generously: the loan to a friend, the extra evenings for a cause, the benefit of the doubt to someone who has not earned it. Faith returns, whether in a spiritual practice, a creative project or simply the sense that things work out. Boundaries go soft, and a plan that looks luminous at midnight looks thinner over breakfast. What you gain is real all the same: a wider sense of meaning, and proof that your imagination is one of your strongest assets.",
    "soft": "Through these weeks inspiration arrives in small doses and stays. You notice small synchronicities, the book that falls open at the right page, the friend who calls just as you think of them, and they feel less like coincidence than guidance. Creative work flows: sketching, writing, playing music or rearranging a room becomes absorbing in a way that restores you. Compassion comes easily, and someone who is struggling feels safe telling you so. Your read on people is sharp, and a hunch about a job or a place proves right. Rest does you more good than usual, so an unplanned Sunday afternoon is time well spent. You come out of it gentler and more certain of what you believe.",
    "hard": "For several weeks hope and reality drift apart. You fall for a plan, a person or a promise that sounds wonderful, and the small print stays blurry until you have already said yes. Money leaks through generosity or vague arrangements, and a friend's favour quietly becomes your responsibility. Tiredness settles in, and escape looks tempting: an extra glass of wine, one more episode, a daydream about moving abroad. Other people's versions of events contradict yours, and it is hard to tell who is fooling whom. Your idealism is sincere, which is exactly why each small disappointment stings. Once the fog lifts, you know precisely which dreams are yours to follow."
  },
  "jupiter|pluto": {
    "conj": "For a few weeks Jupiter lands on your natal Pluto, and your ambition grows teeth. You want more influence and more control over your own direction, and you notice all the places you have been playing small. A chance to lead, invest or take on a bigger role comes up, and you feel ready in a way that surprises you. Conversations go deep fast: a friend confides something heavy over coffee, or you say out loud what you want from your career. Power struggles flare, because others sense your intensity and some of them resist it. Handled with integrity, this is one of the strongest windows you get for lasting growth, and its results outlive the transit by years.",
    "soft": "Over these weeks you find the leverage you have been missing. A conversation with the right person, a well-timed investment or a quiet decision to stop tolerating something shifts your circumstances in your favour. You see through office politics and know exactly whom to trust. Therapy, research or a late-night talk with your partner goes further than usual, and something long buried becomes easier to handle. Resources gather around you: a loan approved, a mentor stepping in, a skill you forgot you had. Nothing about it is flashy, yet the ground under you grows firmer. When Jupiter moves on, you hold more power over your own life than you did before.",
    "hard": "For several weeks your appetite for more runs into other people's appetite for control. A negotiation turns into a standoff, a boss tests your loyalty, or a relative uses money as leverage. You feel the pull to win at all costs, and you catch yourself pushing harder than the situation deserves. Obsession sits close by: checking the account balance, replaying the argument in the car, refusing to let a small slight go. This friction exposes where you have handed your power away and now want it back. A deal struck in anger this month costs you later. Played fairly, the struggle leaves you stronger, clearer and much harder to push around."
  },
  "jupiter|chiron": {
    "conj": "For a few weeks Jupiter sits on your natal Chiron, and an old hurt comes back into view, this time with room around it. You find yourself telling a story about your childhood or an early failure and, for once, it does not choke you. Help arrives in the right shape: a good counsellor, a book that names your experience, a friend who says they went through the same thing. You notice how often your wound has made you kind, and how many people come to you precisely because you understand. Some days the growth feels like pressing on a bruise. Even so, this is a chance to heal something and turn it into a gift you can offer others.",
    "soft": "Through these weeks healing comes more easily than you expect. A conversation with a sibling, a new teacher or a body practice like swimming or yoga eases a tension you have carried for years. You end up mentoring someone, and in helping them you understand your own history better. Old insecurities about your looks, your intelligence or your place in the family lose some of their grip. People trust you with their own soft spots, sensing you will not judge. A course, a support group or a trip somewhere meaningful turns out to be more restorative than you planned. Much of what you learn about yourself now becomes something you pass on.",
    "hard": "For several weeks something tender gets pressed in public. Praise for a colleague lands like criticism of you, or a new opportunity wakes the old voice that says you are not good enough. You overcompensate, taking on too much, giving advice nobody asked for, or insisting you are fine when you are not. Doctors, teachers and advisers disappoint, and you feel let down by the very people meant to help. The ache is real, and pretending otherwise only makes it louder. This pressure shows you where the wound still steers your choices. Seen clearly, it loosens, and you leave these weeks with a more honest story about yourself."
  },
  "saturn|uranus": {
    "conj": "For the next few months Saturn sits on your natal Uranus, and the part of you that craves freedom meets a wall of responsibility. Everyone born within a year or two of you feels this, yet for you it lands in specific places: a job that now needs full commitment, a relationship asking for a clearer shape, a rebellion that has run its course. You feel restless and hemmed in, sometimes on the same afternoon. The temptation is to bolt, quitting on a Monday because the routine has become unbearable. The better path is slower: building a structure that fits the person you are becoming. Your independence comes out of these months with a foundation under it.",
    "soft": "Over these months you find a sensible way to make an unusual idea work. The side project gets a business plan, the career change gets a timetable, and a wild notion becomes something you can actually do on a Tuesday. You share this steadying influence with people born around your year, and in your life it shows as older colleagues taking your originality seriously and helping you give it form. You feel secure enough to experiment without risking everything. A new system or working pattern settles in and makes daily life easier. Change here is gradual rather than dramatic, which is why it lasts. When Saturn moves on, your freedom rests on something solid.",
    "hard": "For several months the old and the new pull at you from opposite ends. Part of you wants to keep the job, the mortgage and the familiar shape of things, while another part wants to tear it all up. Rules at work tighten just as you most need flexibility, or a partner asks for commitment when you feel least ready. Your nerves run high, and tension shows as sleepless nights, a stiff neck or a short fuse in queues. You swing between rebelling and giving in, and neither feels right. The harder work is renegotiating the terms of your life rather than smashing them. Once this passes, you hold a freedom that is sturdier and far more your own."
  },
  "saturn|neptune": {
    "conj": "For the next few months Saturn presses on your natal Neptune, a meeting you share with most people born around your year, and your dreams are asked to prove themselves. The novel you have always meant to write, the spiritual practice you talk about, the plan to live by the sea: each gets tested against time, money and effort. Some fade, and there is a quiet grief in letting them go. Others become more real than ever, because you give them a schedule. You tire more easily, and escapes that used to soothe you no longer work. What remains when the fog clears is a smaller set of dreams, and every one of them is buildable.",
    "soft": "Over these months imagination and discipline finally cooperate. You commit to the painting class every Thursday, turn a vague spiritual interest into a steady practice, or put structure behind a charity you care about. Dreams you once filed under someday get a practical first step, and it feels natural rather than forced. Sleep improves when you respect a routine, and quiet evenings recharge you properly. You become the calm, reliable one for a friend who is struggling, compassionate without being swallowed. Nothing dramatic happens, yet your ideals grow roots. You trust your inner vision more now, because you have watched it survive contact with real life.",
    "hard": "For several months reality keeps puncturing your illusions, one small pinprick at a time. A job you believed in turns out to be less than it seemed, or someone you idealised shows an ordinary, disappointing side. Confusion about duty runs through the days: you feel obliged to rescue people, then resentful when you do. Energy dips, and you reach for escapes, scrolling late into the night or staying in bed longer than you meant to. Contracts, health routines and money need clear eyes, because vagueness costs you now. You share the wider mood of this transit with people your age, yet the disillusionment in your own life is specific and honest. Whatever you still believe in afterwards is worth believing in."
  },
  "saturn|pluto": {
    "conj": "For the next few months Saturn sits on your natal Pluto, and the deepest pressures in your life become impossible to ignore. People born around your year feel this together, yet your version has its own names and faces: the job you have outgrown, the family pattern you keep repeating, the debt or the power imbalance you have lived with too long. Things end, sometimes firmly, and you feel the weight of that. You are also unusually strong, capable of hard decisions, long hours and saying no without apologising. The work is heavy, slow and serious. Built through it is a kind of authority over your own life that nobody can take away.",
    "soft": "Over these months you have the stamina to change something fundamental, steadily and without drama. You pay down the debt, finish the long therapy, restructure the business or set firm terms with a difficult relative, and it holds. People with power notice your seriousness and hand you responsibility. You feel focused, even formidable, and distractions lose their pull. Control comes from patience rather than force, which surprises you. There is little glamour in the process, only a growing sense that you are in charge. The change you make now sits deep, like new foundations poured under an old house.",
    "hard": "For several months the pressure on your life feels relentless. An employer, an institution or someone close to you pushes hard, and you push back just as hard, until it becomes a test of who breaks first. A job, a relationship or a financial arrangement reaches the point where something has to give. You feel cornered, or you catch your own controlling side in a way that is uncomfortable to watch. Fear rises at night: of loss, of failure, of what happens if you let go. Much of your age group is under this same weight, but the battle in your life is personal, and it shows you what you are made of. What survives these months is fireproof, and you know exactly what you will no longer tolerate."
  },
  "saturn|chiron": {
    "conj": "For the next several months Saturn sits on your natal Chiron, and an old wound asks for grown-up attention. You recognise how a childhood fear still shapes your working life: over-preparing, refusing help, feeling like a fraud in meetings. A doctor's appointment, a long talk with a parent or a performance review brings the pattern into sharp focus. The feeling is heavy and sometimes lonely. You also find the patience to deal with it properly, through a therapist, a steady routine or a mentor who has walked the same road. The hurt does not vanish, but it gains a structure around it, and you can use it to help others.",
    "soft": "Over these months you find practical ways to tend an old hurt. A regular session with a physio, a course that fills a gap you were once ashamed of, or a weekly call with an older friend steadies you. Responsibility, which used to feel crushing, now feels like proof that you can cope. You become a reliable guide for someone younger who struggles with something you know well. Your self-doubt shrinks each time you finish what you start. Healing here is unglamorous, a matter of turning up again and again. The habits you build now carry you for years, and you feel more competent in your own skin.",
    "hard": "For several months life presses on your most sensitive spots. A setback at work echoes an old failure, a critic sounds uncannily like a parent, or your body insists on rest you did not want to give it. You feel inadequate, and the urge is to work twice as hard or give up entirely. Old shame surfaces in ordinary moments: filling out a form, waiting for a reply, hearing a colleague praised. Nobody seems to make it easier, and some make it harder. The pressure forces a reckoning you have avoided for years. You face the wound squarely this time, and it stops running your decisions in the dark."
  },
  "uranus|neptune": {
    "conj": "Uranus crosses your natal Neptune about once in a lifetime, and your birth year decides when: many meet it in childhood or youth, others not until old age. When it arrives, for a year or more and alongside your whole age group, your inner world gets rewired. What you believe, how you pray or meditate, the art that moves you, the dream you hold for your life: all of it wakes up. Sudden insights arrive in the shower or on a train, and a chance encounter reshapes your creative or spiritual direction. Old illusions crack open, sometimes shockingly, and you see through a person or a cause you once idealised. Sleep turns light and your nerves run close to the surface. The awakening is real, and you come out with a clearer, freer vision of what matters to you.",
    "soft": "For a year or more Uranus opens a clear line to your natal Neptune, a contact shared by people born around your time, and your imagination gets a jolt of fresh air. You take up something unexpected: a meditation retreat, digital art, a new language, a community that thinks differently. Intuition sharpens, and hunches about people or places prove right with uncanny timing. Spiritual or creative habits that had gone stale are easy to drop. Ideals feel practical for once, and you find ways to live them in small daily choices, from what you buy to how you spend Sunday mornings. Looking back, this is when your inner life became more your own.",
    "hard": "Uranus grinds against your natal Neptune for a year or more, as it does for most people born within a few years of you, and the beliefs you have leaned on start to wobble. A cause, a teacher, a relationship or a dream you trusted shows cracks, and the disappointment arrives abruptly. You feel unsettled, flitting between excitement about something new and confusion about what is real. Sleep runs lighter, and anxiety shows up as scattered thoughts at three in the morning. Escapism beckons, and so does a sudden conversion to the next shiny philosophy. Underneath the upheaval, you are shedding a vision of life that no longer fits. Your beliefs come out of it less comforting, and far more honest."
  },
  "uranus|pluto": {
    "conj": "Uranus crosses your natal Pluto at most once in a lifetime, in childhood for some generations and not until later life for others. When it comes, for a year or more and shared with everyone born near you, your deepest drives are jolted awake. Situations you thought were settled break open fast: a job ends, a secret surfaces, a relationship reaches its turning point overnight. You feel an electric urge to change your life at the root and very little patience for anything that holds you back. Power shifts around you, sometimes in your favour, sometimes not. The shocks are real and occasionally frightening. Each one clears away something that was blocking you, and the person who emerges has far more freedom and force than before.",
    "soft": "For a year or more Uranus supports your natal Pluto, a current running through your whole age group, and deep change becomes possible without catastrophe. You break a compulsive habit, leave a controlling situation or take a bold financial step, and it works more smoothly than you feared. New technology, new people or a surprising offer give you leverage you did not have before. Insight arrives in flashes: one evening you suddenly see why you have repeated a pattern for twenty years. You feel brave, curious and strangely calm about transformation. Change here is radical in effect but gentle in delivery, and part of your life is rebuilt from the ground up.",
    "hard": "Upheaval runs through your life on several fronts at once while Uranus pushes against your natal Pluto, a stretch of a year or more. Your generation feels this pressure together, but you meet it in particular crises: a sudden job loss, a rupture with family, a hidden power struggle forced into the open. You feel volatile, capable of drastic decisions made in a single sleepless night. Control slips from your hands, and grabbing for it makes things worse. Stress lives in your body as clenched shoulders and restless sleep. Still, the crisis breaks a stranglehold that has held you for years. Everything you rebuild from the rubble is unmistakably yours."
  },
  "uranus|chiron": {
    "conj": "For many months, often more than a year, Uranus sits on your natal Chiron, and an old wound is suddenly lit up. A remark, a medical result or a reunion with someone from school throws you straight back into a feeling you thought you had outgrown. The difference now is that you see it clearly, often in a single startling flash. You try unconventional help: a new kind of therapy, bodywork, a support community online. Some days you feel raw and exposed. Others bring a surprising freedom, as if you no longer have to carry the hurt in the old way. Seeing your wound this way makes you a more original healer for others.",
    "soft": "Over many months Uranus eases your natal Chiron, and healing arrives from unexpected places. A new friend, an unusual practitioner or a podcast you stumbled on names something you have felt for years. You experiment with how you look after yourself, and some of it works remarkably well. Old embarrassment about being different starts to feel like a signature rather than a flaw. You find yourself helping others in unconventional ways, sharing your story openly online or in a group. The shifts come in bursts rather than steady progress, but each one sticks. You leave this period freer from an old limitation than you thought possible.",
    "hard": "For many months Uranus jolts your natal Chiron, and old hurts return without warning. A sudden change at work, a health scare or a break with a friend reopens a wound you thought had closed. Your nerves fray, and you swing between wanting to fix everything at once and wanting to run from all of it. Help feels unreliable: advisers contradict each other, appointments get cancelled, the group chat goes quiet when you need it. You rebel against the careful ways you once coped. The shock breaks a pattern that kept you small and quietly hurting. You carry the old wound differently afterwards, more openly and with far less shame."
  },
  "neptune|uranus": {
    "conj": "Neptune reaches your natal Uranus only in some generations: people born from the mid 1990s onwards meet it in childhood or youth, and for anyone born earlier it never arrives. When it does, it lasts several years and your urge for freedom goes soft at the edges. Instead of rebelling loudly, you drift towards quieter forms of independence: art, spirituality, a gentler way of living. Plans for radical change blur, and it is harder to say exactly what you are breaking away from. Intuition becomes your guide, sometimes accurate, sometimes wishful. Your nerves are more sensitive and your dreams stranger. Over time you discover that liberation does not always need a fight, and you find a more inspired way to be different.",
    "soft": "For a year or more Neptune flows kindly to your natal Uranus, something you share with people born around your time, and your originality finds a dreamier voice. Ideas arrive through music, dreams or long walks rather than debate. You feel drawn to communities built on shared ideals: a creative collective, a volunteering project, an online circle of kindred spirits. Changes happen gently, almost without you noticing, like a shift in taste or a new way of spending Sundays. Your sense of where things are heading is unusually good, and you act on it without fuss. Nothing is forced or dramatic, and your life widens gracefully all the same.",
    "hard": "Neptune clouds your natal Uranus for a year or more, as it does for most of your age group, and the path to freedom goes misty. You want change but cannot name it, or you chase a vision of escape that dissolves as you get close. Unreliable people and vague plans slip into your days: a partner who drifts, a promised new job that never quite materialises. Restlessness turns inward as unease, a low hum under ordinary afternoons. Deception, including self-deception, is the particular hazard now. The confusion clears away rebellions that were never yours. A quieter, truer sense of your own independence is what stays."
  },
  "neptune|pluto": {
    "conj": "Neptune will not reach your natal Pluto in this lifetime: for everyone alive today it already runs well ahead of where Pluto stood at your birth, and catching up would take well over a century. What you feel instead is the long, quiet conversation between the two, through the sextiles, squares and trines Neptune makes to your Pluto over the decades. In those years old obsessions and fears lose their hard edges, and you forgive people you once held onto tightly. A dream that stays with you for days, a grief that opens into compassion, an evening of music that undoes you: inner experiences hit harder than they used to. Power over your life comes less from control and more from letting go. Slowly, something in you is transformed at the root.",
    "soft": "Across a long stretch of years Neptune supports your natal Pluto, a gentle current your whole generation lives through, and deep change arrives through understanding rather than struggle. You find healing in places you did not expect: a choir, a walk by the sea every morning, a long friendship that finally feels safe. Old compulsions loosen their grip without a fight. You read hidden motives in people easily, and you meet them with compassion rather than suspicion. Creative or spiritual work reaches unusual depth, and you are moved by what you make. Nothing about this period is loud, yet the part of you that once needed control learns to trust.",
    "hard": "For a long stretch of years Neptune erodes the ground under your natal Pluto, a tension your whole age group feels, and the certainties you built on start to slip. Power structures you trusted, whether a company, a faith or a family arrangement, prove shakier than they looked. You sense undercurrents you cannot quite name, and suspicion creeps into quiet moments, like lying awake wondering what a friend really meant. Exhaustion and escapism are real hazards. The pull is to hold on even harder, which only tightens the confusion. The dissolving does its slow work regardless, clearing away what was false. Any trust you keep has been tested by years of fog, and it holds."
  },
  "neptune|chiron": {
    "conj": "Neptune rests on your natal Chiron for a year or more, and an old wound becomes both more tender and more open to healing. You weep at films, feel the sadness of strangers on the bus, and recognise your own pain in other people's stories. Confusion about what really happened to you surfaces, memories blurring or changing shape. Music, prayer or creative work helps more than analysis does. Some healers and remedies promise more than they deliver, and you learn to tell the difference. Through all of it compassion grows, and you begin to see your wound as something you share with many others.",
    "soft": "Over a long stretch Neptune softens your natal Chiron, and healing arrives through gentleness. A retreat, a choir, a meditation class or a quiet friendship eases pain you have carried for years. You forgive someone, or yourself, without a big conversation, simply because the grudge has gone. Your empathy deepens, and people come to you in their hardest moments, the late phone call, the tearful coffee. Art you make now carries unusual emotional depth. Sleep and dreams become places of repair rather than worry. The wound still exists, yet it no longer defines your inner weather.",
    "hard": "For a long stretch Neptune blurs the edges of your natal Chiron, and old pain returns in confusing forms. You feel vaguely low or unwell without a clear reason, and advice from doctors, friends or healers contradicts itself. You are drawn to rescuers, or to rescuing others, and both leave you drained. Victimhood beckons, with its story in which nothing you do matters. Wine, fantasy or endless scrolling offer relief that does not last past the evening. Under the haze, you are learning to feel your wound fully rather than numbing it. Slowly the haze thins, leaving a kinder understanding of yourself."
  },
  "pluto|uranus": {
    "conj": "For several years Pluto grinds slowly over your natal Uranus, a contact shared by everyone born within a few years of you, and your idea of freedom is remade from the inside. What once felt like independence, a job, a habit, a way of standing apart, now feels shallow. You want deep, lasting change, not a new haircut and a different playlist. Struggles arise around your autonomy, with employers, partners or institutions that expect you to fit. Some doors close abruptly and permanently. In their place grows a stronger, more determined version of your originality, one willing to pay the real cost of being free.",
    "soft": "For a long stretch of years Pluto supports your natal Uranus, a slow tide your whole age group shares, and radical change becomes something you can steer. You take on bold projects, rebuild your working life or reinvent how you live, and the changes hold. Insight into your own patterns arrives with calm force, often while doing something ordinary like cooking or driving. People with influence notice your originality and back it. You feel less need to shock and more drive to transform. Change unfolds deliberately over months rather than in sudden bursts. The reinvention of these years sets the shape of your life for a long time to come.",
    "hard": "For years Pluto presses hard on your natal Uranus, as it does for your whole generation, and the tension between control and freedom sits at the centre of your life. Jobs, relationships or institutions demand compliance, and something in you flatly refuses. You feel pushed towards drastic moves: quitting, leaving, breaking a contract, cutting someone off. At other times you are the one gripping the wheel, and the effort exhausts you. The pressure builds slowly for months, then breaks in a single week. Each crisis strips away a false kind of independence. The freedom you hold at the far end is hard-won, and nobody can talk you out of it."
  },
  "pluto|neptune": {
    "conj": "For many years Pluto sits slowly on your natal Neptune, a passage your whole age group shares, and your beliefs and dreams are transformed at the root. Illusions you did not know you held come to light, often painfully, and you let go of a spiritual path, a romantic ideal or a fantasy of being rescued. Your imagination deepens, drawn to darker and truer themes in the books you read and the art you make. Grief and awakening arrive together, sometimes in the same conversation. You sense undercurrents in people and rooms with uncanny accuracy. Your faith is stripped back to its essentials, and it becomes fiercely your own.",
    "soft": "Across a long stretch of years Pluto supports your natal Neptune, a steady current your generation lives through together, and your ideals gain power. A creative, spiritual or humanitarian vision takes root and grows. You turn intuition into something tangible: a practice, a body of work, a way of caring for others that people come to rely on. Compulsions tied to escape loosen, and you choose depth over distraction, the long book over the endless feed. You feel drawn to what is authentic and repelled by the fake. This is steady transformation rather than upheaval. Your dreams carry weight now, and people take them seriously.",
    "hard": "For years Pluto pressures your natal Neptune, as it does for most people born near you, and your illusions come under slow, relentless scrutiny. A belief system, a guru, a romantic fantasy or a flattering idea of who you are collapses, and it hurts. You feel disoriented, cynical some weeks and desperate to cling to what is falling away in others. Secrecy, addiction or manipulation surfaces, in your own habits or in someone close to you. The pressure exposes what is hollow, and nothing false survives it. Friends notice you have less patience for pretence and more for honesty. What remains is a harder-won faith, cleaner and truer than the one you started with."
  },
  "pluto|chiron": {
    "conj": "Pluto settles on your natal Chiron for a year or more, and your oldest wound is brought fully into the light. Memories, patterns or grief you had buried surface with force, sometimes through a crisis, a loss or a relationship that mirrors the past almost exactly. You feel exposed and raw in ways that are hard to explain, even to the people closest to you. Therapy goes deep, old shame loses its power, and you reclaim parts of yourself you gave up long ago. The process is slow and demanding, with weeks when you simply want it to stop. Afterwards your wound becomes a source of strength and hard-earned insight.",
    "soft": "Over a long stretch Pluto supports your natal Chiron, and deep healing becomes possible without breakdown. You find the right therapist, the right community or the right practice, and progress is steady. Old wounds lose their charge, and you start telling your story openly, at a friend's kitchen table or in a room of strangers, often helping others as you do. You feel stronger, clearer and less defined by what happened to you. Power grows through vulnerability rather than defence. The transformation is quiet but profound. You come out of it with a healed relationship to your past and a new sense of purpose.",
    "hard": "For a long stretch Pluto presses on your natal Chiron, and old pain returns with full intensity. Crises at work, in your health or in love reopen wounds you thought had closed, and you feel powerless in painfully familiar ways. Shame and anger rise, along with a sense of being punished by life for reasons you cannot see. Bosses, institutions or partners exercise control in ways that echo your past, down to the tone of voice. The pressure forces you to confront the wound at its root rather than around its edges. What seemed unbearable turns, slowly, into resilience. You come to know your wound intimately, and it loses its hold over you."
  },
  "chiron|uranus": {
    "conj": "For many months Chiron sits on your natal Uranus, and the old sore spot around being different starts to ache again. You catch how often you have shrunk your oddness to fit a room, laughing along at a joke about people like you, or keeping the unusual plan to yourself. Sudden events touch this nerve: a restructure at work, a friend group that drifts apart, a meeting where you are the only one who sees things a certain way. It feels lonely and unsettling, as if the ground keeps shifting just when you have found your footing. Yet this is also when you stop apologising for how your mind works. Something you once hid, a talent, an identity, a strange idea, becomes the very thing people come to you for.",
    "soft": "Over these many months Chiron makes an easy angle to your Uranus, and healing arrives through freedom rather than effort. You find yourself drawn to people who think sideways: a new online community, an unconventional teacher, a friend who takes up something no one expected. Talking openly about what once made you feel like an outsider suddenly feels possible, even light, and someone thanks you for saying it first. Small experiments help more than long analysis, whether that is a different way of working, a bold haircut or a trip you plan alone. Old restlessness finally has somewhere useful to go. You come out of this stretch more at ease with your own originality, and less braced for other people's surprise.",
    "hard": "Change seems to find the tender places while Chiron grinds against your Uranus for many months. A plan collapses without warning, a relationship shifts shape, or a sudden decision by someone else leaves you exposed and out of step. Part of you wants to bolt, to quit the job or cut the tie before anyone can hurt you further, and another part fears any change at all. Both come from the same old bruise about not belonging. Conversations turn prickly when people call you difficult or strange, even in jest. Underneath the jolts, a lifelong habit of either rebelling or hiding is being loosened. What grows in its place is a steadier independence, one that no longer needs a fight to prove itself."
  },
  "chiron|neptune": {
    "conj": "Chiron spends many months on your natal Neptune, and old longings surface with a softness that is hard to bear. You tear up at a song playing in the supermarket, or dream vividly of someone you lost years ago. Disappointments you thought were filed away come back: the rescuer role you played in the family, the partner you idealised, the faith that let you down. Boundaries thin, so other people's pain seeps into you and you come home drained without knowing why. Escapes look tempting on grey evenings, an extra glass of wine, endless scrolling, sleeping late. Alongside the ache runs a gift. Compassion deepens, creative or spiritual work gains a new honesty, and you begin to forgive yourself for having hoped so much.",
    "soft": "For many months Chiron flows kindly with your Neptune, and healing slips in through quiet, almost invisible doors. You find yourself at a yoga class, in a choir, on a long walk by the sea, and come home lighter than you left. Someone shares a story that mirrors your own, and the shame you carried about it begins to dissolve. Intuition sharpens, so you sense who needs a message before they reach out, and you are right more often than not. Creative work draws on old sadness without drowning in it: a song, a painting, a page in a notebook that says what you never could. This gentle stretch restores some faith in life and in your own tenderness.",
    "hard": "Old confusion around trust, rescue and disappointment rises to the surface as Chiron presses on your Neptune for many months. You see how quickly you give someone the benefit of the doubt, then feel foolish when the promise dissolves. A friend leans on you heavily, or you catch yourself waiting for a partner, a guru or a plan to make everything right. Fatigue and vagueness creep in, and telling intuition from wishful thinking gets harder. The pull towards numbing yourself is strong at the end of a long day. Slowly this period teaches honesty about what you see rather than what you hope. Your compassion comes out of it cleaner, less mixed with self-sacrifice, and far harder to exploit."
  },
  "chiron|pluto": {
    "conj": "For many months Chiron sits right on your natal Pluto, and the oldest wound you carry reaches down into your depths. Situations stir raw feelings about power: a boss who controls, a relative who manipulates, a loss that brings back every earlier loss. You notice how fiercely you guard yourself, and how quickly you go cold when trust is broken. Dreams turn intense, and buried memories rise without being asked, sometimes in the middle of an ordinary afternoon. This is heavy, slow work, and there are weeks when nothing seems to move. Still, something fundamental is being composted. You emerge with a quieter, deeper strength, able to sit with other people's darkness without flinching.",
    "soft": "Deep healing becomes possible without a crisis forcing it while Chiron makes a supportive angle to your Pluto over many months. You feel ready to look at what you have avoided for years: a family secret, a pattern of control, the grief you never fully let out. Therapy, a long honest conversation or a book that names your experience lands at exactly the right time. People in pain sense your steadiness and confide in you, and you find you can hold their story without being swallowed by it. Old fears loosen their grip in small ways, like sleeping better or letting someone help with the heavy lifting. By the time Chiron moves on you carry a new kind of power, rooted in having faced yourself.",
    "hard": "Chiron squares or opposes your Pluto for many months, and the old wound collides with your need for control. Power struggles flare with people who echo someone from your past: a partner who withholds, a manager who holds all the cards, a relative who knows exactly where to press. You feel the pull either to dominate the situation or to vanish from it entirely. Jealousy, suspicion or grief arrive stronger than the moment seems to justify, which is the clue that something older is speaking. Some endings come in this period, and they hurt. Beneath the friction, a long buried pattern of self-protection is being exposed and worn down. Afterwards you carry less armour and far more resilience."
  },
  "northNode|sun": {
    "conj": "For a few months the transiting North Node crosses your Sun, and life starts pointing you towards who you are becoming. Opportunities arrive that feel oddly fated: a role offered out of the blue, a person who sees your potential before you do, a move that clicks into place. You feel a hunger to be seen for yourself rather than for what you do for others. Some of these doors are uncomfortable, because they ask you to step forward when you would rather stay useful in the background. People you meet in this stretch tend to matter for years. You come out of it with a clearer sense of direction, and a self that feels more like your own.",
    "soft": "Growth feels natural rather than forced while the North Node makes an easy angle to your Sun over the coming months. Invitations fit you: a course that suits your strengths, a colleague who wants to collaborate, a friend who connects you with exactly the right person. Saying what you want from life gets easier, and people take you seriously when you do. Small choices, like accepting a lunch or volunteering for a project, lead further than expected. There is a sense of being on your path without having to push. Confidence grows steadily, so that by the end you stand a little taller in rooms that once intimidated you.",
    "hard": "For a few months the transiting South Node sits on your Sun, with the North Node opposite, and this is a season of release. Parts of your identity that once fitted now feel stale: a job title, your role in the family, the version of yourself you perform at parties. You grow tired of being the one everyone expects things from, and some people and situations quietly fall away. It feels like losing ground when others seem to be racing ahead. Partners and close allies take up more of your attention, sometimes demanding, sometimes offering what you could never find alone. Letting go is the work here, and it is not always graceful. The self left standing is less rehearsed and more true."
  },
  "northNode|moon": {
    "conj": "Your emotional life turns in a direction that feels meant as the North Node crosses your Moon for a few months. Home and family come to the fore: a move, a new closeness with a parent, a baby in the family, or simply the sense that your flat no longer fits. Feelings arrive strongly and ask to be honoured rather than managed. Someone new becomes important quickly, almost as if you have known them before. The pull is towards a kind of nurture and belonging you have not quite let yourself have. Needing things this openly feels exposing. Yet the growth of this period happens exactly there, in letting yourself be cared for as well as caring.",
    "soft": "Over the coming months the North Node makes a gentle angle to your Moon, and emotional growth arrives through ordinary life. A chat at the kitchen table, a friend who drops round with soup, a slow Sunday with family: these small moments start to feel important. Naming what you need, and asking for it without apology, becomes easier. Caring figures in your life, often women, offer support or advice that moves you along. Moods settle, and your instincts about people become sharp and reliable. Home turns into more of a refuge, and your inner life starts to line up with the direction you want to take.",
    "hard": "Old emotional habits come up to be let go while the South Node sits on your Moon for a few months. You slip into the familiar role at home without meaning to: the peacemaker, the worrier, the one who keeps everyone fed and calm. Family patterns replay with almost comic precision, and your patience for them runs thin. Comforts that once soothed you, a routine, a place, a certain person, start to feel like a cage. Work and the wider world tug from the other side, asking you to step beyond the nest. Grief surfaces for what is ending, sometimes over something as small as a sold house or a changed tradition. Releasing it frees feelings that have been tied to the past for far too long."
  },
  "northNode|mercury": {
    "conj": "This season the North Node crosses your Mercury, and your mind turns towards the ideas that will shape your next chapter. You find yourself signing up for a course, starting a newsletter, or having one conversation that rearranges your thinking in an afternoon. Books, podcasts and chance remarks land with uncanny timing, as if someone planted them for you. Contracts, applications and messages carry more weight than usual, so an email you send this season can open a door. Your voice wants to be heard, and speaking up feels awkward if you are used to listening. Still, the words you find now point firmly towards where you are going.",
    "soft": "Learning feels like a natural next step while the North Node makes a supportive angle to your Mercury over the coming months. Conversations flow with people who stretch you, whether a mentor at work, a neighbour with an unusual hobby or a sibling you talk to properly. Writing, teaching or pitching an idea goes better than expected. One good question from a colleague opens a whole line of enquiry, and you follow it happily. Paperwork and plans fall into order without much fuss. Your thinking comes out of this stretch sharper and more your own, and you speak about your direction with far more certainty.",
    "hard": "With the South Node on your Mercury for a few months, old ways of thinking ask to be put down. The same arguments replay in your head, the same stories about yourself, the same opinions offered on autopilot. Some conversations start to feel pointless, and you lose interest in the gossip or group chats that once filled your evenings. A larger picture pulls at you instead: a belief, a journey, a philosophy that asks for more than facts. Your mind feels tired of detail and hungry for meaning. Admitting you no longer know what you think is uncomfortable. Clearing out that mental clutter leaves space for a wiser, more spacious voice."
  },
  "northNode|venus": {
    "conj": "Love, pleasure and money turn in a direction that feels fated as the North Node crosses your Venus for a few months. You meet someone who matters, or an existing relationship shifts into a deeper, more honest phase. Your taste changes too: clothes, music and the way you arrange a room start to reflect who you are becoming. Money questions circle around what you truly value, and a job offer or a big purchase marks a turning point. Wanting things this openly feels vulnerable, especially if you are used to settling. This period rewards the risk. What you let yourself love now leads somewhere important.",
    "soft": "Good things arrive through warmth and connection while the North Node makes an easy angle to your Venus over the coming months. A friend introduces you to someone lovely, a creative project finds its audience, or a money matter resolves in your favour without a battle. You feel more attractive, and people respond to that ease in shops, at work and on dates. Pleasure becomes part of your growth rather than a distraction from it: a dance class, a weekend away, a dinner that turns into a new friendship. Choosing what you like, rather than what you think you should, gets simpler. Slowly your relationships start to look like your values, and that fit feels good.",
    "hard": "This is a releasing season for love and money, as the South Node sits on your Venus for a few months. You feel drawn back to a familiar type, an ex who texts late at night, a habit of spending to soothe a bad day. Some relationships run their course, and the ending is less dramatic than sad. Comfort that used to satisfy now feels flat, and even a favourite restaurant loses its shine. Something more intense calls from the other side: shared money, intimacy, the harder questions about trust. Letting go of what is merely pleasant takes courage. The love left standing afterwards has depth."
  },
  "northNode|mars": {
    "conj": "For a few months the North Node crosses your Mars, and your drive locks onto a direction that feels destined. A surge of energy arrives for something new: a business idea, a training plan, a fight worth having at work. Hesitation that held you back for years seems less important than the thing you want. Conflicts come too, often with people who mistake your new boldness for aggression. Some of that friction is necessary, because it shows you where your courage belongs. Early runs, heavy gardening or anything physical helps steady the intensity. The actions you take in this stretch set a course you keep following for a long time.",
    "soft": "Effort flows easily towards your goals while the North Node makes a supportive angle to your Mars over the coming months. You start the project, send the application, go to the gym on a wet Tuesday, and each step builds on the last. People admire your initiative and want to join in rather than compete. Desire feels clean and uncomplicated, at work and in the bedroom alike. Asserting yourself no longer leaves the usual guilty hangover afterwards. There is a satisfying sense of momentum, of doing rather than endlessly planning. Something that felt stuck for a year starts to move under your hands.",
    "hard": "The South Node spends a few months on your Mars, and old ways of fighting and chasing ask to be released. You snap at people out of habit, push hard on goals that no longer mean much, or pick the same argument with a partner for the hundredth time. Energy drains faster than usual, and the old adrenaline tricks stop working. Some battles end, sometimes because you walk away and sometimes because the other side does. Partners and colleagues ask for cooperation rather than conquest, and that grates at first. Losing your edge is the fear. In truth you are shedding a kind of anger that has cost you more than it ever won."
  },
  "northNode|jupiter": {
    "conj": "Doors to growth open in ways that feel almost arranged as the North Node crosses your Jupiter for a few months. A trip, a course, a teacher or a chance introduction points you towards a larger life. Optimism returns after a flat spell, along with an appetite for meaning, travel or study. Offers arrive that stretch your sense of what is possible, and saying yes to all of them is tempting. Overreaching is the danger, promising too much or spending ahead of the good news. Still, the luck of this period is genuine. What you begin now has room to grow for years.",
    "soft": "Over the coming months the North Node makes an easy angle to your Jupiter, and good fortune arrives through generosity and faith. Someone vouches for you, a mentor offers advice at the right moment, or a plan you had half abandoned suddenly finds backing. You feel more hopeful and it shows, so people want to be around you. Learning becomes a pleasure, whether a language app on the train or a weekend workshop in another city. Small risks pay off, like applying for the stretch role or booking the trip. There is a feeling of being carried a little by life, with your beliefs lining up behind your direction.",
    "hard": "Old beliefs and easy optimism come up for release as the South Node settles on your Jupiter for a few months. The familiar habits show up: promising too much, trusting a plan because it sounds good, chasing the next big thing to avoid the details of this one. A teacher, faith or philosophy you leaned on starts to feel too small. Some opportunities that looked golden fade out before they begin. Ordinary facts demand attention instead: emails, local conversations, the practical steps you skipped. After a period of expansion this feels like shrinking. In its place grows a wiser, more grounded hope that no longer needs to overpromise."
  },
  "northNode|saturn": {
    "conj": "For a few months the North Node crosses your Saturn, and responsibility becomes part of your destiny rather than a weight against it. A call to step up arrives: a management role, a serious commitment, a structure you build for yourself or your family. Older people or authority figures play a key part, as mentors or as tests. Fear of failure rises, along with the familiar voice that says you are not ready. Yet the timing is right, and the work you commit to now carries weight. Slow, steady effort in this stretch lays foundations you stand on for years, even on the evenings when it feels like pure slog.",
    "soft": "Discipline feels like a friend rather than a punishment while the North Node makes a supportive angle to your Saturn over the coming months. Keeping the routine, finishing the tax return and saying no to what drains your time all get easier. An older colleague or mentor offers guidance that helps you shape a clearer plan. Commitments you make now feel solid and sensible rather than heavy. People start to see you as someone reliable, and that trust opens doors. There is quiet satisfaction in building something brick by brick. Ambition and direction finally pull the same way.",
    "hard": "Across the next few months the South Node sits on your Saturn, loosening old duties and rigid rules. You see how many obligations you carry out of habit: the committee you never wanted to join, the role of family organiser, the standards inherited from a strict parent. Tiredness sets in around control and constant self-discipline. Some structures end, a job, a routine, a commitment that has outlived its purpose. Home and your emotional life call from the other side, asking for softness rather than endurance. At first letting go looks like failure. In fact it frees you from burdens that were never yours to carry."
  },
  "northNode|uranus": {
    "conj": "Sudden change arrives with the feeling that it was always meant to happen as the North Node crosses your Uranus for a few months. Restlessness builds, along with a craving for freedom and impatience with anything that feels stale. An unexpected offer, a new friend who thinks differently, or a piece of technology changes how you live and work. Plans shift at short notice, and not knowing what next month holds is unsettling. Yet each surprise nudges you closer to a more authentic life. Something unusual about you becomes an asset rather than an oddity. The breakthroughs of this period feel electric, and they last.",
    "soft": "Over the coming months the North Node makes an easy angle to your Uranus, and change feels exciting rather than frightening. You try something new, a different route to work, a club, a creative experiment, and it opens a surprising door. Friends and online communities bring fresh ideas and useful contacts. Your independence grows without any need to rebel against anyone. Insights arrive in the shower or halfway up a hill, fully formed and useful. This stretch has a lightness to it, a sense that the future is roomier than you thought. Small innovations add up to a lasting shift in how you live.",
    "hard": "With the South Node resting on your Uranus for a few months, old ways of rebelling or staying detached come up for release. You notice how often you keep people at arm's length, or change plans just to prove you cannot be pinned down. Groups or causes that once felt like home start to feel hollow. Some sudden endings happen: a friendship, a project, a scheme that fizzles overnight. Your own creativity and heart pull from the other side, asking you to commit to something personal. Wanting roots after so long prizing freedom feels strange. What replaces the old detachment is a warmer, more grounded kind of originality."
  },
  "northNode|neptune": {
    "conj": "The North Node spends a few months on your Neptune, and dreams, faith and imagination point you towards your path. A strong pull towards meaningful work appears: art, music, healing, service or a spiritual practice. Coincidences multiply, and you meet people who seem to understand you without words. Staying grounded gets harder, and it becomes easy to forget appointments or overcommit to someone in need. Idealism rises, so clear sight about who deserves your trust matters more than usual. Still, the inspiration is real. Something you begin in this stretch carries a sense of calling that lasts long after the Node has moved on.",
    "soft": "Intuition leads you well while the North Node makes a gentle angle to your Neptune over the coming months. Creative ideas arrive easily, whether you sketch, write, play music or cook for friends on a Friday night. A chance encounter or a vivid dream nudges you in the right direction. Compassion comes easily, and helping others feels nourishing rather than draining. Spiritual interests deepen, and meditation, prayer or long walks bring peace. There is a sense of trust in life, of being guided. Your inner world and your outer path start to feel like one road.",
    "hard": "Old illusions and escapes are due for release while the South Node sits on your Neptune over the next few months. A familiar pattern of drifting, daydreaming or rescuing someone who never quite changes becomes hard to ignore. Spiritual beliefs or creative dreams that once sustained you begin to feel vague or unreliable. Disappointments land, especially where you trusted a hope more than the facts. Practical life pulls from the other side: health routines, daily work, the diary you keep meaning to organise. The whole period is like waking from a long dream. Releasing the fog brings a clearer and more useful kind of faith."
  },
  "northNode|pluto": {
    "conj": "For a few months the North Node crosses your Pluto, and a deep transformation feels fated. Intense encounters arrive: a relationship that changes you, a crisis that forces a decision, a power dynamic at work that has to shift. Old fears around control and loss rise, and you stand at the edge of something you cannot undo. Yet the pull is unmistakable, towards depth, truth and your own power. Some people or situations leave your life abruptly. What replaces them carries more meaning. This stretch leaves you changed, with a stronger sense of what you are here to do.",
    "soft": "The North Node makes a supportive angle to your Pluto this season, and transformation arrives without the usual drama. You find the courage to face something long avoided: a debt, a secret, an old grief. Therapy, research or one deep conversation brings release. People sense your strength and trust you with serious matters, the late phone call, the confidential problem. Your influence at work or in a group grows steadily, earned rather than grabbed. A quiet renewal is happening under the surface. Your own life starts to feel like yours to shape, and change stops looking like a threat.",
    "hard": "The South Node crosses your Pluto for a few months, and old intensity, control and fear come up for release. You catch yourself gripping too hard: checking a partner's phone, nursing a grudge, needing to win every power struggle. Some endings feel heavy and unavoidable, as though something is being taken from you. Crises from the past echo, and old grief resurfaces at odd moments. Simpler pleasures and steadier values call from the other side, asking for calm rather than drama. Losing your armour is frightening. Real safety, you are learning, does not depend on control."
  },
  "northNode|chiron": {
    "conj": "Your oldest wound becomes part of your path as the North Node crosses your Chiron for a few months. Memories and feelings from painful periods return, often triggered by small things: a comment at work, an old photo, a waiting room. People who share your struggle appear, and helping them helps you too. Having the tender place touched so openly feels raw. Yet healing happens here, through a teacher, a group or your own honesty. The wound starts to become a source of wisdom rather than shame. Years from now, you pass on what you learn in these months.",
    "soft": "Across the coming months the North Node makes an easy angle to your Chiron, and healing arrives gently. You meet people who understand what you have been through, and their kindness helps old hurts soften. Speaking about a past struggle becomes easier, and it lands better than you feared. Chances to mentor, teach or support others appear, and you turn out to be good at it. Moments of self-acceptance come unexpectedly, on a walk, over a book, during a long talk with a friend. There is a sense that your pain has a purpose. You carry your wound more lightly, and that helps others see theirs.",
    "hard": "Across these few months the South Node rests on your Chiron, and old ways of coping with pain come up for release. You slip into playing the victim, the fixer or the one who always manages, even when it no longer helps. Past hurts resurface, sometimes through a relationship that echoes an old dynamic almost word for word. It feels like the same lesson again. Your sense of identity and purpose pulls from the other side, asking you to step beyond the story of your injury. Letting go of how you have defined yourself through the wound is hard. What remains is a self no longer organised around pain."
  },
  "northNode|northNode": {
    "conj": "For a few months the North Node returns to where it stood when you were born, and life turns you back towards your true direction. This Nodal return comes around the ages of 18, 37, 56 and 74, and it rarely passes quietly. A pull to change course arrives: a new job, a move, a relationship that begins or ends, a decision that sets the next two decades. People and events feel fated, turning up just when you need them. If you have drifted from what matters, the correction is unsettling. Yet the direction is clear. What you choose now shapes the next chapter of your life.",
    "soft": "Your life direction flows smoothly while the North Node makes a supportive angle to its own natal place over the coming months. A sense of rightness settles around the choices in front of you. Opportunities arrive that fit your path, and you have the confidence to take them. People you meet feel aligned with your goals, and conversations over coffee or on a train point you forwards. Old doubts fade a little, replaced by trust in where you are heading. Nothing dramatic happens, but the momentum is real. You end this stretch more certain of your purpose and more at ease with it.",
    "hard": "The South Node sits on your natal North Node for a few months, a reversal that comes around the ages of 9, 28, 47 and 65. Old habits and comfort zones pull you back, just as you sense you should be moving forward. Situations from the past repeat, and familiar people reappear with familiar demands. Going backwards, stuck in patterns you thought you had outgrown, is how it feels. Friends, partners and colleagues question your choices, and some of their doubts sting. Letting go of what is familiar but no longer yours takes real effort. The clarity that follows sets up the next stage of your path."
  },
  "northNode|asc": {
    "conj": "As the North Node crosses your Ascendant for a few months, how you present yourself becomes part of your path. You want to change your look, your posture, even the way you introduce yourself at a party. People respond to you differently, and new doors open simply because you show up. Being seen this clearly feels exposing. With the South Node on your Descendant, partnerships ask less of you for once, and your own life demands attention. The changes of this period are personal and visible, from a new wardrobe to a new way of walking into a room. You step into a version of yourself that feels more real.",
    "soft": "Over the coming months the North Node makes an easy angle to your Ascendant, and life backs you in stepping forward. Confidence rises, and it shows in how you walk into a meeting or a crowded bar. Introductions come easily, and strangers warm to you quickly. A new haircut, outfit or fitness routine feels like a genuine expression of who you are rather than a disguise. Friends and colleagues notice your energy and hand you opportunities. How you look and where you are going start to match. You carry yourself with more ease and more purpose, and people remember you.",
    "hard": "Old ways of presenting yourself come up for release while the South Node crosses your Ascendant for a few months. You notice how often you play a part: the capable one, the joker, the one who needs nobody. Being seen that way starts to feel tiresome. Partnerships and one-to-one relationships call from the other side, asking you to let someone in rather than go it alone. Depending on others, or sharing the spotlight, feels vulnerable. Some self-image habits fade without much fuss. What emerges is a self more open to connection and far less defended."
  },
  "northNode|mc": {
    "conj": "Your career and public life turn towards your calling as the North Node crosses your Midheaven for a few months. Offers, promotions or public roles appear that feel meant for you. People in authority notice your work, and a single meeting can reshape your professional direction. The pressure is real, as though the world is suddenly watching. Home and family ask less of you, or ask you to trust that they can manage for a while. The choices you make now carry weight for years. You step into a role that fits who you are becoming.",
    "soft": "The North Node makes a supportive angle to your Midheaven through the coming months, and career growth comes without a fight. A colleague recommends you, a project lands well, or a new client arrives through a friend of a friend. You feel surer of your professional direction and better able to talk about it in interviews and appraisals. Recognition comes slowly but steadily. Work feels more meaningful, as if it connects with a larger purpose. Your ambitions seem supported by life rather than fought for. This stretch brings you closer to the work you are meant to do.",
    "hard": "With the South Node on your Midheaven for a few months, old ambitions and public roles come up for release. Fatigue gathers around titles, status and the image you have built at work. Some professional roles end, or lose their shine, and the promotion you chased stops mattering. Home, family and your private life call from the other side, asking for attention and care. Stepping back while others seem to be climbing stings. Yet what you release creates room for a more personal kind of success. You begin to measure achievement by how your life feels rather than how it looks."
  },
};
window.AstroDeep.transitHousesRich = {
  "jupiter": {
    "1": {
      "text": "For about a year you walk into rooms differently. Jupiter crossing your first house lifts your confidence, and people answer you faster, smile back sooner and assume you know what you are doing. You catch yourself saying yes to the haircut, the new coat, the solo project you shelved two years ago. Strangers start conversations with you in queues. Your appetite grows along with your nerve, and the body often carries a little more of you by the end of it. The difficulty is promising more than one person can deliver, because everything feels possible when you are this warm. What opens now is a new twelve-year chapter that starts with you taking up the space you always half wanted."
    },
    "2": {
      "text": "Money starts to move more easily for you while Jupiter spends its year in your second house. A client pays more than you quoted, a skill you treated as a hobby turns out to have a price, or you simply stop flinching when you check your balance. With it comes a quieter shift: you begin to believe your time is worth something. Spending climbs just as fast, though, and you notice the basket filling with nice things you did not plan for. The generous mood makes carelessness feel like abundance. Underneath the good fortune, this year is teaching you what you value, so the extra lands somewhere that still matters to you when the transit ends."
    },
    "3": {
      "text": "Your inbox, your bookshelf and your diary all fill up this year. With Jupiter in your third house, your mind is hungry: you sign up for the course, start the newsletter, and find yourself talking to the neighbour you have nodded at for years. A sibling or colleague brings good news or a useful tip, and short trips turn out to be more fun than the long one you planned. Ideas arrive faster than you can write them down. The snag is scatter, with seven tabs open and a stack of half-read books by the bed. Your voice carries further than usual now, and people remember what you say."
    },
    "4": {
      "text": "Home becomes the place where your life grows for the next year or so. Jupiter in your fourth house often brings a move, a renovation, a bigger kitchen table or a new person living under your roof. You feel warmer towards family, and old tensions with a parent soften over long Sunday lunches. Even staying put, you sleep better and feel more rooted in your own four walls. The catch is overreaching: the mortgage stretched a little too far, the house project that swallows every weekend. Something deeper is happening too, as you come to understand where you come from and let that give you a steadier floor inside."
    },
    "5": {
      "text": "Pleasure moves to the centre of your year while Jupiter passes through your fifth house. You flirt more, laugh louder, and find whole afternoons vanishing into painting, music, dancing or whatever makes you lose track of time. Romance arrives easily, and if you have children they become better company than usual. Your creative confidence swells, so you finally share the work instead of hiding it. The trouble is the gambler in you waking up, drawn to the dramatic affair, the risky bet, the third glass of wine. At its best, this year proves to you that joy is not a reward for finishing your work but the source of your best ideas."
    },
    "6": {
      "text": "Your ordinary Tuesday gets better this year. Jupiter in your sixth house tends to bring a kinder workplace, a job that suits you more, or a routine that finally clicks, with the morning walk and the proper lunch break actually happening. Colleagues help without being asked. You feel motivated to look after your body, booking the overdue check up and cooking proper meals again. The hitch is saying yes to every task because each one looks small, until your week is quietly overloaded. Small improvements add up now, and by the end of the year your daily life runs on habits that support you."
    },
    "7": {
      "text": "Other people bring luck to your door while Jupiter moves through your seventh house. For about a year you meet someone who matters, commit more deeply to the person you already have, or find a business partner who opens a door you could not open alone. Negotiations go your way, and contracts tend to be signed in good spirits. You learn a great deal about yourself through the person across the table. The pitfall is idealising them, or agreeing to terms too quickly because the mood is so good. Generosity flows both ways at its best, and your relationships grow larger than either of you alone."
    },
    "8": {
      "text": "Things get deeper and more entangled for you this year. With Jupiter in your eighth house, shared money often grows through a partner's income, an inheritance, a settlement or a joint venture, and intimacy becomes more honest and more charged. You find yourself having the late-night conversation about death, sex or money that you have avoided for years. A crisis that would once have floored you becomes something you move through with surprising courage. The danger is taking on debt or merging your life with someone faster than you have looked properly. What opens is trust, the kind that lets another person all the way in."
    },
    "9": {
      "text": "Your world gets bigger for about a year. Jupiter is at home in your ninth house, and you feel the pull towards the long flight, the degree, the retreat, the book you want to write or the teacher whose ideas rearrange your thinking. Conversations with people from other cultures light you up. The future feels roomy, and your sense of meaning expands with it. The shadow is restlessness, booking the next trip before you have unpacked the last, or preaching your new philosophy at dinner. This is often one of the most inspiring years of your cycle, and it leaves you with a wider sense of what your life is for."
    },
    "10": {
      "text": "Your work gets noticed this year. Jupiter in your tenth house puts you in view of people who make decisions, and a promotion, a public role, a mentor's backing or an invitation to lead is common. Ambition feels natural rather than anxious, and you speak about your achievements without squirming. Much of this is groundwork from earlier years paying off at last. The trap is chasing the title that looks impressive but does not fit you, or letting praise inflate your sense of importance. By the end of it your reputation stands on firmer, higher ground, and people know your name."
    },
    "11": {
      "text": "New people keep arriving in your life while Jupiter moves through your eleventh house. You get added to the group chat, invited to the dinner, asked to join the committee or the collaboration that matters to you. A friend of a friend opens a door you could not have reached alone. Your hopes for the next few years start to feel achievable, and you speak them aloud more often. The downside is spreading yourself thin across every invitation, or leaning on connections when effort is needed. Over this year you find out who your real allies are, and what future you want to build alongside them."
    },
    "12": {
      "text": "Growth goes underground for you this year. With Jupiter in your twelfth house, the progress happens where nobody sees it: in therapy, in long walks alone, in quiet service, or in the dreams you wake up still thinking about. You notice a strange sense of protection, as if things resolve without you having to push. Outwardly life can look slow, and you feel less inclined to perform. The shadow is escape, the extra episode or glass that numbs rather than rests you. Much of what you tend now in private becomes the foundation for a fresh start when Jupiter reaches your Ascendant next year."
    }
  },
  "saturn": {
    "1": {
      "text": "For about two and a half years you feel older, and people treat you as if you are. Saturn crossing your first house brings a sober, defining stretch: responsibilities land squarely on you, and the way you used to present yourself stops fitting. You notice tiredness sooner, and your body asks for sleep, pacing and respect. The jokes you used to hide behind fall flat. The difficulty is heaviness, a sense of carrying everything alone with little applause. Out of it comes a self you choose for your own reasons rather than for approval, sturdier and plainer and very much yours."
    },
    "2": {
      "text": "Money gets serious for you over the next couple of years. With Saturn in your second house, you check prices twice, feel the pinch of a tighter income, or discover your finances rest on shakier ground than you assumed. You also face how you value yourself: the invoice you undercharged, the things you cling to because they feel like safety. Nights spent doing sums at the kitchen table are common. It can feel lean and anxious for a long time. Slowly, though, you build something solid, a realistic relationship with resources and a sense of worth that no longer depends on a good month."
    },
    "3": {
      "text": "Your words start to carry weight for the next couple of years. Saturn in your third house makes you careful about what you say, what you put in writing and who you say it to. You reread emails three times before sending them. Study feels harder but more rewarding, which makes this a strong time for a qualification or serious training. A sibling or neighbour brings responsibility or friction, and paperwork, errands and the daily commute can feel like a grind. Doubts about your own intelligence creep in during this stretch. What you gain is a disciplined mind and a voice that people trust."
    },
    "4": {
      "text": "Home becomes a place of duty for about two and a half years. Saturn in your fourth house often means caring for an ageing parent, dealing with a leaking roof, moving under pressure, or facing family patterns you hoped you had left behind. You feel the old rules of your childhood house in the way you react. Evenings can be lonely, with more obligation than comfort around you. Your emotional foundations are being tested. By the end you have built a sense of security that does not depend on anyone else, and a home, literal or inner, that genuinely holds you."
    },
    "5": {
      "text": "Fun starts to feel like something you have to earn while Saturn crosses your fifth house for a couple of years. Romance turns serious or goes quiet, your creative work stalls under your own criticism, and children bring extra responsibility. You notice yourself declining the party because there is too much to do. Yet this is a strong period for learning a craft properly, finishing the long project, or committing to someone with clear eyes. The danger is letting self judgement shut down play entirely. What returns afterwards is a more mature joy, rooted in skill and in choices you made on purpose."
    },
    "6": {
      "text": "Your daily routine goes under the microscope for the next couple of years. Saturn in your sixth house brings a heavier workload, an exacting manager, or a job that plainly no longer suits you. Your body speaks up too, making it obvious which habits cannot continue: the skipped lunches, the late screens, the coffee in place of sleep. Some weeks feel like pure drudgery. The work now is practical reorganisation, with realistic schedules and steady habits. What you are left with is a working life that respects your limits and a daily rhythm you can actually keep up."
    },
    "7": {
      "text": "Your relationships are tested for about two and a half years. Saturn in your seventh house shows which partnerships have solid foundations: some end, while those with genuine commitment deepen and formalise, sometimes through marriage or a signed agreement. You feel the weight of a partner's needs, or notice you keep having the same argument with different people. Contracts and business arrangements demand clear terms and patience. Evenings can feel sobering or lonely. The clarity is hard-won, and it leaves you knowing exactly what you need from others and what you are willing to give."
    },
    "8": {
      "text": "Hard matters come to the surface for you over the next couple of years. With Saturn in your eighth house, you deal with debt, tax, a will, a partner's finances or a settlement that drags on. Intimacy becomes guarded, and trust has to be rebuilt one conversation at a time. Old losses and fears you have avoided rise up, often at three in the morning. The shadow is shutting down to protect yourself and calling it strength. Facing it slowly makes you far stronger, and much of what once frightened you shrinks once you look at it directly."
    },
    "9": {
      "text": "Your beliefs are put on trial while Saturn moves through your ninth house for a couple of years. Ideas you inherited from your family or picked up casually stop holding, and you want a philosophy that survives real life. You notice yourself arguing less and reading more. Higher study is demanding and worthwhile, so this suits a serious degree, a teaching credential or a writing project. Travel feels complicated or dutiful, and legal matters move slowly. The frustration is how little feels certain for a while. What you build instead is a worldview that is yours, earned from evidence and experience."
    },
    "10": {
      "text": "Your career faces its reckoning over the next two and a half years. Saturn in your tenth house assesses everything you have built: where the foundations are strong, you gain authority, a senior role or public recognition; where they are weak, you hit a ceiling or a setback. You feel watched, and the pressure to prove yourself sits on your chest during meetings. Responsibility increases either way. The weight is heavy, and some days it feels like nobody sees the effort. By the end of this stretch your standing is more solid than it has ever been, provided you carry it honestly."
    },
    "11": {
      "text": "Your social circle gets sorted for the next couple of years. Saturn in your eleventh house lets friendships built on convenience or old habit fade away, while a handful become deeper and more reliable. You notice who actually turns up when you need help. You also take on an organising role in a group or cause, doing the unglamorous work behind a shared goal. Long-range hopes come under scrutiny, and wishful thinking gives way to plans. Stretches of this can feel isolating. What remains is a smaller, sturdier circle and a clear sense of which dreams deserve years of effort."
    },
    "12": {
      "text": "A quiet, inward stretch begins for about two and a half years. With Saturn in your twelfth house, old fears, patterns and unfinished business surface, usually when you are alone and the house is still. Your energy runs lower and outward progress slows. You find yourself caring for someone, working behind the scenes, or waiting on matters that cannot be rushed. It feels like a long winter at times. The work is clearing space: letting go of what belongs to an older you, resting properly, and facing what you avoided. All of it prepares a clean start when Saturn reaches your Ascendant."
    }
  },
  "uranus": {
    "1": {
      "text": "For about seven years you keep surprising yourself. Uranus crossing your first house loosens every fixed idea of who you are: you change your hair, your style, your name online, sometimes your whole direction, often with very little warning. People who knew you ten years ago struggle to keep up, and you feel faintly allergic to anyone telling you how to be. Your body runs on nervous energy, and sitting still in a long meeting becomes torture. The cost is jumpiness, sudden exits and a restlessness that leaves others unsettled and you exhausted. Out of the upheaval steps a freer, more original version of you that no longer bothers to explain itself."
    },
    "2": {
      "text": "Your income stops behaving predictably for a long stretch of seven or so years. Uranus in your second house brings sudden windfalls and sudden drops, a new way of earning through freelancing, a side business or technology that changes your pay almost overnight. Your attitude to possessions shifts as well: you give things away, sell the car, or wake up wanting a completely different kind of security. What you value can flip after a single conversation. The strain comes from months of plenty followed by months of scrambling, with no steady line on the graph. Gradually a more inventive relationship with money forms, along with a self-worth that stands on your own terms."
    },
    "3": {
      "text": "Your mind speeds up and your routines scatter for about seven years. With Uranus in your third house, ideas arrive from odd places, opinions change quickly, and you find yourself deep in subjects you never cared about before. A new gadget, a sudden trip, or a sibling or neighbour doing something nobody expected keeps shaking up your ordinary days. Your nervous system hums, and sleep suffers when your thoughts refuse to switch off. The hard part is settling: ten projects started, twenty tabs open, conversations abandoned halfway. Friends and colleagues begin coming to you for the fresh angle, because your thinking has become genuinely original."
    },
    "4": {
      "text": "The ground under your home shifts for a long stretch of about seven years. Uranus in your fourth house often brings sudden moves, unusual living arrangements, a family upheaval, or a revelation that changes how you see your childhood. You feel restless in the house where you once felt settled, rearranging the furniture one month and looking at flats in another city the next. Family members behave in ways you did not predict. Losing the sense of a stable base is unnerving, all the more when the rug gets pulled more than once. In exchange you win freedom from inherited family patterns, and eventually a home that reflects who you are."
    },
    "5": {
      "text": "Love and creativity turn electric for you over about seven years. Uranus in your fifth house brings sudden attractions, unconventional romances, and creative ideas that arrive fully formed at two in the morning. You feel bored by anything predictable and drawn to people and projects that shock you awake. Children in your life surprise you, or plans around having them change abruptly. Affairs burn bright and end fast, and projects get dropped the moment the thrill fades, which leaves a trail of beginnings. Underneath the chaos you are gaining permission to love and create in a way nobody else would, and to enjoy it."
    },
    "6": {
      "text": "Your working week refuses to stay the same shape for the next seven or so years. Uranus in your sixth house brings job changes, remote or flexible work, colleagues who arrive and vanish, and a growing allergy to the nine to five. Stress shows up quickly in your body, through broken sleep, a jumpy stomach or tension in your shoulders. You rebuild your schedule every few months and still feel it does not fit. Chaos wears you down fast, and without some rhythm you end up running on adrenaline. Slowly a working life emerges that is designed around your own rhythms, often more independent and far more interesting than the one you left."
    },
    "7": {
      "text": "Relationships get shaken up for you over about seven years. Uranus in your seventh house brings sudden meetings, sudden endings, and a sharp need for space inside partnership. You find yourself drawn to people who are unusual, independent or entirely unlike your usual type, and friends raise an eyebrow at your new choices. Existing relationships change shape, and sometimes the one who wants out is you. Commitments that once felt cosy start to feel like cages, and breaks arrive out of nowhere. Through all of it you are working out a new model of closeness, one where two free people keep choosing each other."
    },
    "8": {
      "text": "Deep change arrives without warning while Uranus moves through your eighth house for a long stretch of about seven years. Shared money shifts overnight, through an unexpected inheritance, a partner's job change, a debt called in or a sudden windfall. Intimacy becomes a place of awakening, where you discover desires and boundaries you did not know you had. Insight into your own psychology comes in flashes, sometimes after a shock that leaves you shaking. You rarely feel sure where the floor is, and trust in joint arrangements wobbles. Old fears loosen their grip as a result, and your relationship with power and closeness becomes far more honest."
    },
    "9": {
      "text": "Your beliefs break open over the next seven or so years. With Uranus in your ninth house, you drop inherited ideas, book a trip on a whim, sign up for an unusual course, or stumble into a philosophy that rewires how you see everything. Dogma makes you impatient, including your own. Foreign places, online teachers and strangers with odd opinions shake your assumptions loose, and you enjoy the vertigo. The trap is restless rebellion, throwing away every old belief before you have found anything to stand on. When the dust settles you hold a worldview that is your own, open, curious and very hard to shake."
    },
    "10": {
      "text": "Your career takes unexpected turns over a long stretch of about seven years. Uranus in your tenth house brings sudden changes of role, a leap into self-employment, a public moment you did not plan, or a boss who disappears overnight. Any job that asks you to fit a mould starts to feel unbearable, and you notice yourself drafting resignation letters in your head. Your reputation can change quickly, for better or worse. Plans get rewritten more than once, and colleagues are never quite sure what you will do next. Eventually you land in a vocation that fits your originality, often in a field that barely existed when you started."
    },
    "11": {
      "text": "Your friendships and hopes get reinvented while Uranus spends seven or so years in your eleventh house. New people arrive fast, often through online communities, activism or unconventional groups, and some old friends drop away almost overnight. You feel pulled towards causes bigger than yourself, and meetings with strangers who share your ideals feel more alive than dinners with people you have known for years. Your picture of the future changes shape more than once. Circles form and dissolve so quickly that it is hard to feel settled anywhere. Along the way you gather a network of genuinely like minded people and a future that excites you."
    },
    "12": {
      "text": "Something stirs underneath your ordinary life for about seven years. With Uranus in your twelfth house, old fears and hidden patterns break loose in sudden flashes of insight, often in dreams, in therapy, in meditation or during the quiet hours of the night. You feel restless in ways you cannot quite explain to anyone. Secrets surface, your own or other people's, and some of them change how you see your past. A jittery sense that something is about to change sits under the surface, with anxiety that has no clear cause. All of this is preparation, and by the time Uranus reaches your Ascendant you have shed enough to become someone new."
    }
  },
  "neptune": {
    "1": {
      "text": "For a long stretch of many years your edges soften. Neptune crossing your first house makes you more sensitive, more intuitive, more affected by the mood of every room you walk into. People project onto you, seeing a healer, a muse or a mystery, and you find yourself becoming whatever they need. You drift between identities, unsure how to describe yourself and not much bothered. Alcohol, medication and noise hit your body harder than before. Losing yourself in other people's expectations is the main hazard. Kept clear, this becomes a gentler and more compassionate way of being, with a presence people find magnetic."
    },
    "2": {
      "text": "Money becomes blurry for you over a long stretch of years. Neptune in your second house clouds your sense of what you earn, owe and spend, and figures that seemed solid turn out to be vaguer than you thought. You give generously, sometimes far too generously, and avoid opening the bank statement. At the same time, what you value shifts towards meaning, beauty and spirit over possessions, and you feel less interested in owning things. Offers that sound too good to be true tempt you, and some of them are. In time your sense of worth comes to rest on something deeper than any balance."
    },
    "3": {
      "text": "Your thinking grows more poetic and less precise for a long stretch of years. With Neptune in your third house, you daydream in meetings, lose your keys, misread a text, and then write or speak with startling imagination. You pick up on what people mean rather than what they say, sometimes before they know it themselves. A sibling or neighbour becomes confusing, idealised or in need of quiet care. Vague agreements, forgotten details and promises that dissolve cause misunderstandings along the way. Your words gain the power to move people, because your mind now listens to intuition as closely as it listens to facts."
    },
    "4": {
      "text": "Home becomes a place of longing for you over a long stretch of many years. Neptune in your fourth house softens the walls: you dream of the perfect house, feel nostalgic for a childhood that never quite existed, or end up living near water. Family matters grow hazy, with old secrets, quiet dependencies, or a relative who needs gentle care. You feel homesick even when you are sitting in your own kitchen. Escaping into a fantasy of family, rather than seeing people as they are, keeps the ache alive. Slowly a spiritual sense of belonging grows in you that no single address can give or take away."
    },
    "5": {
      "text": "Romance turns dreamy for you over a long stretch of years. Neptune in your fifth house makes love feel cinematic, and you fall for people who seem almost too good to be real. Creative work flows from somewhere beyond you, especially music, film, photography and anything that comes from imagination. Children become a source of wonder, or of worry that is hard to put into words. Disillusion arrives when the beloved turns out to be human, or when a project dissolves before it is finished. Even so, your capacity for inspiration deepens, and you make things that touch people in places they cannot explain."
    },
    "6": {
      "text": "Your daily routine goes soft at the edges for a long stretch of years. Neptune in your sixth house makes the ordinary grind feel meaningless, and you start looking for work that heals, serves or inspires. Your body grows sensitive, reacting to diet, stress, alcohol and surroundings in ways that are hard to pin down. Job roles blur, and colleagues say one thing and mean another. Whole days slip past without shape, and a tiredness you cannot explain follows you around. Over the years you shape a working life with meaning, along with daily habits that care for your spirit as well as your body."
    },
    "7": {
      "text": "Your relationships take on a dreamlike quality for a long stretch of many years. Neptune in your seventh house draws you towards soulmate connections, partners who need rescuing, or people you see through a romantic haze. You feel an almost telepathic bond with someone close, finishing each other's thoughts across the table. Boundaries blur, and you notice you are giving far more than you receive. Idealising a partner until disappointment arrives is the old pattern here, and contracts and business dealings can mislead you too. Seen clearly, this transit teaches you unconditional compassion and a tenderness that holds two real people."
    },
    "8": {
      "text": "Intimacy and shared money grow misty while Neptune moves through your eighth house for a long stretch of years. Joint finances become unclear, with debts, inheritances or a partner's income wrapped in confusion or vague promises. Sexually and emotionally you crave a union so complete that the edges between you dissolve. You feel drawn to the mystical, to vivid dreams about death and rebirth, or to healing work of some kind. Losing yourself in someone else's power or money is a genuine hazard. Alongside the fog comes a profound sense of connection with the unseen, and a far softer relationship with loss."
    },
    "9": {
      "text": "Your search for meaning takes on a spiritual colour over a long stretch of years. Neptune in your ninth house draws you towards pilgrimages, retreats, faiths, gurus and philosophies that promise transcendence. Music, art or a landscape in a foreign place moves you to tears without warning. Formal study competes with intuition, and you trust the second more. The trap is following a teacher or a belief without questioning it, or wandering without ever arriving anywhere. Across these years a compassionate faith in life takes root, and a sense of the sacred stays with you long after any journey ends."
    },
    "10": {
      "text": "Your career and public image go foggy for a long stretch of many years. Neptune in your tenth house makes ambition feel hollow unless the work has meaning, and you drift towards creative, spiritual or healing roles. People see you through their own ideals, which brings glamour one year and confusion the next. You feel unsure what you are meant to be doing, and the question follows you into every appraisal. Misunderstandings, rumours or a direction that never quite crystallises are part of the ride. Gradually a vocation appears that serves something larger than status, and people come to associate your name with inspiration."
    },
    "11": {
      "text": "Your friendships and hopes soften into something more idealistic over a long stretch of years. Neptune in your eleventh house draws you towards spiritual communities, charities, artistic circles or causes with a dream at their centre. You feel a strong pull to belong to something meaningful, and you give your evenings to it happily. Some friends turn out to be different from how you pictured them, and a group you adored lets you down. Getting swept along by a collective fantasy is easy here. Those disappointments leave you with a compassionate circle and a set of hopes that come straight from your heart."
    },
    "12": {
      "text": "A long, quiet dissolving begins while Neptune moves through your twelfth house for many years. Your inner life grows vast: dreams become vivid, intuition sharpens, and solitude feels necessary rather than lonely. You find yourself drawn to meditation, prayer, art, or helping people who are suffering. The line between your feelings and everyone else's grows thin, and a crowded room can leave you drained for a day. Escaping through substances, sleep or fantasy when reality feels too much is the pull to watch. It is slow preparation, and when Neptune reaches your Ascendant you meet the world gentler and more open."
    }
  },
  "pluto": {
    "1": {
      "text": "For a long stretch of years you are being remade. Pluto crossing your first house strips away the personality you built for approval, and a raw intensity enters the way you move, dress and look people in the eye. Others sense your power and respond with attraction, wariness or both. Your body can change dramatically, through illness, training, weight or simply the way you carry yourself. Feeling exposed and consumed is part of it, as old versions of you die off before the new one has fully arrived. The self that emerges is forged in fire, magnetic and very hard to push around."
    },
    "2": {
      "text": "Your relationship with money and self worth is being rebuilt from the ground up over a long stretch of years. Pluto in your second house brings intense financial events: a major gain, a painful loss, or a struggle over who controls the resources. You notice how much of your security you have tied to what you own and earn, and it frightens you. Obsessions surface, like checking accounts compulsively or refusing to spend on yourself. Fear of losing everything drives grasping and hoarding. Slowly you arrive at a sense of worth nobody can take from you, along with power over your own resources."
    },
    "3": {
      "text": "Your thinking turns intense and penetrating for a long stretch of years. With Pluto in your third house, you hear what people are really saying beneath their words, and ordinary conversations turn into investigations. You become obsessed with a subject, a truth, or a piece of writing that will not leave you alone. A sibling or neighbour goes through a crisis that pulls you in. Compulsive thinking, suspicion and words used as weapons are the dark side of this power. Across these years your mind grows formidable, and your voice learns to cut straight to what matters."
    },
    "4": {
      "text": "Your roots are being dug up over a long stretch of many years. Pluto in your fourth house brings deep change at home: a family death or crisis, a forced move, secrets from the past coming to light, or a reckoning with your parents. You feel the weight of generations in your own reactions, hearing your mother's tone in your voice or your father's silence in yours. Your emotional foundations shake. So much has to fall before anything new can be built, and the grief is real. Eventually you lay a foundation of your own, freed from family patterns you no longer have to carry."
    },
    "5": {
      "text": "Love and creativity become intense and all consuming for you over a long stretch of years. Pluto in your fifth house brings obsessive attractions, romances that change you permanently, and creative work that goes straight to the bone. Children, or the question of having them, bring profound change. You feel pleasure at a depth you did not know existed, and you cannot go back to shallow fun. Jealousy, control and love turned into a battle of wills are the price when it goes wrong. Your creative power grows enormously, and you learn a way of loving that holds nothing back."
    },
    "6": {
      "text": "Your daily life and health go through a deep overhaul for a long stretch of years. Pluto in your sixth house brings power struggles at work, a job that demands everything, or a health wake-up call that changes your habits permanently. You feel compelled to strip your routine back to what works, cutting out whatever drains you. Small daily choices, like what you eat or when you sleep, start to feel significant. Burning yourself out to prove your worth, or trying to control every variable, is the danger. Your relationship with work and body is transformed, built on a discipline that comes from inside."
    },
    "7": {
      "text": "Your relationships become the site of profound change for a long stretch of years. Pluto in your seventh house brings intense partnerships, power struggles, and people who reach deep into your psyche. You meet someone who changes the course of your life, or watch an old relationship transform completely or end. Trust, control and jealousy all come up for examination, sometimes in painful late-night arguments. Getting caught in the grip of someone else's power is a real possibility. On the far side you find a capacity for true intimacy between equals, where nothing has to be hidden."
    },
    "8": {
      "text": "Pluto moves through its own territory here, and the next long stretch of years takes you to the depths. Shared money, inheritance, debt, sexuality and death all become intensely real for you. You feel drawn to what is hidden, whether psychology, the occult, or the secrets of the people closest to you. Crises arrive that you cannot talk your way out of, and some of them change everything. Fear, and the urge to control what cannot be controlled, keep rising. Having faced the worst, you discover an astonishing resilience and a freedom that nothing can take away."
    },
    "9": {
      "text": "Your beliefs go through a deep transformation over a long stretch of years. Pluto in your ninth house challenges every truth you inherited, and you search for answers with an intensity that surprises you. A journey, a course of study or a single teacher changes you profoundly. You feel drawn to extreme or radical ideas and argue for them hard. Fanaticism is a danger, holding the new belief as tightly as you held the old one. Gradually a philosophy you have earned through experience takes shape, along with the courage to see the world without illusions."
    },
    "10": {
      "text": "Your career and public role are being transformed over a long stretch of many years. Pluto in your tenth house brings power struggles with authority, a rise to influence, or a collapse that forces you to rebuild from nothing. You feel driven to make a lasting mark on the world, and others notice the force of your ambition. Your reputation carries weight, and every move you make gets watched. Ruthlessness, or a crisis of status that shakes your identity, lurks in the background. A vocation eventually arrives that you pursue with total conviction, and your authority in your field becomes hard won and real."
    },
    "11": {
      "text": "Your friendships and group ties are overhauled for a long stretch of years. Pluto in your eleventh house brings intense friends, power dynamics in groups, and endings with people who were once close. You feel drawn to movements that aim to change society, and you give them more of yourself than you expected. Your hopes for the future transform completely, sometimes more than once. Manipulation or betrayal within a circle you trusted is part of the lesson. Afterwards you are surrounded by people bound to you by shared purpose, and you hold a vision you are willing to fight for."
    },
    "12": {
      "text": "Something deep is shifting in the hidden parts of your life over a long stretch of years. Pluto in your twelfth house brings buried fears, secrets and old psychological patterns to the surface, often through dreams, crises or therapy. You feel a pull towards solitude and inner work, and crowds exhaust you. Some losses happen behind closed doors, where nobody else sees how much they cost you. Self-sabotage, or being haunted by the past, can undermine you quietly. This profound clearing is preparing a rebirth, and that rebirth arrives when Pluto finally reaches your Ascendant."
    }
  },
  "chiron": {
    "1": {
      "text": "For many months, often a few years, the old sore spot is your own face in the mirror. Chiron crossing your first house brings up every early message about how you look, sound or take up space. You notice yourself shrinking in photos, apologising for being in the room, or overcompensating with a performance of confidence. Your body sometimes carries the ache too. Feeling exposed, as if everyone can see the crack, makes ordinary days tiring. Once you stop hiding the parts you were ashamed of, your presence starts to heal other people simply by being honest."
    },
    "2": {
      "text": "Your old wound around worth and money surfaces over many months, often a few years. Chiron in your second house brings back the voice that says you are not enough: the invoice you underprice, the guilt after buying something for yourself, the panic when savings dip. You notice how early lessons about scarcity still run your choices at the checkout. The shame sits deep and shifts slowly, and some weeks it feels like nothing has changed. A hard-won sense of value grows anyway, and you often end up helping others heal their own relationship with money."
    },
    "3": {
      "text": "The wound around speaking, learning or being understood opens up for many months, sometimes a few years. With Chiron in your third house, you remember being told you were slow, too talkative or not clever enough, and you hear that voice in meetings and messages. A sibling relationship aches again. You second-guess every sentence before sending it, then rewrite it anyway. Freezing up just when you most want to be heard is the painful part. A voice grows out of this that speaks directly to other people's hurt, because you know exactly what it is to be misunderstood."
    },
    "4": {
      "text": "Your oldest family ache comes home over many months, often a few years. Chiron in your fourth house brings up whatever felt missing in childhood: warmth, safety, a parent who was really present. You notice it in your reactions at family gatherings, and in the restlessness that makes nowhere quite feel like home. A parent's health or history pulls the wound open again, often during an ordinary phone call. Grief arrives that seems out of all proportion to the moment. Through it you learn to become the home you needed, for yourself and for the people around you."
    },
    "5": {
      "text": "The wound around joy, play and creative confidence surfaces for many months, sometimes a few years. With Chiron in your fifth house, you feel self-conscious when you dance, share your art, or let yourself be seen falling for someone. Old memories of being mocked or ignored when you showed off come back vividly. Children in your life mirror the wound back to you in their own shyness or bravado. Fear of looking foolish keeps you from playing at all on some days. Slowly your creativity roots itself in honesty, and you become the person who gives others permission to shine."
    },
    "6": {
      "text": "The ache shows up in your daily routine and your body for many months, often a few years. Chiron in your sixth house brings up old feelings of never being useful enough, stress that settles in your neck or stomach, and workplaces that echo early criticism. You notice yourself staying late to prove your worth, then lying awake replaying a small mistake. Health niggles demand patience rather than quick fixes. Perfectionism refuses to let you rest. Out of it grows a deep understanding of healing, and often a calling towards service, care or work that helps others recover."
    },
    "7": {
      "text": "The wound shows up in your closest relationships for many months, sometimes a few years. Chiron in your seventh house stirs fears of abandonment, of being too much, or of never quite being chosen. You notice yourself drawn to people who need fixing, or feeling hurt by partners in painfully familiar ways. Old relationship pain comes back into focus, sometimes through an ex reappearing. Repeating the pattern instead of seeing it keeps the wound open. Partnership becomes something new when both of you bring your wounds into the open, and healing starts to happen together."
    },
    "8": {
      "text": "Deep old pain around trust, intimacy or loss surfaces over many months, often a few years. Chiron in your eighth house brings back memories of betrayal, grief or powerlessness, sometimes triggered by a shared financial matter, a bereavement or an intimate relationship. You feel a strong urge to protect yourself by closing off, and you notice how quickly you brace for bad news. It feels raw, like pressing on the same bruise every single day. From that rawness comes profound empathy for others in crisis, and a way of being close that honours your scars."
    },
    "9": {
      "text": "The wound around belief and meaning surfaces for many months, sometimes a few years. With Chiron in your ninth house, you question the faith or philosophy you were raised with, or feel like an outsider in a foreign place where nobody quite gets you. Education brings up old feelings of inadequacy around exams or teachers. You notice cynicism creeping into conversations about meaning. Losing trust in anything bigger than yourself is the lonely part of this long stretch. A wiser, humbler worldview grows in its place, and you gain the ability to guide others who are searching."
    },
    "10": {
      "text": "The ache shows up in your career and public life for many months, often a few years. Chiron in your tenth house brings up old feelings of not being good enough to succeed, and fears about being seen by too many people. You notice imposter feelings in meetings, or a boss who sounds uncannily like a critical parent. Your reputation feels fragile, as if one mistake could undo everything. Hiding your talent to avoid judgement is the easy way out. A vocation shaped by your wound emerges instead, often in healing, teaching or advocacy, with authority earned through honesty."
    },
    "11": {
      "text": "The wound around belonging and friendship surfaces for many months, sometimes a few years. With Chiron in your eleventh house, you feel like the outsider in groups, left out of the chat, unsure whether you are really wanted. Old memories of exclusion from school or family come flooding back. You notice yourself standing at the edge of every circle, ready to leave first. Withdrawing before anyone can reject you keeps you lonelier than you need to be. Your gift for including others grows from this, and a community forms around the shared experience of feeling different."
    },
    "12": {
      "text": "Hidden pain rises quietly for many months, often a few years. Chiron in your twelfth house brings up old sorrows, fears and memories that live beneath conscious awareness, often surfacing in dreams or in solitary moments at the end of the day. You feel a vague ache without a clear source, and sometimes cry without knowing why. Escaping into scrolling, busyness or sleep feels easier than feeling what is there. Compassion for suffering, your own and other people's, deepens in the silence. This quiet healing prepares a renewed sense of self for when Chiron crosses your Ascendant."
    }
  },
  "sun": {
    "1": {
      "text": "For about a month the Sun crosses your first house, and you feel more like yourself than you have all year. You catch your reflection in a shop window and decide the haircut is overdue, or you walk into a meeting and speak first without planning to. People notice you more readily, and your energy lifts in the mornings. The month carries the feel of a personal new year, a moment to decide how you want to come across. The catch is that everything starts to revolve around your own plans, and the people close to you feel the draught. Impatience with anyone who slows you down rises too. What this month hands you is a clean start and the nerve to be seen making it."
    },
    "2": {
      "text": "Money comes into focus while the Sun moves through your second house over the next month. You open the banking app more often, notice what the weekly shop costs to the cent, and feel an odd pleasure in sorting out a drawer of old receipts. There is energy for earning: asking for the rate you deserve, selling something you no longer use, finishing the invoice you kept postponing. Underneath the numbers runs a quieter question about what you are worth to yourself. Buying comfort to settle a restless mood is the easy slip, and so is measuring your whole value by a bank balance. By the time the Sun moves on, you know better what you want your money and your time to hold."
    },
    "3": {
      "text": "Your phone rarely stops for the next month, as the Sun lights up your third house. Messages, quick errands, a sibling who rings with news, a neighbour you have a proper chat with over the fence: daily life fills with small exchanges. Your mind runs faster than usual, and you find yourself reading three things at once and finishing other people's sentences. Writing flows, so the email you dreaded goes out in ten minutes. The strain comes from scatter, with twenty tabs open in your head and nothing quite completed. Nervous energy keeps you up late scrolling. This stretch leaves you with a sharper voice and the confidence to say what you think."
    },
    "4": {
      "text": "Home pulls at you for about a month while the Sun sits at the base of your chart in your fourth house. You want your own bed, your own kitchen, an evening with the curtains drawn and nobody expecting anything of you. Jobs around the house suddenly feel urgent: the shelf that needs putting up, the wardrobe you clear out. Family comes to mind too, through a parent's phone call, an old photo, a memory that surfaces while you cook. Childhood moods stir more easily, and you feel tender or touchy about things that normally slide past. Public life goes quieter, which can look like a lull. In truth it is a month of putting down roots and refilling from the inside."
    },
    "5": {
      "text": "Something playful wakes up in you as the Sun crosses your fifth house for about a month. You want fun that is actually fun: a night out, a game with a child, an afternoon lost in a hobby you had half forgotten. Romance warms up, whether it is flirting across a room or a partner who suddenly seems new again. Creative ideas arrive with heat, and you feel like showing people what you have made. The flip side is a craving for applause, and a sulk when it does not come. Spending on treats and taking silly risks for the thrill also tempt you. This month reminds you that joy feeds your work rather than competing with it."
    },
    "6": {
      "text": "Work and body take the spotlight while the Sun moves through your sixth house for the next month. Your to-do list looks manageable, and you feel a quiet satisfaction clearing the backlog, reorganising the desk, or booking the appointment you have put off since spring. Colleagues bring you their problems, and you are the one who knows where the file is. Your body sends clearer signals too: heaviness after a late night, a stiff back that asks for a walk instead of another coffee. Perfectionism creeps in, and you notice every flaw in a task or a person. Feeling indispensable becomes its own trap. Over these weeks, small daily changes stick in a way they rarely do."
    },
    "7": {
      "text": "Other people move to the centre of your life for about a month as the Sun crosses your seventh house. A partner needs more of your attention, a client wants a meeting, a friend asks for a straight opinion, and you find yourself thinking in terms of 'we'. Relationships show their true shape under this light, both what works and what grates. You become more aware of how much you give and how much comes back. Some days you lose track of your own wishes while accommodating everyone else. On other days someone opposes you openly, and it stings more than you let on. Out of these meetings comes a clearer picture of what you need from the people beside you."
    },
    "8": {
      "text": "The Sun sinks into your eighth house for about a month, and life asks you to look below the surface. Shared money comes up: a joint account, a tax form, a debt someone owes you or one you owe them. Conversations turn intimate, and a late-night talk goes deeper than either of you planned. You notice the power running through your closest bonds, who holds the purse strings, who pulls back when things get close. Jealousy or a need for control surfaces faster than you would like. Old fears get stirred, and the month can feel heavy for a while. What you come away with is honesty, and a closeness that no longer relies on keeping things tidy."
    },
    "9": {
      "text": "Your world wants to get bigger while the Sun travels through your ninth house for the next month. You look up flights, sign up for a course, or fall into a long conversation about belief with someone from a very different background. Ordinary routine feels small, and you crave meaning, a view from a height, a book that rearranges how you see things. Legal, academic and publishing matters move forward with less resistance. Restlessness is the shadow, along with a streak of preaching once you have found an idea you like. Plans also grow faster than your diary allows. By the end of this stretch, your sense of what is possible has widened."
    },
    "10": {
      "text": "For about a month the Sun climbs to the top of your chart in the tenth house, and your working life steps into the light. Bosses notice what you do, a client remembers your name, and a project you have nursed for months finally gets seen. You feel ambitious in a clear, uncomplicated way, and speaking with authority comes more easily. Where your career is heading occupies your thoughts on the commute home. The pressure is real as well: mistakes are more visible and home life gets squeezed. Some days you feel only as good as your last result. Work that deserves recognition gets it, and you see the standing you want in sharper focus."
    },
    "11": {
      "text": "Friends and groups fill your calendar while the Sun moves through your eleventh house for about a month. Invitations arrive, an old friend gets back in touch, and you find yourself at a gathering where you meet exactly the person you needed to know. Team projects go well, and your hopes for the next year or two come within reach. You think about the future in broad strokes, about the kind of life you want to be part of and who you want in it. Social overload is the snag, along with the odd feeling of being lonely in a crowded room. Group politics can grate as well. You come out of it knowing who your people are and where you belong."
    },
    "12": {
      "text": "The Sun slips into your twelfth house for about a month, the last stretch before it reaches your Ascendant, and your energy drops a notch. You want more sleep, more time alone, fewer people asking things of you. Dreams get vivid, and old memories surface while you are doing something ordinary like washing up. Work behind the scenes goes well, whether it is research, planning or helping someone privately. Low moods and a vague tiredness are common, and you can feel invisible or overlooked at work. Escaping into screens or a second glass of wine is tempting. Underneath it all, you are quietly finishing the old cycle so the next one starts clean."
    }
  },
  "mercury": {
    "1": {
      "text": "Mercury crossing your first house for a few weeks turns up the volume on your mind. You talk more, think faster, and catch yourself explaining your plans to anyone who will listen, including the person behind you in the queue. Your body feels restless too, tapping a foot in meetings, pacing while on the phone. People see you as sharp and quick, and first impressions go well whenever you speak. Nerves are the price: overthinking how you come across, rehearsing what you said long after the conversation ended. You also interrupt more than you realise. For these weeks your words carry your identity, and you get to decide what story you tell about yourself."
    },
    "2": {
      "text": "For a few weeks Mercury moves through your second house, and you think about money in practical detail. You compare prices, cancel a forgotten subscription, sketch a budget on the back of an envelope, or have a frank conversation about pay. Ideas for earning come easily, and a skill you take for granted starts to look like something people would buy. You notice how your self-worth hums along with the numbers. Worry loops keep you awake some nights, adding up the same sums again and again. Small impulse buys slip past when your attention is elsewhere. Your head ends up clearer about what you own and what you are worth."
    },
    "3": {
      "text": "Mercury is at home in your third house, and for these few weeks your days turn into a relay of messages. Calls, texts, short trips across town, a form to fill in, a brother or sister with something urgent to tell you. You learn fast, pick up a new app or a phrase of another language, and ideas come to you on the bus. Conversation feels easy, and you can talk your way through almost any awkward moment. Mental overload is the downside, with unread articles stacking up and a buzzing head at bedtime. Gossip tempts you more than usual too. The weeks end with a sharper tongue, a fuller notebook and a few loose ends tied up."
    },
    "4": {
      "text": "Mercury moving through your fourth house for a few weeks brings family talk and household logistics to the front of your mind. You browse flats online, chase the plumber about the boiler, or settle who is hosting the next big family meal. A parent rings with news, and a conversation about the past opens a door you thought was shut. You think about where you come from and what home means to you now. Old family habits show up in how you speak, and you hear a parent's phrase coming out of your own mouth. Arguments at home flare more easily than usual. Things that have gone unsaid under your own roof finally find their way out."
    },
    "5": {
      "text": "With Mercury in your fifth house for a few weeks, your mind turns playful. You flirt with words, send the funny message, and come up with ideas for creative projects faster than you can start them. Games, puzzles and banter with children or friends lift your mood on a grey afternoon. Romantic conversations sparkle, and a text exchange keeps you smiling through a dull day at work. The trouble is that talk runs ahead of action, so projects stay as notes on your phone. You also want an audience, and feel flat when nobody laughs at the joke. For now you think like an artist and speak with the lightness you usually save for close friends."
    },
    "6": {
      "text": "A few weeks of Mercury in your sixth house make you the organiser at work. You write lists, streamline a clumsy process, answer the emails nobody else wants to touch, and spot the small error before it spreads through a whole report. Your mind likes detail now, and practical problems give you satisfaction. You read up on sleep or food, and a small change to your routine makes a noticeable difference. Worry is the drag: a niggling symptom looked up online at midnight, or a colleague's offhand comment replayed for days. Criticism, given and received, stings more than usual. Steady, careful work done properly pays off now in ways people notice."
    },
    "7": {
      "text": "For a few weeks Mercury crosses your seventh house, and conversations with one other person take up much of your thinking. A partner wants to talk things through, a contract lands on your desk, or a friend asks for an honest opinion and actually wants it. You listen well and speak clearly, and negotiations start to move. Talks that have been stuck for months get unstuck. You also become more aware of where you disagree, and a small remark can turn into a long debate over the washing up. Some days you lose your own view by quietly adopting theirs. Each real conversation sharpens how you meet people."
    },
    "8": {
      "text": "Mercury slides into your eighth house for a few weeks, and your thinking turns deep and private. Paperwork about shared money comes up: a mortgage form, a will, a tax query, a talk about who pays for what. You want to understand what lies beneath, and a documentary about the mind or a true crime book grips you late at night. Conversations about sex, death or trust arise in unexpected places, sometimes with near strangers. Suspicion creeps in, and you read hidden meaning into a short reply. Secrets feel hard to keep and hard to hear. Words finally come for things you usually keep locked away."
    },
    "9": {
      "text": "For a few weeks Mercury travels through your ninth house, and your mind reaches past the everyday. You plan a trip, read the long article to the end, sign up for a talk, or argue happily about politics and philosophy over dinner. Foreign languages, study and publishing get a lift, and a deadline for an application suddenly feels doable. Your thinking goes big, and you see how small facts connect to larger ideas. Opinions harden quickly, though, and you sound more certain than you feel. Details slip while you gaze at the horizon, so a booking goes wrong or a form stays half filled. A broader view stays with you, and so does a hunger to learn more."
    },
    "10": {
      "text": "Mercury in your tenth house for a few weeks puts your words on public view. Emails to your boss, a presentation, an interview, a post that more people see than usual: your career runs on communication right now. You think strategically about your next move and speak with more authority than you expected of yourself. Useful contacts come through work conversations, sometimes in a corridor or a lift. Every slip is visible, though, and a badly worded message travels further than you would like. You can also overthink your reputation until you freeze in front of a blank screen. Right now you have a chance to be heard where it counts."
    },
    "11": {
      "text": "Your group chats come alive while Mercury moves through your eleventh house for a few weeks. Friends message more, networking events turn up, and a chat with a colleague sparks a plan for the year ahead. You are full of ideas for a team, a club or a cause, and people listen when you share them. Your thinking stretches into what comes next, a year or two down the line. The strain is noise: too many threads, too many opinions, and a sense of being everywhere and nowhere at once. A friendship wobbles over a careless word in a group message. Your ideas find the people who can carry them further."
    },
    "12": {
      "text": "For a few weeks Mercury drifts through your twelfth house, and your mind turns inward. You think more than you say, fill pages of a journal, or find an answer in a dream or on a quiet walk. Research, planning and private conversations go well. Memories surface out of nowhere, and a song in a shop brings back a whole year of your life. The difficulty is fog: forgetting names, misplacing keys, misreading a message and replying to the wrong thing. Worry works away under the surface, and you keep back things that need saying. Old thoughts get sorted before Mercury rises over your Ascendant and your voice returns."
    }
  },
  "venus": {
    "1": {
      "text": "Venus crossing your first house for about a month makes you easier to like, and you feel it. You take more care over your clothes, buy the new shirt or the good perfume, and walk into rooms with a softer, warmer presence. People smile back, compliments arrive from unexpected places, and someone new notices you. Your mood is sweeter than usual, and conflict feels like something to smooth over rather than fight. Vanity sneaks in, along with a wish to please everyone you meet. Spending on appearance adds up quickly. This month lets you enjoy being yourself, and shows you how magnetic a little ease can be."
    },
    "2": {
      "text": "For about a month Venus moves through your second house, and money and pleasure mix. You treat yourself to the good coffee, the soft jumper, the dinner out, and it feels deserved rather than guilty. Income can rise through a pleasant arrangement or a talent that people pay for gladly. You value what you already have and enjoy your own things more, the favourite mug, the well-worn coat. Overspending is the obvious snag, and you notice that a bad day nudges you towards the checkout. Comfort can turn lazy if you let it. This stretch teaches you what you value and how good it feels to have it around you."
    },
    "3": {
      "text": "With Venus in your third house for about a month, everyday life gets friendlier. Messages are warmer, a neighbour offers help with the bins, and you and a sibling laugh on the phone like you used to. You find the kind words easily, and you can smooth over a tension that has hung around for weeks. Short trips feel like small holidays, even a drive to the next town. Flirting slips into texts and quick chats at the school gate or the coffee machine. The shadow is saying what people want to hear rather than what you think. A single well-chosen sentence turns out to carry a surprising amount of kindness."
    },
    "4": {
      "text": "Venus settles in your fourth house for about a month, and home becomes the place you most want to be. You buy flowers for the kitchen, repaint a tired room, rearrange the furniture, or cook a long meal for people you love. Family relations soften, and a visit to a parent goes better than you expected. You crave comfort: candles, clean sheets, a good film on the sofa with someone warm beside you. The trap is hiding indoors and turning down the world outside. Buying things for the house can get expensive too. Home becomes a softer base, somewhere you can rest properly and be looked after."
    },
    "5": {
      "text": "Romance and fun are in the air while Venus travels through your fifth house for about a month. Dates feel light and exciting, a crush makes you giddy, and a long relationship gets its sense of play back. You enjoy art, music, dancing and anything that makes you feel properly alive. Children and creative projects bring joy, and an afternoon of making something passes in minutes. The risk is chasing pleasure too hard, overspending on treats, or falling for someone mainly for the thrill. Drama looks more attractive than it should. You rediscover how good it feels to be enjoyed, and to enjoy without apology."
    },
    "6": {
      "text": "For about a month Venus moves through your sixth house, and work becomes noticeably more pleasant. A colleague turns into a friend, the office atmosphere lifts, or you make your desk a nicer place to sit with a plant and a decent lamp. You enjoy routine a little more: the morning walk, the lunch you actually look forward to. Small acts of care, for yourself and for others, feel meaningful rather than dutiful. Laziness slips in, and so does the biscuit tin as a reward for every finished task. An office crush can complicate things. Ordinary days improve noticeably with a touch of beauty and kindness."
    },
    "7": {
      "text": "Venus in your seventh house for about a month is a sweet time for partnership. Your partner seems more loving, and you feel more loving towards them, laughing at the same things again. If you are single, you meet someone who charms you, or a friendship takes a romantic turn. Business deals go smoothly, and people are willing to meet you halfway. The shadow is giving in to keep the peace, or seeing someone through rose tinted glasses. You also lean on others to make you happy and feel lost when they are busy. This month teaches you how good it is to share your life on fair terms."
    },
    "8": {
      "text": "For about a month Venus moves through your eighth house, and closeness goes deeper. Intimacy becomes more intense, and you want connection, the kind of talk that happens at two in the morning. Shared money brings good news: a partner's pay rise, a loan approved, a gift or a refund you had forgotten. You feel drawn to people and things with depth and a little mystery. Jealousy and possessiveness surface too, and you feel an urge to hold on too tightly. Spending on credit tempts you when you want to feel secure. Trust and pleasure grow quickly once you let someone properly in."
    },
    "9": {
      "text": "Venus travels through your ninth house for about a month, and beauty seems to live somewhere far away. You browse holiday photos, book a weekend in a city you have never seen, or fall for a foreign film, a language, a cuisine. Study feels like a pleasure, and a teacher or a book wins your heart. Love can arrive through travel or through someone from a different culture, and conversations about big ideas become a form of flirting. The snag is idealism, since a place or a person looks perfect from a distance. Spending on travel and courses runs over budget. By the time Venus moves on, your world feels larger and lovelier than it did."
    },
    "10": {
      "text": "For about a month Venus climbs through your tenth house, and your working life gets a touch of grace. Bosses are warmer, a client praises your work in front of others, and you are the person people like dealing with. Charm opens professional doors now, and a creative or artistic side of your career comes forward. Your public image improves, and you enjoy being seen doing what you do. Romance can arrive through work, which brings its own complications. The trap is relying on being liked in place of being good, or smoothing over a problem that needs facing. Recognition feels pleasant, and your reputation softens around the edges."
    },
    "11": {
      "text": "Venus in your eleventh house for about a month fills your social life with warmth. Friends invite you out, a group welcomes you in, and you enjoy being part of something bigger than your own week. A friendship can turn romantic, or you meet someone special through mutual friends at a birthday drinks. Your wishes for the future feel closer and lighter to carry. Networking becomes easy, even pleasurable, and a favour from a friend opens an unexpected door. The pitfall is saying yes to every party and ending the month tired and broke. This stretch reminds you how much the right friends add to your life."
    },
    "12": {
      "text": "For about a month Venus drifts through your twelfth house, and love works in private. You enjoy time alone: a long bath, a quiet film, a day with your phone switched off. Compassion runs high, and you want to help someone who is struggling without making a fuss about it. An old love surfaces in your thoughts, or a private attraction you tell nobody about. The shadow is longing for what you cannot have, or slipping into escape through food, drink or fantasy. Self-sacrifice feels noble when it is simply draining you. Venus softens you in private before she reaches your Ascendant and you step back into the light."
    }
  },
  "mars": {
    "1": {
      "text": "Mars charges across your first house for about six weeks, and you feel ready to go. You wake early, train harder, start projects on impulse, and say what you think without softening it first. People notice your energy, and some of them find it a lot. Your temper runs short, and a slow queue or a vague answer can set you off. Rushing leads to small knocks and scrapes: a bumped head, a cut finger, a dented wing mirror. Competition excites you, and you want to win even at a board game. These weeks give you the courage to put yourself first and start something that is truly yours."
    },
    "2": {
      "text": "For about six weeks Mars pushes through your second house, and you want to earn more, now. You chase an overdue invoice, go after a new client, ask for a raise, or sell things you no longer need. Money moves fast, both in and out of your account. You get protective of what is yours and irritated when someone borrows without asking. Impulse spending is the danger, the expensive gadget bought in a burst of frustration after a bad day. Arguments over money flare up at home more easily than usual. Your income gets the push it needed, and you learn to stand up plainly for your worth."
    },
    "3": {
      "text": "Mars in your third house for about six weeks sharpens your tongue. You argue more, debate hard, and fire off messages without rereading them. Your mind works fast, and you tear through paperwork and errands at a speed that surprises you. Driving and travel need care, since impatience at the wheel leads to near misses and parking tickets. Friction with siblings or neighbours flares over something small, like a parking space or a noisy evening. You speak up for yourself in situations you would usually let slide. Your voice carries force, and the people around you hear exactly where you stand."
    },
    "4": {
      "text": "For about six weeks Mars moves through your fourth house, and home becomes a building site. You tear up the old carpet, paint every wall, or tackle the overgrown garden. Family tension runs high, and an old argument with a parent or partner flares over dinner. You feel restless at home, and on a bad day the walls seem to close in. Anger that has nothing to do with the house often comes out there anyway, aimed at whoever left the dishes. Household accidents rise when you rush. Your living space changes, and so does what you are willing to put up with."
    },
    "5": {
      "text": "Mars in your fifth house for about six weeks fires up your passion. Romance heats up, desire runs strong, and you chase the person you like without playing it cool. Creative projects, sport and competition all get a burst of energy, and you work late on the thing you love simply because you cannot stop. Children test your patience, or you end up playing with them harder than anyone expected. The danger is taking chances for the thrill, betting money you need or starting a drama to feel something. Ego clashes flare when someone ignores your efforts. Courage rises to go after whatever delights you."
    },
    "6": {
      "text": "For about six weeks Mars pushes through your sixth house, and you are a force at work. You clear the backlog, take on the task everyone else avoids, and finish in a day what normally takes a week. Exercise suits you now, and a new training routine actually sticks. Colleagues irritate you, and a small complaint about the rota turns into a row. Overwork is the main risk: pushing through tiredness, skipping lunch, straining a muscle because you would not stop. Small injuries and flare ups come from rushing. These weeks reward effort generously and teach you, sometimes bluntly, where your limits sit."
    },
    "7": {
      "text": "Mars in your seventh house for about six weeks brings other people's will up against yours. A partner becomes more assertive, a rival appears at work, or a negotiation turns tough just when you wanted it settled. Arguments come up fast, and you find yourself defending your position before you have finished your coffee. Sexual chemistry rises too, and passion can reignite a relationship that had gone quiet. Legal or business disputes heat up. You also notice the moments when you let someone else carry the anger you do not want to own. Your relationships show where they need honesty and force, not just politeness."
    },
    "8": {
      "text": "For about six weeks Mars pushes through your eighth house, and intensity rises. Desire becomes deep and urgent, and intimacy feels electric one night and stormy the next. Money you share with others turns into a battleground, over debts, taxes or a partner's spending. Power struggles surface in close relationships, and you feel something raw stirring under your calm face. You face fears head on, and a crisis that would once have floored you leaves you stronger. The danger is control, jealousy, or burning a bridge in a moment of fury. Something that has been stuck for far too long finally starts to shift."
    },
    "9": {
      "text": "Mars in your ninth house for about six weeks gives you the urge to go further. You book a trip on impulse, enrol on a course, or throw yourself into a cause you believe in, signing petitions and arguing online. Debates about beliefs and politics heat up, and you defend your views with passion at the dinner table. Travel is exciting but needs care, with missed connections and lost luggage more likely when you rush. Legal matters move quickly. The danger is becoming preachy or reckless with your opinions and alienating people you like. You end up well beyond your usual limits, clearer about what you believe."
    },
    "10": {
      "text": "For about six weeks Mars pushes through your tenth house, and your ambition catches fire. You go after a promotion, pitch the big idea, and push your career forward with a directness that surprises people. Your boss notices your drive, and some colleagues feel threatened by it. Clashes with authority figures flare, especially with anyone who blocks your way without good reason. You work long hours and feel restless when things move slowly. Burnout is the danger, along with making enemies through sheer force. A visible result comes out of it, the kind people remember you for."
    },
    "11": {
      "text": "Mars in your eleventh house for about six weeks puts fire into your social life. You throw yourself into a group project, a campaign, a team sport or a club, and you end up leading the charge. Friends inspire you to act, and a plan hatched over drinks becomes something real. Conflicts within groups flare, over direction, credit or plain ego. A friendship can turn competitive, and you notice a flash of envy at someone's success. You set bold goals for the next year and want to start on them now. Other people rally around what matters to you, and a shared plan gets moving."
    },
    "12": {
      "text": "For about six weeks Mars drifts through your twelfth house, and your energy turns inward. You feel tired or blocked, and anger simmers without an obvious outlet, leaking out as sighs and slammed cupboard doors. Old frustrations surface, and you realise you have been swallowing more than you admitted. Working alone or behind the scenes goes well, and a private project moves forward steadily. Dreams become vivid and restless, full of chases and arguments. Self-sabotage and quiet resentment are the dangers. These weeks clear the ground for a fresh start when Mars crosses your Ascendant and your drive returns in full."
    }
  },
  "northNode": {
    "1": {
      "text": "For about a year and a half the North Node crosses your first house, and life keeps pushing you to stand on your own feet. Decisions you once ran past a partner or friend now land on you alone, and you find yourself choosing the restaurant, the holiday, the next step in your career. Independence feels awkward at first, almost selfish, because your old habit is to fit around other people. That pull, from the South Node in your seventh house, makes compromise feel oddly empty. People start to see you as someone with your own direction. Taking up space without apology is uncomfortable at first. Slowly a self emerges that you chose rather than one shaped by others."
    },
    "2": {
      "text": "The North Node moves through your second house for about a year and a half, and your life asks you to build something of your own. Money, skills and self-worth take centre stage, and you feel drawn to earn independently, save steadily and trust your own resources. Shared finances and other people's money, the old South Node pull from your eighth house, feel heavier and less satisfying. You notice how much you have relied on a partner's income, a crisis or an intensity to feel alive. Simple pleasures, a paid off card, a garden, a skill you can sell, start to matter more. Growth feels slow and unglamorous at times. This period teaches you that stability is a strength, not a compromise."
    },
    "3": {
      "text": "With the North Node crossing your third house for about a year and a half, your growth lies in the everyday. Conversations, local connections, short courses and writing all ask more of you. You find yourself learning a practical skill, chatting to neighbours, reconnecting with a sibling, or putting your thoughts into words for other people. Grand philosophies and far horizons, the South Node pull in your ninth house, feel less rewarding. You notice how often you have lectured when you could have listened, and curiosity starts to take the place of certainty. The challenge is staying present with small details when your mind wants to roam. Right on your doorstep, a richness opens up that you had walked past for years."
    },
    "4": {
      "text": "For about a year and a half the North Node moves through your fourth house, and your life asks you to come home. Family, roots, a place of your own and your inner emotional life call for attention. You find yourself spending more evenings in, sorting out the house, looking after a parent, or finally building the private life you have kept postponing. Career and public status, the old South Node draw in your tenth house, lose some of their shine. You notice how much you have used work to avoid feeling. Slowing down feels uncomfortable, almost like failing. Your roots grow, so that whatever you build later has somewhere solid to stand."
    },
    "5": {
      "text": "The North Node crosses your fifth house for about a year and a half, and your growth comes through joy and self-expression. You feel drawn to create something, fall in love, play with children, or take a risk on a passion you shelved long ago. Group life and the approval of friends, the familiar South Node pull in your eleventh house, feel less nourishing. You notice how often you have blended into the crowd rather than stepping into the light. Standing alone on your own creative ground feels exposing, as if you are showing off. People respond warmly when you let your personality out. Your individual spark turns out to matter more than you let yourself believe."
    },
    "6": {
      "text": "For about a year and a half the North Node moves through your sixth house, and growth arrives through daily routines, work and care of your body. You feel drawn to organise, commit to a job properly, help practically, and build habits that support you. Dreaming, escaping and drifting, the old South Node pull in your twelfth house, stop feeling restful and start to feel like avoidance. You notice how often you have waited for inspiration rather than showing up. Discipline feels dull at first, like giving up something precious. Yet small, repeated efforts reshape your days more than any grand plan. Your gifts get grounded in useful service."
    },
    "7": {
      "text": "With the North Node crossing your seventh house for about a year and a half, your growth comes through other people. Partnerships, collaboration and close one-to-one bonds ask you to listen, compromise and let someone else matter as much as you. You meet people who change your direction, a partner, a business ally, even a worthy opponent. Going it alone, the familiar South Node pull in your first house, starts to feel lonely rather than free. You notice how often you have acted without asking anyone. Sharing decisions feels awkward, almost like losing yourself. This period teaches you that you grow most in the company of others."
    },
    "8": {
      "text": "The North Node crosses your eighth house for about a year and a half, and growth asks you to go deep. Intimacy, shared resources, trust and transformation come into focus, and you are drawn into closer bonds that change you. You find yourself merging finances, facing a loss, starting therapy, or letting someone see the parts you usually hide. Self-sufficiency and material security, the old South Node pull in your second house, feel limited now. You notice how tightly you have held on to control and possessions. Letting go is frightening, like stepping off a ledge. Real security, you discover, grows through connection and courage."
    },
    "9": {
      "text": "For about a year and a half the North Node travels through your ninth house, and your life asks you to widen your horizons. Travel, higher learning, philosophy and meaning call to you, and you feel drawn to study, explore another culture or chase a bigger vision. Constant chatter, local busyness and scattered information, the South Node pull in your third house, leave you restless and unfulfilled. You notice how often you have collected facts without asking what they mean. Stepping into unfamiliar territory feels risky and exposing. This period opens your mind and helps you find the story that gives your life direction."
    },
    "10": {
      "text": "The North Node climbs through your tenth house for about a year and a half, and your life asks you to step into public view. Career, responsibility and reputation come to the fore, and you feel drawn to take charge, aim higher and be seen for what you do. Home and family comfort, the familiar South Node pull in your fourth house, feel less fulfilling than before. You notice how often you have hidden behind domestic duties or the safety of the private sphere. Leadership feels exposing, and you worry about failing in front of others. Bit by bit you see what you are meant to build in the world."
    },
    "11": {
      "text": "For about a year and a half the North Node moves through your eleventh house, and growth comes through friends, groups and a shared vision of the future. You feel drawn to join a community, a cause or a network, and to think about the long term. Personal glory and the spotlight, the old South Node pull in your fifth house, feel less satisfying. You notice how often you have needed to be the star. Being one voice among many feels strange at first, even diminishing. Yet people who share your hopes open doors you could not reach alone. Belonging becomes a source of strength rather than a loss of self."
    },
    "12": {
      "text": "The North Node crosses your twelfth house for about a year and a half, and your life asks you to slow down and turn inward. Solitude, spiritual practice, dreams and compassion call to you, and you feel drawn to retreat, reflect or help people quietly. Order, routine and control, the old South Node pull in your sixth house, feel exhausting and pointless. You notice how often you have kept busy to avoid feeling. Surrender feels frightening, like losing your grip. Yet the quiet teaches you what no to-do list can. A deeper faith opens, with a sense of meaning that does not depend on being useful."
    }
  },
};
window.AstroDeep.transitPlanetsRich = {
  "sun": {
    "brings": "The transiting Sun works on you like a moving spotlight. For about a month it lights one part of your life, and that is where your energy, attention and willingness to show up naturally go. You notice it in small ways: suddenly wanting to sort the finances, spending more evenings at home, or feeling bolder at work. Matters you have avoided come up for attention, not dramatically, but steadily, as though the light makes them hard to ignore. Where the Sun touches a point in your chart for a couple of days, you feel more confident and visible around that theme. Ego can swell, until everything feels like it is about you. Followed over a year, the Sun shows you your own seasons of focus."
  },
  "moon": {
    "brings": "The Moon moves so fast that its transits register as passing moods rather than chapters of your life. For a few hours, or a couple of days as it crosses a house, your feelings, appetite and need for comfort lean towards one area. You feel homesick for no reason, crave a particular food, or cry at an advert and laugh at yourself for it. When the Moon touches a sensitive point, an ordinary conversation lands harder than expected. Over a month these small tides add up to a rhythm you can learn to recognise in yourself. Mistaking a passing mood for permanent truth is the easy error. Watched over time, the Moon becomes a daily reading of your emotional weather."
  },
  "mercury": {
    "brings": "Conversations, errands, paperwork and ideas gather wherever Mercury moves in your chart. For a few weeks your thinking circles that area, and messages, short trips and small decisions cluster there. It shows when your inbox fills with one kind of email, or when every chat with friends returns to the same topic. Where Mercury touches a point in your chart for a few days, words matter more than usual, and you say something you have been holding back. During its retrograde periods, old topics and old contacts come back for review, and misunderstandings rise. Scatter and nervous overthinking are the price. Mercury gives you a mind that is busy, lively and quick to connect."
  },
  "venus": {
    "brings": "Venus brings ease, pleasure and a softer touch to the part of your life she passes through. For about a month, affection, spending, beauty and the things you value gather there, and people become more cooperative. You notice it when you want to redecorate, treat yourself, or when someone suddenly seems more attractive. Where Venus touches a point in your chart for a few days, you feel charming, generous or in love with your life. During her retrograde periods, old loves and questions of worth come back for a second look. Indulgence creeps in, along with wanting everything to be nice. Venus reminds you what makes your life sweet."
  },
  "mars": {
    "brings": "Wherever Mars goes in your chart, drive, heat and friction follow. For about six weeks the area it crosses becomes a place where you want to act, compete or fix something now. It shows up as snapping at a queue, tackling a project at midnight, or desire flaring out of nowhere. Where Mars touches a point in your chart for a few days to a week, patience runs short and courage runs high. During its retrograde periods, the energy turns inward and old frustrations surface to be handled. The difficulty is rushing, arguments and small accidents. Its gift is fuel for stuck plans and the nerve to stand up for yourself."
  },
  "jupiter": {
    "brings": "Jupiter widens whatever it touches in your life. For about a year it crosses one house, and that area fills with opportunity, generosity, helpful people and a feeling that more is possible. You notice it when a door opens you did not expect, a course or a trip appears at the right moment, or you simply feel more hopeful about something that used to worry you. When Jupiter touches a point in your chart, the lift lasts for weeks and often arrives with a person or an offer. Excess is its shadow: overcommitting, overspending, overpromising. Growth sticks when you follow through on what you say yes to. Jupiter reminds you that luck is often simply readiness meeting a good moment."
  },
  "saturn": {
    "brings": "Saturn brings structure, effort and hard truth to the part of your life it moves through. For two to three years that area feels heavier and slower, and shortcuts stop working. You notice it when a job demands more than it used to, when a relationship asks for commitment, or when your body sends a firm message about limits. When Saturn touches a point in your chart, the pressure lasts for months and makes you face what you have avoided. Many people find it sobering at first, even lonely. Over time it rewards patience, honesty and steady work with something solid that lasts. Saturn shows you what is real, and what you are strong enough to carry."
  },
  "uranus": {
    "brings": "Sudden change, surprises and a hunger for freedom arrive with Uranus. It stays in a house for about seven years, and that area becomes restless and unpredictable. It looks like a job ending out of the blue, a new person turning your plans upside down, or waking one morning knowing you cannot carry on as before. When Uranus touches a point in your chart, the shake-up lasts a year or more, with sharp shocks along the way. Instability follows, and so does the urge to break things just to feel free. Liberation comes from a life that has become too small, and with it a chance to become more fully yourself."
  },
  "neptune": {
    "brings": "Neptune brings dissolving, dreaming and a longing for something beyond the everyday. It moves slowly, staying in one house for over a decade, and the area it crosses becomes blurred, idealised or spiritual. You notice it when you lose interest in goals that once drove you, when you fall for a vision or a person, or when your intuition becomes uncannily sharp. When Neptune touches a point in your chart, the fog lasts a year or more. The difficulty is confusion, disappointment and the pull to escape through fantasy or substances. In return you gain compassion, creativity and a sense that life holds more meaning than you can see."
  },
  "pluto": {
    "brings": "Deep, irreversible change is what Pluto brings to the part of your life it crosses. It stays in a house for many years, and that area goes through slow endings, power struggles and rebirth. You see it when something you relied on falls away, when a relationship becomes intense and consuming, or when you discover a strength you did not know you had. When Pluto touches a point in your chart, the process lasts a year or more and leaves you changed. Fear, control and clinging to what must go make it harder. Renewal follows, the kind of power that comes from having faced the worst and survived."
  },
  "chiron": {
    "brings": "Chiron touches old wounds in the part of your life it crosses. It moves irregularly, spending years in some houses and less in others, and its effects are tender and revealing. You notice it when an ordinary event stings more than it should, when an old hurt from childhood resurfaces in a new form, or when you find yourself helping someone with the very struggle you carry. When Chiron touches a point in your chart, the sensitivity lasts many months. Feeling exposed and unfixable is part of it. Over time the hurt looks different, help that works appears, and your wound becomes wisdom others can lean on."
  },
  "northNode": {
    "brings": "The North Node moves backwards through the zodiac and points to where your life is asking you to grow. For about a year and a half it crosses one house, and you feel pulled towards unfamiliar experiences there and away from comfortable habits in the opposite area. You notice it when meaningful people arrive, when a direction starts to feel inevitable, or when old routines lose their appeal without a clear reason. When the Node touches a point in your chart, encounters and decisions feel fated. Awkwardness comes with it, since growth here never feels natural at first. What the North Node offers is a clearer sense of where your life is heading."
  },
};
/* The lunar Nodes squaring a birth point: a crossroads, not the South Node sitting on it. Used for squares only; the "hard" reading above covers the opposition. */
window.AstroDeep.transitNodeSquares = {
  "sun": "For a few months the lunar Nodes cross your Sun at right angles, and you stand at a crossroads about who you are becoming. The old version of you and the one you are growing into both make their case, and neither wins outright. A job offer, a move or a request to step up arrives at an awkward moment, and you feel out of step with the timetable everyone else seems to follow. You hesitate, then overcorrect, and small decisions feel oddly weighty. Some people push you back towards the familiar role while others expect a leap you are not sure you can make. The choice you make here, even a modest one, sets the direction of the next few years.",
  "moon": "Your emotional life reaches a turning point while the lunar Nodes square your Moon for a few months. Old family habits pull one way and a new kind of home life pulls the other: you want to stop being the one who holds everything together, yet you feel guilty the moment you step back. Moods arrive out of nowhere and feel bigger than the day deserves. A move, a change in who lives with you or a shift in how you care for a parent or child comes up at an inconvenient time. You feel slightly out of sync with the people closest to you. What you decide about your own needs now shapes where you feel at home for years.",
  "mercury": "Your thinking stands at a fork in the road while the lunar Nodes square your Mercury for a few months. You catch yourself repeating the same opinions and the same stories, while the new ideas pulling at you still refuse to fit into words. A course, a contract or a conversation forces a decision before you feel ready, and you rewrite the email four times. Advice comes from every side, and much of it contradicts itself. Plans made in a hurry need unpicking later, and a mixed message with a sibling or colleague takes longer than usual to clear up. What you choose to learn, say or sign now points your mind towards its next chapter.",
  "venus": "Love and money reach a crossroads while the lunar Nodes square your Venus for a few months. A familiar type of partner or a familiar way of spending tempts you back, just as you sense your taste has moved on. A relationship asks for a decision it has been avoiding, whether that means moving in, pulling back or finally naming what you want. Someone new arrives at an awkward moment, or an old flame reappears when you had settled into something else. Choosing feels uncomfortable because each option costs you something you value. The choice you make now teaches you what you are worth to yourself, and your relationships start to reflect it.",
  "mars": "With the lunar Nodes squaring your Mars for a few months, the way you chase what you want comes to a turning point. The sharp reply and the solo push still work, yet they leave you more tired than they used to. A goal you chased for years loses its pull just as a new challenge appears that you are not sure you have the energy for. Frustration spikes at awkward moments: in traffic, in meetings, at a partner's slow answer. You start things and stall, or stall and then rush. Where you decide to put your effort now, and what you stop fighting for, shapes the next stretch of your life.",
  "jupiter": "Your sense of what is possible reaches a turning point while the lunar Nodes square your Jupiter for a few months. Opportunities appear, but they rarely line up with your plans: the course starts the week you move house, or the offer asks you to believe in something you have outgrown. You feel torn between the faith you grew up with and a bigger, less certain view of life. Overcommitting is the easy mistake: saying yes to two paths so you never have to choose. Teachers and advisers disagree, and you notice you trust your own judgement more than theirs. Whichever door you walk through now opens onto years of growth in that direction.",
  "saturn": "Duty and direction pull against each other while the lunar Nodes square your Saturn for a few months. A responsibility you took on long ago suddenly feels in the way: a role at work, a promise to family or a rule you live by. You weigh whether to keep carrying it or set it down, and both choices feel heavy. Deadlines and delays land at the worst moments, and someone in authority asks for commitment before you are sure. You feel older than your years one week and restless the next. The structure you choose to keep or build now becomes the frame of your life for years to come.",
  "uranus": "For a few months the lunar Nodes square your Uranus, and the urge to break free arrives at an awkward crossroads. You feel restless with arrangements that suited you last year, yet the new path is not clear enough to leap towards. Sudden changes force choices you had been putting off: a cancelled plan, a surprise offer, a friend who moves away. Part of you wants to walk out, and part of you wants to keep everything exactly as it is. You notice where your independence has turned into a habit of keeping people at a distance. The change you make now, planned or sudden, shapes how free your next few years feel.",
  "neptune": "Your dreams reach a crossroads while the lunar Nodes square your Neptune for a few months. An old escape stops working: the late-night scrolling, the rescue mission, the fantasy about another life. No clearer vision has taken its place yet. You feel foggy about direction, and a decision about a creative project, a spiritual practice or a person you idealise keeps slipping away from you. Timing goes strange: messages cross, plans blur and coincidences pile up. Someone asks you to believe in them at exactly the moment you are losing faith. What you choose to keep dreaming about now sets the tone for years.",
  "pluto": "A deep change you have been circling reaches its turning point while the lunar Nodes square your Pluto for a few months. A power struggle at work or at home forces a choice between holding on and letting go, and both feel costly. Old fears about control, money or loss flare up, sometimes over something small, like who holds the keys or who decides. You see clearly where you have been gripping too hard, and where you have handed your power to someone else. The timing feels fated and unwelcome at once. What you release or reclaim now reshapes the next chapter of your life from the ground up.",
  "chiron": "An old wound comes to a crossroads while the lunar Nodes square your Chiron for a few months. Situations press on the sore spot at inconvenient moments: a rejection just before an important day, a comment that echoes a parent, a health niggle that will not settle. You feel pulled between the familiar ways you protect yourself and a new, more open way of living with the hurt. Helping others with the same struggle tempts you as a way of avoiding your own. The timing feels unfair, yet it brings the wound into the open where it can finally change. How you choose to carry this hurt now shapes the kind of healer you become.",
  "northNode": "This transit comes around roughly every nine years, near the ages of 5, 14, 23, 33, 42, 51 and 60, and for a few months your life path takes a sideways turn. You feel caught between the direction you set out in and the one you are growing towards, as if someone turned the map ninety degrees. Choices about work, relationships or where to live arrive out of order, before you have finished the chapter you are in. Old habits look comfortable and tired at the same time. People who shaped your early direction reappear or come to mind. The small corrections you make now keep you on course for the next nine years.",
  "asc": "The way you present yourself reaches a crossroads while the lunar Nodes square your Ascendant for a few months. The image that has served you starts to feel like a costume: the capable one, the easy-going one, the one who never makes a fuss. Home and career pull on you from both ends while your sense of who you are wobbles in the middle. A new look, a new title or a new place to live comes up at an awkward moment. People react to you in unfamiliar ways, and you are not sure yet which reactions to trust. How you choose to show up now becomes the way people know you for years.",
  "mc": "Your career stands at a crossroads while the lunar Nodes square your Midheaven for a few months. The role you have built still pays the bills, yet it no longer quite matches who you are becoming. Offers and setbacks arrive out of sequence: a promotion when you are thinking of leaving, a quiet patch just as you want to move up. Your own needs and a partner's plans both have a say in the decision, and they rarely agree. You feel out of step with colleagues who seem sure of their path. The professional choice you make now, even a sideways one, sets your public direction for years."
};
/* What a sign brings to anything in it on the Today tab: the colour of the sky, not the reader's own placements. */
window.AstroDeep.transitSigns = {
  "aries": "Anything in Aries moves fast and wants to begin. Where it touches your life it brings urgency and nerve: you want to start, act and be first, and waiting feels harder than usual.",
  "taurus": "Anything in Taurus slows to the pace of the body and the bank balance. Where it touches your life it asks for patience, comfort and proof that something will last, and you change course only once it feels safe.",
  "gemini": "Anything in Gemini gets talked about, questioned and passed on. Where it touches your life, messages, errands and second opinions multiply, and your mind jumps between options faster than you can settle on one.",
  "cancer": "Anything in Cancer turns personal and protective. Where it touches your life it draws you towards home, family and feeling safe, and you answer with your gut and your memories before your head.",
  "leo": "Anything in Leo turns up the warmth and the volume. Where it touches your life it wants to be seen, praised and enjoyed, and pride, play and generosity all rise closer to the surface.",
  "virgo": "Anything in Virgo comes down to the detail. Where it touches your life, things get sorted, fixed and improved, and small flaws you usually ignore start to nag at you.",
  "libra": "Anything in Libra is weighed against other people. Where it touches your life it turns you towards partnership, fairness and good manners, and decisions wait until every side has been heard.",
  "scorpio": "Anything in Scorpio goes beneath the surface. Where it touches your life it becomes intense, private and all-or-nothing, and you want the real story rather than the polite one.",
  "sagittarius": "Anything in Sagittarius widens the view. Where it touches your life it stretches you towards travel, learning and belief, and you want more room, more meaning and fewer rules.",
  "capricorn": "Anything in Capricorn is built for the long haul. Where it touches your life it asks for structure, effort and responsibility, and shortcuts lose their appeal.",
  "aquarius": "Anything in Aquarius steps back to see the whole system. Where it touches your life it turns you towards friends, groups and the future, and you want the freedom to do things your own way.",
  "pisces": "Anything in Pisces softens at the edges. Where it touches your life it blurs into feeling, imagination and compassion, and it is harder to tell where your mood ends and someone else's begins."
};
